window.__CONTENT_EN__=window.__CONTENT_EN__||{};window.__CONTENT_EN__[0]={"0":{"example:0:exzh":"I drink water.","example:0:exzh2":"Water, please.","grammar:0:ex:trans":"Drink water.","grammar:0:ex:structure":"(object) を + verb masu-form","grammar:0:ex:explain":"This is the most basic \"object + を + transitive verb\" pattern. を marks the thing the action directly acts on — here, the 水 that is drunk; every transitive verb meaning \"do something to something\" uses を to point out its object. Keep the division of labor between を and が clear: を marks the object of the action, が marks the doer of the action, so the full sentence is actually 私が水を飲む. The polite form of the verb 飲む is 飲みます, which expresses present, future, or habitual action; in conversation the subject 私は is usually omitted.","grammar:0:ex:words:0:zh":"water","grammar:0:ex:words:0:note":"みず","grammar:0:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:0:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:0:ex:words:1:note":"Marks the thing the action directly acts on (the thing being drunk)","grammar:0:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:0:ex:words:2:zh":"to drink","grammar:0:ex:words:2:note":"のみます; masu-form (polite form), dictionary form 飲む (godan (u-) verb)","grammar:0:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:0:ex:points:0":"を marks the **object** of a transitive verb (the thing drunk = 水). Any transitive verb meaning \"do something to something\" takes を.","grammar:0:ex:points:1":"❓What's the difference between を and が? を = the **object** of the action (drinking \"water\"); が = the **doer** of the action (who drinks). Both can appear in the same sentence: 私が 水を 飲む.","grammar:0:ex:points:2":"The masu-form (polite form) is the polite present/future, and also expresses habit; the dictionary form (plain form) is 飲む. The subject 私は is usually omitted.","grammar:0:ex2:trans":"Please give me water.","grammar:0:ex2:structure":"noun + を + ください. を marks the thing being requested, and ください at the end of the sentence makes it a polite request.","grammar:0:ex2:words:0:zh":"water","grammar:0:ex2:words:0:note":"みず","grammar:0:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:0:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:0:ex2:words:1:note":"Marks the thing being requested","grammar:0:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:0:ex2:words:2:zh":"please give (me)","grammar:0:ex2:words:2:note":"〜をください: a fixed polite way to say \"please give me 〜\"","grammar:0:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:0:ex2:points:0":"〜をください: a polite way to ask someone for something","grammar:0:ex2:points:1":"ください is the imperative form of くださる, used for polite requests","exam:0:zh":"I poured cold water into an empty glass and drank it.","exam:0:why":"「水」 can be poured straight into a glass and drunk. 「しょうゆ」 is soy sauce, usually used as seasoning, not a drink you drink directly here."},"1":{"example:1:exzh":"This is a good book.","example:1:exzh2":"I read a book.","grammar:1:ex:trans":"This is a good book.","grammar:1:ex:structure":"A は B です","grammar:1:ex:explain":"This is the textbook example of the noun-predicate pattern 「AはBです」. The 「は」 here is not a subject marker: it takes 「これ」 and sets it up as the topic, with a feel like “as for this, it's…”. The predicate 「本です」 uses 「です」, which makes the whole sentence polite. The 「いい」 in the middle is an i-adjective, and Japanese i-adjectives can modify a noun directly without adding any particle, so 「いい本」 is “a good book” — put it all together and you get “This is a good book.”","grammar:1:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:1:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:1:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:1:ex:words:1:note":"marks the topic","grammar:1:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:1:ex:words:2:zh":"good","grammar:1:ex:words:2:note":"i-adjective; can modify a noun directly","grammar:1:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:1:ex:words:3:zh":"book","grammar:1:ex:words:3:note":"ほん","grammar:1:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:1:ex:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:1:ex:words:4:note":"polite assertion","grammar:1:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:1:ex:points:0":"は marks the topic (not the subject marker が)","grammar:1:ex:points:1":"i-adjectives can attach directly to a noun: いい＋本","grammar:1:ex2:trans":"I read a book.","grammar:1:ex2:structure":"noun ＋ を ＋ verb (masu-form)","grammar:1:ex2:words:0:zh":"book","grammar:1:ex2:words:0:note":"ほん","grammar:1:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:1:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:1:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:1:ex2:words:2:zh":"read","grammar:1:ex2:words:2:note":"よみます; masu-form, dictionary form 読む","grammar:1:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:1:ex2:points:0":"を marks the object of a transitive verb","grammar:1:ex2:points:1":"読む → 読みます (masu-form of a godan verb)","exam:1:zh":"This book I borrowed from the library has a full hundred pages about a cat as the main character.","exam:1:why":"The item borrowed from the library that contains a long story should be 「本」. 「ノート」 is a notebook, which doesn't fit borrowing a storybook here."},"4":{"example:4:exzh":"I go home.","example:4:exzh2":"My house is close.","grammar:4:ex:trans":"Go home.","grammar:4:ex:structure":"Place＋に＋verb of movement","grammar:4:ex:explain":"This follows the pattern “place＋に＋verb of movement.” Here, “に” marks the endpoint or destination of the movement: “家,” the home one is returning to. Although the verb “帰る” ends in “る,” it is a godan verb (an exception), so its polite form is not made by dropping る and adding ます. Instead, change “る” to “り” and add “ます” to get “帰ります.” When indicating the direction of movement, “に” and “へ” are often interchangeable, but “に” places more emphasis on the destination reached.","grammar:4:ex:words:0:zh":"house","grammar:4:ex:words:0:note":"いえ","grammar:4:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:4:ex:words:1:zh":"(direction)","grammar:4:ex:words:1:note":"Marks the destination of movement","grammar:4:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:4:ex:words:2:zh":"go home / return","grammar:4:ex:words:2:note":"かえります; masu-form; dictionary form: 帰る","grammar:4:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:4:ex:points:0":"に marks the endpoint/destination of movement","grammar:4:ex:points:1":"帰る→帰ります (masu-form of a godan verb)","grammar:4:ex2:trans":"My home is nearby.","grammar:4:ex2:structure":"Noun＋の＋noun＋は＋i-adjective＋です","grammar:4:ex2:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:4:ex2:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:4:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:4:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:4:ex2:words:1:note":"Shows possession","grammar:4:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:4:ex2:words:2:zh":"house","grammar:4:ex2:words:2:note":"いえ","grammar:4:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:4:ex2:words:3:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:4:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:4:ex2:words:4:zh":"close","grammar:4:ex2:words:4:note":"ちかい","grammar:4:ex2:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:4:ex2:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:4:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:4:ex2:points:0":"の connects two nouns to express possession: 私の家","grammar:4:ex2:points:1":"近い＋です: an i-adjective used as a polite-form predicate","exam:4:zh":"The house where I live with my family is a five-minute walk from the station.","exam:4:why":"「家」 means the house you live in. 「会社」 is a company, and here the sentence is about the place where you live with your family."},"5":{"example:5:exzh":"I like dogs.","example:5:exzh2":"The dog is sleeping.","grammar:5:ex:trans":"I like dogs.","grammar:5:ex:structure":"〔the thing you like〕が ＋ 好きです","grammar:5:ex:explain":"In Japanese, 「好き」 is actually an adjective, not a verb, so the thing you like is always marked with 「が」 — a rule shared by words like 「好き・嫌い・上手・下手・ほしい」. The subject is left out of this sentence; the full version is 「私は犬が好きです」, where 「は」 marks the topic (me) and 「が」 marks the target (dogs). You could also say 「犬は好き」, but that turns dogs into a contrasting topic, hinting that you may not like other animals; for a neutral “I like dogs,” 「が」 is the most natural choice.","grammar:5:ex:words:0:zh":"dog","grammar:5:ex:words:0:note":"いぬ","grammar:5:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:5:ex:words:1:zh":"(marks the object of liking)","grammar:5:ex:words:1:note":"Here が is not the subject — it marks the object of 好き","grammar:5:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:5:ex:words:2:zh":"to like","grammar:5:ex:words:2:note":"suki; Japanese treats \"like\" as an adjective, not a verb","grammar:5:ex:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:5:ex:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:5:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:5:ex:points:0":"❓Why use が and not は? \"好き (like)\" is an **adjective** in Japanese, and the \"object\" of liking is always marked with **が** — the same goes for 好き・嫌い・上手・下手・ほしい.","grammar:5:ex:points:1":"Saying 犬**は**好き is also possible, but the nuance is different: は treats \"dog\" as a **topic for contrast** (dogs, sure, I like them… implying maybe not other things). To say \"I like dogs\" neutrally, が is the most natural.","grammar:5:ex:points:2":"The sentence actually omits the subject 私は: the full form is 私は 犬が 好きです — は marks the topic (me), while が marks the object (dog).","grammar:5:ex2:trans":"The dog is sleeping.","grammar:5:ex2:structure":"〔subject〕が＋verb-ています","grammar:5:ex2:words:0:zh":"dog","grammar:5:ex2:words:0:note":"いぬ","grammar:5:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:5:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:5:ex2:words:1:note":"Marks the doer of the action \"is sleeping\"","grammar:5:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:5:ex2:words:2:zh":"is sleeping","grammar:5:ex2:words:2:note":"ねています; 〜ている expresses an action in progress / a state, dictionary form 寝る","grammar:5:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:5:ex2:points:0":"Here が is a true **nominative**, marking the doer (the dog). This is a different use from the object-が that goes with 好き in the previous sentence — don't mix them up.","grammar:5:ex2:points:1":"❓Why use が and not は? Because this is a **new-information / phenomenon description** — \"I see a dog sleeping right in front of me\" — and Japanese customarily uses が; using は would turn it into a topic tone: \"as for this dog (by contrast), it's sleeping.\"","grammar:5:ex2:points:2":"〜ている: an action in progress (the state of being asleep). 寝る→寝て (te-form) + いる.","exam:5:zh":"The animal barking \"woof woof\" in the yard is a dog.","exam:5:why":"「ワンワン」 is the sound a dog makes, so 「犬」 is correct. A cat's cry is usually written 「ニャーニャー」."},"6":{"example:6:exzh":"I go to work.","example:6:exzh2":"Work is busy.","grammar:6:ex:trans":"I'm going to work.","grammar:6:ex:structure":"noun + に + 行きます","grammar:6:ex:explain":"This に marks the purpose of the action: 仕事に行く means \"to go for the sake of work / to go to work.\" This usage often appears before verbs of movement such as 行く・来る・帰る, spelling out the purpose of going to do something. The verb 行く is a godan (u-) verb; in the polite form the ending く becomes き and ます is added, giving 行きます. The subject 私は is omitted as usual, and context tells you that the speaker is the one going to work.","grammar:6:ex:words:0:zh":"work","grammar:6:ex:words:0:note":"しごと","grammar:6:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:6:ex:words:1:zh":"(purpose)","grammar:6:ex:words:1:note":"Marks the purpose of an action","grammar:6:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:6:ex:words:2:zh":"go","grammar:6:ex:words:2:note":"いきます; masu-form (polite form)","grammar:6:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:6:ex:points:0":"に can mark the purpose of an action (going to work)","grammar:6:ex:points:1":"行く→行きます (godan (u-) verb)","grammar:6:ex2:trans":"I'm busy with work.","grammar:6:ex2:structure":"Noun + が + i-adjective + です","grammar:6:ex2:words:0:zh":"work","grammar:6:ex2:words:0:note":"しごと","grammar:6:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:6:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:6:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:6:ex2:words:2:zh":"busy","grammar:6:ex2:words:2:note":"いそがしい","grammar:6:ex2:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:6:ex2:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:6:ex2:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:6:ex2:points:0":"が marks the subject (describing its state)","grammar:6:ex2:points:1":"忙しいです: polite form of an i-adjective","exam:6:zh":"My father works as a doctor at a hospital.","exam:6:why":"「医者の仕事をする」 means to work as a doctor. 「練習」 means practice and cannot express the job your father does at the hospital."},"9":{"example:9:exzh":"I don't have time.","example:9:exzh2":"Please tell me the current time.","grammar:9:ex:trans":"I don't have time.","grammar:9:ex:structure":"Noun + が + ありません","grammar:9:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the negative of the existence verb ある. ある expresses the existence or possession of inanimate things and abstract concepts, and its polite negative form is ありません (= ないです), so 時間がありません means \"I don't have time.\" Here が marks 時間, the subject that exists or is possessed, and it is the fixed particle that pairs with ある／ない sentences. Note that for living things you use いる／います instead, so don't mix the two up.","grammar:9:ex:words:0:zh":"time","grammar:9:ex:words:0:note":"じかん","grammar:9:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:9:ex:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:9:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:9:ex:words:2:zh":"don't have","grammar:9:ex:words:2:note":"negative of あります; ある → ありません","grammar:9:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:9:ex:points:0":"The polite negative of ある (existence/possession) is ありません","grammar:9:ex:points:1":"が marks the subject of existence","grammar:9:ex2:trans":"Please tell me what time it is now.","grammar:9:ex2:structure":"〜を教えてください","grammar:9:ex2:explain":"今の時間 means the current time; in this context it refers to what time it is right now. を marks the information you want the other person to give you. 教える is an ichidan (ru-) verb: drop る and attach て to make 教えてください, meaning \"please tell me.\"","grammar:9:ex2:words:0:zh":"now","grammar:9:ex2:words:0:note":"いま","grammar:9:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:9:ex2:words:1:zh":"(connects to a noun, showing a time relation)","grammar:9:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:9:ex2:words:2:zh":"time; here it refers to the current time of day","grammar:9:ex2:words:2:note":"じかん","grammar:9:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:9:ex2:words:3:zh":"(object)","grammar:9:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:9:ex2:words:4:zh":"tell","grammar:9:ex2:words:4:note":"おしえ","grammar:9:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:9:ex2:words:5:zh":"(connects to a request expression)","grammar:9:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:9:ex2:words:6:zh":"please","grammar:9:ex2:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:9:ex2:points:0":"Besides \"to teach,\" 教える can also mean to tell someone a piece of information.","grammar:9:ex2:points:1":"Verb te-form + ください politely asks someone to do something.","exam:9:zh":"The time it takes to walk from my house to the station is 30 minutes.","exam:9:why":"「三十分」 indicates the time required, matching 「かかる時間」. 「道」 means road, and 30 minutes can't describe the road itself."},"11":{"example:11:exzh":"Hello, how are you?","example:11:exzh2":"Hello, nice to meet you.","grammar:11:ex:trans":"Hello, how are you?","grammar:11:ex:structure":"こんにちは、〜ですか","grammar:11:ex:explain":"This sentence is a combination of everyday greetings. 「こんにちは」 is a greeting used during the daytime; note that it is written with 「は」 at the end but pronounced 「わ」, because it comes from an old particle. The second half, 「元気ですか」, uses \"na-adjective + です + か\" to ask about the other person's condition. 「元気」 is a na-adjective, so when it serves as the predicate it attaches directly to 「です」 and no 「な」 is needed. The 「か」 at the end is a question particle that turns the whole sentence into a question — put together, it simply asks how the other person is doing: \"How are you?\"","grammar:11:ex:words:0:zh":"Hello","grammar:11:ex:words:0:note":"a daytime greeting","grammar:11:ex:words:0:pos":"a set greeting phrase","grammar:11:ex:words:1:zh":"energetic; doing well","grammar:11:ex:words:1:note":"げんき","grammar:11:ex:words:1:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:11:ex:words:2:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:11:ex:words:2:pos":"copula","grammar:11:ex:words:3:zh":"(question)","grammar:11:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:11:ex:points:0":"こんにちは: a greeting used during the daytime","grammar:11:ex:points:1":"元気ですか: na-adjective + ですか to ask about someone's condition","grammar:11:ex2:trans":"Hello, nice to meet you.","grammar:11:ex2:structure":"こんにちは、はじめまして","grammar:11:ex2:words:0:zh":"Hello","grammar:11:ex2:words:0:pos":"a set greeting phrase","grammar:11:ex2:words:1:zh":"Nice to meet you","grammar:11:ex2:words:1:note":"the set greeting for meeting someone for the first time","grammar:11:ex2:words:1:pos":"a set greeting phrase","grammar:11:ex2:points:0":"はじめまして: the greeting used when meeting someone for the first time","grammar:11:ex2:points:1":"often followed by a self-introduction","exam:11:zh":"I met my teacher at two in the afternoon, so I greeted them with 「こんにちは」.","exam:11:why":"「こんにちは」 is a greeting used when meeting someone during the day. 「おはようございます」 is mainly used as a morning greeting."},"15":{"example:15:exzh":"Who will come?","example:15:exzh2":"Who is he?","example:15:exzh3":"Who are you?","example:15:exzh4":"Who is that person?","example:15:exzh5":"Can someone help me?","grammar:15:ex:trans":"Who will come?","grammar:15:ex:structure":"誰が〜ますか","grammar:15:ex:explain":"The point of this sentence is which particle to use when a question word is the subject. When a question word such as 「誰・何・どこ」 is the subject, you always use 「が」, never 「は」, because you are asking about the unknown subject itself, which is new information; 「誰が来ますか」 asks “who is coming?” In the same way, the answer also uses 「が」 to pin it down, as in 「田中さんが来ます」. The verb 「来る」 is an irregular verb, and its polite form is 「来ます」.","grammar:15:ex:words:0:zh":"who","grammar:15:ex:words:0:note":"だれ","grammar:15:ex:words:0:pos":"question word","grammar:15:ex:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:15:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex:words:2:zh":"come","grammar:15:ex:words:2:note":"きます","grammar:15:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:15:ex:words:3:zh":"(question)","grammar:15:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex:points:0":"❗誰（だれ）：who; a question word as subject takes が (not は).","grammar:15:ex:points:1":"誰が来る：who will come.","grammar:15:ex2:trans":"Who is he?","grammar:15:ex2:structure":"〜は誰ですか","grammar:15:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:15:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:15:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:15:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:15:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex2:words:2:zh":"who","grammar:15:ex2:words:2:note":"だれ","grammar:15:ex2:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:15:ex2:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:15:ex2:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:15:ex2:words:4:zh":"(question)","grammar:15:ex2:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex2:points:0":"❗〜は誰ですか: who is ...?","grammar:15:ex2:points:1":"彼は誰: who he is.","grammar:15:ex3:trans":"Who are you?","grammar:15:ex3:structure":"〜は誰ですか","grammar:15:ex3:words:0:zh":"you","grammar:15:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:15:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:15:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex3:words:2:zh":"who","grammar:15:ex3:words:2:note":"だれ","grammar:15:ex3:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:15:ex3:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:15:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:15:ex3:words:4:zh":"(question)","grammar:15:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex3:points:0":"あなたは誰: who you are.","grammar:15:ex3:points:1":"誰ですか: who is it?","grammar:15:ex4:trans":"Who is that person?","grammar:15:ex4:structure":"〜は誰ですか","grammar:15:ex4:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:15:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:15:ex4:words:1:zh":"person","grammar:15:ex4:words:1:note":"ひと","grammar:15:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:15:ex4:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:15:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex4:words:3:zh":"who","grammar:15:ex4:words:3:note":"だれ","grammar:15:ex4:words:3:pos":"question word","grammar:15:ex4:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:15:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:15:ex4:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:15:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:15:ex4:points:0":"あの人: that person.","grammar:15:ex4:points:1":"誰ですか: who is it?","grammar:15:ex5:trans":"Can someone help me?","grammar:15:ex5:structure":"誰か〜てくれますか","grammar:15:ex5:words:0:zh":"someone","grammar:15:ex5:words:0:note":"だれか","grammar:15:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:15:ex5:words:1:zh":"help","grammar:15:ex5:words:1:note":"てつだって","grammar:15:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:15:ex5:words:2:zh":"Can you ... for me?","grammar:15:ex5:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:15:ex5:points:0":"❗誰か: someone, anyone (誰 + か).","grammar:15:ex5:points:1":"〜てくれますか: could you ... (for me)?","exam:15:zh":"I didn't know that person's name, so I asked my teacher, \"Who is that person?\"","exam:15:why":"「誰」 is used to ask who someone is. 「どれ」 asks which one among several options and isn't suited to asking directly about this person's identity."},"16":{"example:16:exzh":"She is a student.","example:16:exzh2":"She is beautiful.","example:16:exzh3":"She is my friend.","example:16:exzh4":"She likes music.","example:16:exzh5":"I watched a movie with her.","grammar:16:ex:trans":"She is a student.","grammar:16:ex:structure":"A は B です","grammar:16:ex:explain":"This is a noun-predicate sentence, \"AはBです\". 「は」 brings out 「彼女」 as the topic, giving the nuance of \"as for her, she's a student\"; it is a topic marker, not a nominative particle, and beginners often mix this up. The predicate 「学生です」 uses 「です」 for a polite assertion meaning \"is…\". This pattern is the most basic frame in Japanese for self-introductions and explanations, linking a topic to an identity or attribute.","grammar:16:ex:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:16:ex:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:16:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:16:ex:words:1:note":"Marks the topic \"she\"","grammar:16:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex:words:2:zh":"student","grammar:16:ex:words:2:note":"がくせい","grammar:16:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:16:ex:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:16:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:16:ex:points:0":"は marks the topic \"her\"; it is not a nominative marker.","grammar:16:ex:points:1":"Noun＋です＝polite assertion \"is…\".","grammar:16:ex2:trans":"She is beautiful.","grammar:16:ex2:structure":"〔topic〕は＋i-adjective＋です","grammar:16:ex2:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:16:ex2:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:16:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:16:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex2:words:2:zh":"beautiful","grammar:16:ex2:words:2:note":"うつくしい","grammar:16:ex2:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:16:ex2:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:16:ex2:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:16:ex2:points:0":"美しい is an i-adjective, so it takes です directly to become polite (no な).","grammar:16:ex2:points:1":"The negative is 美しくないです。","grammar:16:ex3:trans":"She is my friend.","grammar:16:ex3:structure":"A は〔C の D〕です","grammar:16:ex3:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:16:ex3:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:16:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:16:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex3:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:16:ex3:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:16:ex3:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex3:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:16:ex3:words:3:note":"Shows possession","grammar:16:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex3:words:4:zh":"friend","grammar:16:ex3:words:4:note":"ともだち","grammar:16:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:16:ex3:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:16:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:16:ex3:points:0":"の links two nouns to show possession: 私の友達.","grammar:16:ex3:points:1":"Noun-predicate sentence: 〜は〜です.","grammar:16:ex4:trans":"She likes music.","grammar:16:ex4:structure":"〔topic〕は〔object〕が好きです","grammar:16:ex4:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:16:ex4:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:16:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:16:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex4:words:2:zh":"music","grammar:16:ex4:words:2:note":"おんがく","grammar:16:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:16:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object of liking)","grammar:16:ex4:words:3:note":"Marks the object of 「好き」","grammar:16:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex4:words:4:zh":"to like","grammar:16:ex4:words:4:note":"すき","grammar:16:ex4:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:16:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:16:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:16:ex4:points:0":"This sentence has both は and が: **は marks the topic (her), while が marks the object of liking (music)** — the classic 「〜は〜が好き」 structure.","grammar:16:ex4:points:1":"❓Why is it が after 音楽 and not は? Because the object of 「好き」 takes が by rule, and は is already used by 「她」 (her) up front as the topic.","grammar:16:ex4:points:2":"For contrast you can switch the object to は: 「音楽は好き（でも…）」= \"I do like the music (but…)\".","grammar:16:ex5:trans":"I watched a movie with her.","grammar:16:ex5:structure":"〜と〜を＋verb-ました","grammar:16:ex5:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:16:ex5:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:16:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:16:ex5:words:1:zh":"with","grammar:16:ex5:words:1:note":"Marks the person you do the action together with","grammar:16:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex5:words:2:zh":"movie","grammar:16:ex5:words:2:note":"えいが","grammar:16:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:16:ex5:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:16:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:16:ex5:words:4:zh":"watched","grammar:16:ex5:words:4:note":"みました; past masu-form, dictionary form 見る","grammar:16:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:16:ex5:points:0":"と marks \"the person you do the action together with\" (with her).","grammar:16:ex5:points:1":"見る→見ました: past masu-form (〜ました).","exam:16:zh":"The woman over there is Ms. Tanaka, and she is my older sister.","exam:16:why":"「彼女」 here refers to the woman mentioned earlier. 「彼」 refers to a man and does not fit 「女の人」."},"19":{"example:19:exzh":"I heard an interesting story.","example:19:exzh2":"I like her story.","example:19:exzh3":"Is that story true?","example:19:exzh4":"Long ago, there was an interesting story.","example:19:exzh5":"Let's talk about all sorts of things.","grammar:19:ex:trans":"I heard an interesting story.","grammar:19:ex:structure":"i-adjective + noun + を + verb-ました. The adjective modifies 「話」 directly, 「を」 marks what was heard, and the verb is in the past polite form.","grammar:19:ex:explain":"This sentence ties a few basics together. First, the i-adjective 「面白い」 modifies the noun 「話」 directly: with no particle in between, you get 「面白い話」 (an interesting story). 「を」 marks what was heard. The verb 「聞く」 is a godan (u-) verb, and its past polite form is 「聞きました」, that is, you change 「ます」 in the masu-form to 「ました」 to show a completed action. The whole sentence says that I heard an interesting story, in the past tense and in polite speech.","grammar:19:ex:words:0:zh":"interesting","grammar:19:ex:words:0:note":"おもしろい; an i-adjective modifies a noun directly","grammar:19:ex:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:19:ex:words:1:zh":"story / talk","grammar:19:ex:words:1:note":"はなし","grammar:19:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:19:ex:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:19:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex:words:3:zh":"heard","grammar:19:ex:words:3:note":"ききました; masu-form past (〜ました)","grammar:19:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:19:ex:points:0":"i-adjectives can attach to nouns directly: 面白い＋話","grammar:19:ex:points:1":"〜ました: the past form of the masu-form (polite)","grammar:19:ex2:trans":"I like her stories.","grammar:19:ex2:structure":"noun + の + noun + が + 好きです. 「の」 links two nouns to show possession, and 「が」 marks the thing you like.","grammar:19:ex2:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:19:ex2:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:19:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:19:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:19:ex2:words:1:note":"Shows possession","grammar:19:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex2:words:2:zh":"story / way of saying","grammar:19:ex2:words:2:note":"はなし","grammar:19:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:19:ex2:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:19:ex2:words:3:note":"The object of 好き takes が","grammar:19:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex2:words:4:zh":"to like","grammar:19:ex2:words:4:note":"すき","grammar:19:ex2:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:19:ex2:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:19:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:19:ex2:points:0":"〜が好きです: expresses liking; the object takes が, not を","grammar:19:ex2:points:1":"の links nouns to show possession: 彼女の話","grammar:19:ex3:trans":"Is that story true?","grammar:19:ex3:structure":"その + noun + は + na-adjective + ですか. 「は」 presents the topic, and the sentence-final 「か」 makes it a question.","grammar:19:ex3:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:19:ex3:words:0:note":"modifies the following noun","grammar:19:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:19:ex3:words:1:zh":"story","grammar:19:ex3:words:1:note":"はなし","grammar:19:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:19:ex3:words:2:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:19:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex3:words:3:zh":"really","grammar:19:ex3:words:3:note":"ほんとう","grammar:19:ex3:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:19:ex3:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:19:ex3:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:19:ex3:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:19:ex3:words:5:note":"marks a question at the end of the sentence","grammar:19:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex3:points:0":"か at the end of a sentence forms a question","grammar:19:ex3:points:1":"その: points to something belonging to the other person or already known, i.e. that one.","grammar:19:ex4:trans":"Once upon a time, there was an interesting story.","grammar:19:ex4:structure":"time adverb + noun + が + ありました. 「が」 marks the thing that exists, and the past polite form of 「ある」 means that it existed (in the past).","grammar:19:ex4:words:0:zh":"long, long ago","grammar:19:ex4:words:0:note":"むかしむかし; a set phrase that opens a story","grammar:19:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:19:ex4:words:1:zh":"interesting","grammar:19:ex4:words:1:note":"おもしろい","grammar:19:ex4:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:19:ex4:words:2:zh":"story","grammar:19:ex4:words:2:note":"はなし","grammar:19:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:19:ex4:words:3:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:19:ex4:words:3:note":"the subject that exists","grammar:19:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex4:words:4:zh":"there was / existed (past)","grammar:19:ex4:words:4:note":"ある→ありました; existence of inanimate things","grammar:19:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:19:ex4:points:0":"ある: existence of inanimate things; the past form is ありました","grammar:19:ex4:points:1":"昔々: the fixed opening phrase for telling a story","grammar:19:ex5:trans":"Let's talk about all kinds of things.","grammar:19:ex5:structure":"na-adjective + noun + を + verb-てみよう. 「色々な」 uses な to modify the noun, and the ending 「〜てみよう」 suggests trying something together.","grammar:19:ex5:words:0:zh":"various","grammar:19:ex5:words:0:note":"いろいろ; a na-adjective uses な to modify a noun","grammar:19:ex5:words:0:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:19:ex5:words:1:zh":"topic","grammar:19:ex5:words:1:note":"はなし","grammar:19:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:19:ex5:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:19:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:19:ex5:words:3:zh":"let's try doing it","grammar:19:ex5:words:3:note":"〜てみる (try doing) + volitional form よう","grammar:19:ex5:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:19:ex5:points:0":"〜てみる: try doing something; the volitional form みよう = let's try","grammar:19:ex5:points:1":"a na-adjective needs な to modify a noun: 色々な話","exam:19:zh":"The story my grandmother told me was about a boy who lived in the mountains long ago.","exam:19:why":"「話をする」 can mean to tell a story, and the second half of the sentence clearly describes the story's content. 「料理をする」 is a correct collocation, but it can't connect to a story about a boy."},"20":{"example:20:exzh":"I exercise every day.","example:20:exzh2":"Studying is important.","example:20:exzh3":"This is easy to do.","example:20:exzh4":"I like playing games with my friends.","example:20:exzh5":"I'm good at cooking.","grammar:20:ex:trans":"I exercise every day.","grammar:20:ex:structure":"〔noun〕＋する","grammar:20:ex:explain":"This sentence shows how 「noun + する」 forms a verb. Many Sino-Japanese nouns turn into verbs when する is attached: 「運動」＋「する」＝「運動する」 (to exercise). Here the dictionary form 「する」 is used, which is plain style with a casual tone; the polite form is 「します」. The adverb 「毎日」 means \"every day\". 「する」 is one of Japanese's two irregular verbs, so its conjugations need special memorizing — for example polite 「します」 and te-form 「して」.","grammar:20:ex:words:0:zh":"every day","grammar:20:ex:words:0:note":"まいにち","grammar:20:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:20:ex:words:1:zh":"exercise","grammar:20:ex:words:1:note":"うんどう","grammar:20:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex:words:2:zh":"do","grammar:20:ex:words:2:note":"dictionary form; polite form します","grammar:20:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:20:ex:points:0":"Noun＋する forms a verb: 運動する＝to exercise.","grammar:20:ex:points:1":"する is the plain dictionary form; the polite form is します.","grammar:20:ex2:trans":"Studying is important.","grammar:20:ex2:structure":"verb＋ことが大切です","grammar:20:ex2:words:0:zh":"study","grammar:20:ex2:words:0:note":"べんきょう","grammar:20:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex2:words:1:zh":"do","grammar:20:ex2:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:20:ex2:words:2:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:20:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex2:words:3:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:20:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex2:words:4:zh":"important","grammar:20:ex2:words:4:note":"たいせつ","grammar:20:ex2:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:20:ex2:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:20:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:20:ex2:points:0":"Plain-form verb＋こと \"nominalizes\" the action so it can work as the subject.","grammar:20:ex2:points:1":"❓Why が? こと is the thing that 「大切」 describes, so が is used.","grammar:20:ex3:trans":"This is easy to do.","grammar:20:ex3:structure":"〜のは＋na-adjective＋です","grammar:20:ex3:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:20:ex3:words:0:note":"これ","grammar:20:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:20:ex3:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:20:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex3:words:2:zh":"do","grammar:20:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:20:ex3:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:20:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex3:words:4:zh":"(topic)","grammar:20:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex3:words:5:zh":"easy","grammar:20:ex3:words:5:note":"かんたん","grammar:20:ex3:words:5:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:20:ex3:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:20:ex3:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:20:ex3:points:0":"Both の and こと can nominalize an action; の is common in casual speech.","grammar:20:ex3:points:1":"❓Why は here and not が? \"Doing this\" is presented as the topic being commented on (it's easy), so は is used.","grammar:20:ex4:trans":"I like playing games with friends.","grammar:20:ex4:structure":"人と〜をすることが好きです","grammar:20:ex4:explain":"「ゲームをする」 means to play games, and 「友達と」 adds the person you play with. 「こと」 nominalizes the whole phrase 「友達とゲームをする」, making it the object of liking. 「好き」 is a na-adjective, and liking is usually expressed with 「〜が好きです」.","grammar:20:ex4:words:0:zh":"friend","grammar:20:ex4:words:0:note":"ともだち","grammar:20:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex4:words:1:zh":"(the person you do the action together with)","grammar:20:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex4:words:2:zh":"game","grammar:20:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object)","grammar:20:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex4:words:4:zh":"do; here it means play","grammar:20:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:20:ex4:words:5:zh":"(nominalizes the action)","grammar:20:ex4:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex4:words:6:zh":"(marks the object of liking)","grammar:20:ex4:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex4:words:7:zh":"to like","grammar:20:ex4:words:7:note":"すき","grammar:20:ex4:words:7:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:20:ex4:words:8:zh":"(states it politely)","grammar:20:ex4:words:8:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:20:ex4:points:0":"The 「と」 in 「友達と」 marks the person you do something together with.","grammar:20:ex4:points:1":"「dictionary-form verb＋ことが好きです」 expresses liking to do something.","grammar:20:ex5:trans":"I'm good at cooking.","grammar:20:ex5:structure":"〜のが得意です","grammar:20:ex5:words:0:zh":"cooking","grammar:20:ex5:words:0:note":"りょうり","grammar:20:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:20:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:20:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex5:words:2:zh":"do","grammar:20:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:20:ex5:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:20:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex5:words:4:zh":"(object)","grammar:20:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:20:ex5:words:5:zh":"good at","grammar:20:ex5:words:5:note":"とくい","grammar:20:ex5:words:5:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:20:ex5:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:20:ex5:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:20:ex5:points:0":"〜のが得意です: to be good at doing….","grammar:20:ex5:points:1":"The object of 「得意」 also takes が (just like 「好き」／「上手」).","exam:20:zh":"I plan to play tennis with friends on Sunday.","exam:20:why":"「テニスをする」 is the natural collocation for playing tennis. 「走る」 means to run, and you cannot say 「テニスを走る」 to mean playing tennis."},"21":{"example:21:exzh":"That's interesting.","example:21:exzh2":"Did you see that?","example:21:exzh3":"I want to buy that.","example:21:exzh4":"That's my dog.","example:21:exzh5":"Please tell me that.","grammar:21:ex:trans":"That is interesting.","grammar:21:ex:structure":"それは＋i-adjective＋です","grammar:21:ex:explain":"This is the pattern 「demonstrative＋は＋i-adjective＋です」. 「それ」 belongs to the 「そ」 series of the こそあど system and refers to something near the listener or something just mentioned; it is often translated as \"that\". 「は」 presents it as the topic. The predicate 「面白い」 is an i-adjective that takes 「です」 directly to become polite, meaning \"interesting\". Note that the 「そ」 series (それ・そこ・その) usually points to the listener's side or to an already-known topic, so keep it distinct from the 「こ」 series, which is near the speaker.","grammar:21:ex:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:21:ex:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:21:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:21:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex:words:2:zh":"interesting","grammar:21:ex:words:2:note":"おもしろい","grammar:21:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:21:ex:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:21:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:21:ex:points:0":"それ: refers to something near the listener or just mentioned (the 「そ」 of こそあど).","grammar:21:ex:points:1":"面白いです: polite form of an i-adjective.","grammar:21:ex2:trans":"Have you seen that?","grammar:21:ex2:structure":"〜を＋verb-ましたか","grammar:21:ex2:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:21:ex2:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:21:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:21:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex2:words:2:zh":"watched","grammar:21:ex2:words:2:note":"みました","grammar:21:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:21:ex2:words:3:zh":"(question)","grammar:21:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex2:points:0":"〜ましたか: past-tense question \"did …?\"","grammar:21:ex2:points:1":"を marks the object.","grammar:21:ex3:trans":"I want to buy that.","grammar:21:ex3:structure":"〜を＋verb-たいです","grammar:21:ex3:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:21:ex3:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:21:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex3:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:21:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex3:words:2:zh":"want to buy","grammar:21:ex3:words:2:note":"かいたい; 買う＋たい","grammar:21:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:21:ex3:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:21:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:21:ex3:points:0":"〜たい: the speaker's wish \"want to…\"; 買う→買いたい.","grammar:21:ex3:points:1":"For the object of a wish, either を or が works in casual speech (それを／それが買いたい).","grammar:21:ex4:trans":"That's my dog.","grammar:21:ex4:structure":"それは＋noun＋です","grammar:21:ex4:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:21:ex4:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:21:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:21:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex4:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:21:ex4:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:21:ex4:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex4:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:21:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex4:words:4:zh":"dog","grammar:21:ex4:words:4:note":"いぬ","grammar:21:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:21:ex4:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:21:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:21:ex4:points:0":"の marks possession: 私の犬.","grammar:21:ex4:points:1":"noun predicate＋です.","grammar:21:ex5:trans":"Please tell me that.","grammar:21:ex5:structure":"〜を教えてください","grammar:21:ex5:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:21:ex5:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:21:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:21:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:21:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:21:ex5:words:2:zh":"tell","grammar:21:ex5:words:2:note":"おしえて; te-form","grammar:21:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:21:ex5:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:21:ex5:words:3:note":"〜てください","grammar:21:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:21:ex5:points:0":"〜てください: please do…; 教える→教えて (te-form).","grammar:21:ex5:points:1":"を marks the content being taught.","exam:21:zh":"I'd like to see what you're holding in your hand now, so please pass that over to me.","exam:21:why":"For something in the listener's hand, close to the listener, you use 「それ」. 「これ」 refers to something close to the speaker."},"24":{"example:24:exzh":"Good morning.","example:24:exzh2":"How are you?","example:24:exzh3":"What is your name?","example:24:exzh4":"I drink tea.","example:24:exzh5":"I bought a souvenir.","grammar:24:ex:trans":"Good morning.","grammar:24:ex:structure":"(fixed greeting)","grammar:24:ex:explain":"「おはようございます」 is the polite morning greeting, used when you meet someone. It actually developed from the honorific form of the adjective 「早い」 and carries the original sense of \"(it's still) early.\" With friends, family, or people of your own status you can shorten it to the more casual 「おはよう」; adding 「ございます」 makes it courteous and formal, which suits superiors, bosses, or the workplace. Whether the register is formal or not is adjusted entirely by this 「ございます」.","grammar:24:ex:words:0:zh":"good morning","grammar:24:ex:words:0:note":"a polite morning greeting","grammar:24:ex:words:0:pos":"a set greeting phrase","grammar:24:ex:points:0":"おはようございます: the polite morning greeting.","grammar:24:ex:points:1":"With people you know well, it can be shortened to おはよう.","grammar:24:ex2:trans":"How are you?","grammar:24:ex2:structure":"お＋noun＋ですか","grammar:24:ex2:words:0:zh":"(beautification / respect)","grammar:24:ex2:words:0:note":"Adding it before a noun makes the phrase more polite.","grammar:24:ex2:words:0:pos":"prefix","grammar:24:ex2:words:1:zh":"well / healthy","grammar:24:ex2:words:1:note":"げんき","grammar:24:ex2:words:1:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:24:ex2:words:2:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:24:ex2:words:2:pos":"copula","grammar:24:ex2:words:3:zh":"(question)","grammar:24:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:24:ex2:points:0":"お is a beautifying / respectful prefix.","grammar:24:ex2:points:1":"お元気ですか: a polite way to ask how someone is doing.","grammar:24:ex3:trans":"What is your name?","grammar:24:ex3:structure":"お名前は何ですか","grammar:24:ex3:words:0:zh":"(respect)","grammar:24:ex3:words:0:pos":"prefix","grammar:24:ex3:words:1:zh":"name","grammar:24:ex3:words:1:note":"なまえ","grammar:24:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:24:ex3:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:24:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:24:ex3:words:3:zh":"what","grammar:24:ex3:words:3:note":"なに／なん","grammar:24:ex3:words:3:pos":"question word","grammar:24:ex3:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:24:ex3:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:24:ex3:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:24:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:24:ex3:points:0":"お名前: the other person's name (the お adds respect; never used for yourself).","grammar:24:ex3:points:1":"何ですか: asks \"what is it?\"","grammar:24:ex4:trans":"I drink tea.","grammar:24:ex4:structure":"お＋noun＋を + verbます","grammar:24:ex4:words:0:zh":"(beautification)","grammar:24:ex4:words:0:pos":"prefix","grammar:24:ex4:words:1:zh":"tea","grammar:24:ex4:words:1:note":"ちゃ","grammar:24:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:24:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:24:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:24:ex4:words:3:zh":"to drink","grammar:24:ex4:words:3:note":"のみます","grammar:24:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:24:ex4:points:0":"お茶: tea (the お is habitually attached and counts as beautifying language).","grammar:24:ex4:points:1":"を＋飲みます: to drink tea.","grammar:24:ex5:trans":"I bought a souvenir.","grammar:24:ex5:structure":"〜を買いました","grammar:24:ex5:words:0:zh":"(beautification)","grammar:24:ex5:words:0:pos":"prefix","grammar:24:ex5:words:1:zh":"souvenir / local gift","grammar:24:ex5:words:1:note":"みやげ","grammar:24:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:24:ex5:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:24:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:24:ex5:words:3:zh":"bought","grammar:24:ex5:words:3:note":"かいました","grammar:24:ex5:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:24:ex5:points:0":"お土産 (おみやげ): souvenir gift (the お is customarily attached).","grammar:24:ex5:points:1":"買う→買いました: past polite form.","exam:24:zh":"When saying 「茶」 politely, you add 「お」 in front and say 「お茶」.","exam:24:why":"「お茶」 uses the prefix 「お」. 「ご」 can also show politeness, but that does not make 「茶」 into 「ご茶」."},"25":{"example:25:exzh":"That's right.","example:25:exzh2":"I think so.","example:25:exzh3":"That's what I said.","example:25:exzh4":"That's what he thinks.","example:25:exzh5":"Yeah, that's a good idea.","grammar:25:ex:trans":"Yeah, that's right.","grammar:25:ex:structure":"そうですね","grammar:25:ex:explain":"「そうですね」 is an extremely common phrase for agreeing or back-channeling in conversation. 「そう」 refers to what was just said (\"that way\"), 「です」 makes it polite, and the sentence-final 「ね」 is a particle that seeks the listener's agreement and closes the distance between you. Note that it is sometimes just a filler that softens your reply or buys time to think — it doesn't necessarily mean strong agreement, and drawn out it can even sound hesitant.","grammar:25:ex:words:0:zh":"that way","grammar:25:ex:words:0:note":"そう","grammar:25:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:25:ex:words:1:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:25:ex:words:1:pos":"copula","grammar:25:ex:words:2:zh":"right?","grammar:25:ex:words:2:note":"seeking agreement","grammar:25:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:25:ex:points:0":"そうですね: a common phrase for agreeing or back-channeling.","grammar:25:ex:points:1":"ね: sentence-final particle seeking the listener's agreement.","grammar:25:ex2:trans":"I think so.","grammar:25:ex2:structure":"〜はそう思います","grammar:25:ex2:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:25:ex2:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:25:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:25:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:25:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:25:ex2:words:2:zh":"that way","grammar:25:ex2:words:2:note":"そう","grammar:25:ex2:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:25:ex2:words:3:zh":"think","grammar:25:ex2:words:3:note":"おもいます","grammar:25:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:25:ex2:points:0":"そう思います: I think so.","grammar:25:ex2:points:1":"思う→思います.","grammar:25:ex3:trans":"I said so.","grammar:25:ex3:structure":"そう＋verbました","grammar:25:ex3:words:0:zh":"that way","grammar:25:ex3:words:0:note":"refers to what was just said","grammar:25:ex3:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:25:ex3:words:1:zh":"said","grammar:25:ex3:words:1:note":"いいました","grammar:25:ex3:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:25:ex3:points:0":"そう refers to what was just said — \"(in) that way.\"","grammar:25:ex3:points:1":"言う→言いました: past polite form.","grammar:25:ex4:trans":"He thinks so.","grammar:25:ex4:structure":"〜はそう思っている","grammar:25:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:25:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:25:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:25:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:25:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:25:ex4:words:2:zh":"that way","grammar:25:ex4:words:2:note":"そう","grammar:25:ex4:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:25:ex4:words:3:zh":"thinks","grammar:25:ex4:words:3:note":"おもっている; 〜ている shows a state","grammar:25:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:25:ex4:points:0":"〜ている: expresses an ongoing thought or state (he keeps thinking that way).","grammar:25:ex4:points:1":"Plain form 思っている (polite 思っています).","grammar:25:ex5:trans":"Yeah, good idea.","grammar:25:ex5:structure":"そうですね、〜です","grammar:25:ex5:words:0:zh":"that way","grammar:25:ex5:words:0:note":"そう","grammar:25:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:25:ex5:words:1:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:25:ex5:words:1:pos":"copula","grammar:25:ex5:words:2:zh":"yeah / right","grammar:25:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:25:ex5:words:3:zh":"good","grammar:25:ex5:words:3:note":"いい","grammar:25:ex5:words:3:pos":"adjective","grammar:25:ex5:words:4:zh":"idea","grammar:25:ex5:words:4:note":"かんがえ","grammar:25:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:25:ex5:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:25:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:25:ex5:points:0":"そうですね: an opener that agrees and gives you a moment to think.","grammar:25:ex5:points:1":"いい考え: a good idea (an i-adjective attaches directly to a noun).","exam:25:zh":"Hearing your opinion that \"this town is quiet and easy to live in,\" I felt the same way.","exam:25:why":"「そう思う」 means to agree or to hold the idea just mentioned. 「たくさん」 means a large amount and can't mean \"having the same view.\""},"26":{"example:26:exzh":"That's an important thing.","example:26:exzh2":"There are lots of things to do.","example:26:exzh3":"You can go to Japan.","example:26:exzh4":"I'm thinking about that.","example:26:exzh5":"I like him.","grammar:26:ex:trans":"That is an important thing.","grammar:26:ex:structure":"〜な＋こと＋です","grammar:26:ex:explain":"The key here is the rule for na-adjectives modifying nouns. When a na-adjective (adjectival noun) attaches to a noun, な must always come in between, so it is 「大切なこと」, not 「大切こと」. That differs from i-adjectives, which attach directly to nouns, and it is a mistake beginners often make. 「こと」 refers to an abstract \"thing/matter.\" 「それは⋯です」 is the noun-predicate frame, and the whole sentence says \"that is an important thing.\"","grammar:26:ex:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:26:ex:words:0:note":"それ","grammar:26:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:26:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:26:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex:words:2:zh":"important","grammar:26:ex:words:2:note":"たいせつ","grammar:26:ex:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:26:ex:words:3:zh":"(na-adjective attributive form)","grammar:26:ex:words:3:note":"na-adjectives use な to modify a noun","grammar:26:ex:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:26:ex:words:4:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:26:ex:words:4:note":"こと","grammar:26:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:26:ex:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:26:ex:points:0":"❗Na-adjectives need な to modify a noun: 大切な＋こと.","grammar:26:ex:points:1":"こと refers to an abstract \"matter.\"","grammar:26:ex2:trans":"There are lots of things to do.","grammar:26:ex2:structure":"verb＋ことがあります","grammar:26:ex2:words:0:zh":"do","grammar:26:ex2:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:26:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominalizer) thing","grammar:26:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex2:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:26:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex2:words:3:zh":"a lot","grammar:26:ex2:words:3:note":"たくさん","grammar:26:ex2:words:3:pos":"adverb","grammar:26:ex2:words:4:zh":"there is / are","grammar:26:ex2:words:4:note":"existential verb","grammar:26:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:26:ex2:points:0":"verb＋こと: nominalizes the verb (the thing to do).","grammar:26:ex2:points:1":"〜がたくさんあります: there are many… (existential sentences use が).","grammar:26:ex3:trans":"I can go to Japan.","grammar:26:ex3:structure":"verb＋ことができます","grammar:26:ex3:words:0:zh":"Japan","grammar:26:ex3:words:0:note":"にほん","grammar:26:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex3:words:1:zh":"(destination)","grammar:26:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex3:words:2:zh":"go","grammar:26:ex3:words:2:note":"いく","grammar:26:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:26:ex3:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:26:ex3:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex3:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:26:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex3:words:5:zh":"can","grammar:26:ex3:words:5:note":"possible","grammar:26:ex3:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:26:ex3:points:0":"〜ことができる: to be able to (do)… (expresses ability / possibility).","grammar:26:ex3:points:1":"に marks the destination of movement.","grammar:26:ex4:trans":"I'm thinking about that.","grammar:26:ex4:structure":"そのことを＋verbています","grammar:26:ex4:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:26:ex4:words:0:note":"その","grammar:26:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:26:ex4:words:1:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:26:ex4:words:1:note":"こと","grammar:26:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:26:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex4:words:3:zh":"thinking about","grammar:26:ex4:words:3:note":"かんがえています; 〜ている","grammar:26:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:26:ex4:points:0":"その＋noun: that… (the \"so\" of the こそあど series).","grammar:26:ex4:points:1":"〜ている: an action in progress (in the middle of considering).","grammar:26:ex5:trans":"I like him.","grammar:26:ex5:structure":"〜のことが／を好きです","grammar:26:ex5:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:26:ex5:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:26:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:26:ex5:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:26:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex5:words:2:zh":"(people or things)","grammar:26:ex5:words:2:note":"refers to \"everything about him\"","grammar:26:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:26:ex5:words:3:zh":"(casual-speech object)","grammar:26:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:26:ex5:words:4:zh":"to like","grammar:26:ex5:words:4:note":"すき","grammar:26:ex5:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:26:ex5:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:26:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:26:ex5:points:0":"「〜のことが好き」 is the idiomatic way to say \"I like someone.\"","grammar:26:ex5:points:1":"❓By the rules, the object of 「好き」 should take が; in casual speech you often hear を (as in this sentence), but on exams use が.","exam:26:zh":"I can write letters in Japanese.","exam:26:why":"「Verb dictionary form + ことができる」 means being able to do something. 「物」 means a thing and cannot replace 「こと」, which turns the action into a noun here."},"29":{"example:29:exzh":"Let's go now.","example:29:exzh2":"Please try once more.","example:29:exzh3":"I'm good now.","example:29:exzh4":"It's already late.","example:29:exzh5":"I'll be there soon.","grammar:29:ex:trans":"Let's go now.","grammar:29:ex:structure":"もう＋verbましょう","grammar:29:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「もう＋verbましょう」 to make a suggestion. 「もう」 means \"already,\" implying the situation has changed and the time has come — \"it's about time we went.\" 「〜ましょう」 is an inviting, proposing expression used to suggest doing something together, like \"let's…\". The verb 「行く」 becomes 「行きましょう」. The whole sentence 「もう行きましょう」 mixes a gentle push with an invitation: \"we should get going — let's go.\"","grammar:29:ex:words:0:zh":"already","grammar:29:ex:words:0:note":"もう","grammar:29:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:29:ex:words:1:zh":"let's go","grammar:29:ex:words:1:note":"いきましょう","grammar:29:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:29:ex:points:0":"もう: already (the situation has changed — time to go).","grammar:29:ex:points:1":"〜ましょう: a suggestion, \"let's…\"","grammar:29:ex2:trans":"Please try once more.","grammar:29:ex2:structure":"もう一度＋verbてください","grammar:29:ex2:words:0:zh":"one more time","grammar:29:ex2:words:0:note":"もういちど","grammar:29:ex2:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:29:ex2:words:1:zh":"try","grammar:29:ex2:words:1:note":"ためして; te-form","grammar:29:ex2:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:29:ex2:words:2:zh":"please","grammar:29:ex2:words:2:note":"〜てください","grammar:29:ex2:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:29:ex2:points:0":"もう一度: one more time (「もう＋quantity」 adds another round).","grammar:29:ex2:points:1":"〜てください: please do…; 試す→試して.","grammar:29:ex3:trans":"I don't need it anymore.","grammar:29:ex3:structure":"もういい（よ）","grammar:29:ex3:words:0:zh":"already","grammar:29:ex3:words:0:note":"もう","grammar:29:ex3:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:29:ex3:words:1:zh":"fine / enough","grammar:29:ex3:words:1:note":"いい","grammar:29:ex3:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:29:ex3:words:2:zh":"(informative tone)","grammar:29:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:29:ex3:points:0":"もういい: enough / no thanks (can be positive or negative depending on tone).","grammar:29:ex3:points:1":"よ: sentence-final particle that informs or reminds the listener.","grammar:29:ex4:trans":"It's already late.","grammar:29:ex4:structure":"もう＋i-adjective＋です","grammar:29:ex4:words:0:zh":"already","grammar:29:ex4:words:0:note":"もう","grammar:29:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:29:ex4:words:1:zh":"late","grammar:29:ex4:words:1:note":"おそい","grammar:29:ex4:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:29:ex4:words:2:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:29:ex4:words:2:pos":"copula","grammar:29:ex4:points:0":"もう＋遅い: it's already late.","grammar:29:ex4:points:1":"遅いです: i-adjective in the polite form.","grammar:29:ex5:trans":"We'll be arriving soon.","grammar:29:ex5:structure":"もうすぐ＋verbます","grammar:29:ex5:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:29:ex5:words:0:note":"もうすぐ","grammar:29:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:29:ex5:words:1:zh":"arrive","grammar:29:ex5:words:1:note":"つきます","grammar:29:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:29:ex5:points:0":"もうすぐ: soon, in a moment (≠もう \"already\").","grammar:29:ex5:points:1":"着く→着きます: to arrive.","exam:29:zh":"My homework is all done, so I can play now.","exam:29:why":"「もう」 with 「終わった」 means something is already finished. 「まだ」 means not yet or still, and it can't express that everything is done here."},"30":{"example:30:exzh":"Has he come yet?","example:30:exzh2":"A friend is coming over.","example:30:exzh3":"The child is coming back from school.","example:30:exzh4":"She's scheduled to come tomorrow.","example:30:exzh5":"Where are you from?","grammar:30:ex:trans":"Has he arrived yet?","grammar:30:ex:structure":"もう＋verbましたか","grammar:30:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「もう〜ましたか」 to ask whether something has already happened. 「もう」 means \"already,\" and with a past-tense question it checks whether an action has occurred: \"has he arrived yet?\" The verb 「来る」 is irregular, and its stem changes sound: polite 「来ます」 (きます) and past 「来ました」 — the reading shifts among き, く, and こ, so it has to be memorized. 「は」 makes 「彼」 the topic, and 「か」 turns the sentence into a question.","grammar:30:ex:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:30:ex:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:30:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:30:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:30:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex:words:2:zh":"already","grammar:30:ex:words:2:note":"もう","grammar:30:ex:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:30:ex:words:3:zh":"came","grammar:30:ex:words:3:note":"きました; irregular","grammar:30:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex:words:4:zh":"(question)","grammar:30:ex:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex:points:0":"来る is an irregular verb: 来ます／来ました (read with き).","grammar:30:ex:points:1":"もう〜ましたか: has … already happened?","grammar:30:ex2:trans":"A friend is coming over.","grammar:30:ex2:structure":"〔verb masu-form / action noun〕に来る","grammar:30:ex2:words:0:zh":"friend","grammar:30:ex2:words:0:note":"ともだち","grammar:30:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:30:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:30:ex2:words:1:note":"the person coming (new information takes が)","grammar:30:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex2:words:2:zh":"hang out","grammar:30:ex2:words:2:note":"あそび; the noun form of 遊ぶ","grammar:30:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:30:ex2:words:3:zh":"(purpose)","grammar:30:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex2:words:4:zh":"come","grammar:30:ex2:words:4:note":"くる","grammar:30:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex2:points:0":"〜に来る: come in order to…; 遊びに来る = come over to hang out.","grammar:30:ex2:points:1":"が marks the person coming (が is used when first mentioning someone).","grammar:30:ex3:trans":"The child is coming home from school.","grammar:30:ex3:structure":"〜から帰って来る","grammar:30:ex3:words:0:zh":"child","grammar:30:ex3:words:0:note":"こども","grammar:30:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:30:ex3:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:30:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex3:words:2:zh":"school","grammar:30:ex3:words:2:note":"がっこう","grammar:30:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:30:ex3:words:3:zh":"from","grammar:30:ex3:words:3:note":"starting point","grammar:30:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex3:words:4:zh":"return","grammar:30:ex3:words:4:note":"かえって; te-form","grammar:30:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex3:words:5:zh":"come","grammar:30:ex3:words:5:note":"くる","grammar:30:ex3:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex3:points:0":"から: from (starting point).","grammar:30:ex3:points:1":"〜てくる: do something and come back / toward the speaker; 帰って来る = come home.","grammar:30:ex4:trans":"She is scheduled to come tomorrow.","grammar:30:ex4:structure":"verb＋予定です","grammar:30:ex4:words:0:zh":"tomorrow","grammar:30:ex4:words:0:note":"あした","grammar:30:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:30:ex4:words:1:zh":"she","grammar:30:ex4:words:1:note":"かのじょ","grammar:30:ex4:words:1:pos":"pronoun","grammar:30:ex4:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:30:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex4:words:3:zh":"come","grammar:30:ex4:words:3:note":"くる","grammar:30:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex4:words:4:zh":"plan","grammar:30:ex4:words:4:note":"よてい","grammar:30:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:30:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:30:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:30:ex4:points:0":"〜予定です: is scheduled to…","grammar:30:ex4:points:1":"来る＋予定: is scheduled to come.","grammar:30:ex5:trans":"Where are you from?","grammar:30:ex5:structure":"どこから来ましたか","grammar:30:ex5:words:0:zh":"where","grammar:30:ex5:words:0:note":"どこ","grammar:30:ex5:words:0:pos":"question word","grammar:30:ex5:words:1:zh":"from","grammar:30:ex5:words:1:note":"starting point","grammar:30:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex5:words:2:zh":"came","grammar:30:ex5:words:2:note":"きました","grammar:30:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:30:ex5:words:3:zh":"(question)","grammar:30:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:30:ex5:points:0":"どこから: from where (questioning the starting point).","grammar:30:ex5:points:1":"It can also ask about origin or where someone is from.","exam:30:zh":"My friend is coming to my house tomorrow, so I will wait at home.","exam:30:why":"「来る」 means moving toward the place where the speaker is. 「帰る」 means returning to your own home or the place you belong to, but here the friend is visiting."},"31":{"example:31:exzh":"I'm a student.","example:31:exzh2":"My name is Taro.","example:31:exzh3":"There are four people in my family.","example:31:exzh4":"I like music.","example:31:exzh5":"I'll go.","grammar:31:ex:trans":"I'm a student.","grammar:31:ex:structure":"僕は＋noun＋です","grammar:31:ex:explain":"This is a self-introduction sentence using 「僕は〜です」. 「僕 (ぼく)」 is a first-person \"I\" used by men; it sounds casual and friendly — more relaxed than 「私」 but politer than 「俺」. Women generally don't use 「僕」. 「は」 makes 「僕」 the topic, and the predicate 「学生です」 uses 「です」 for a polite statement. Which first-person pronoun you pick reveals your gender, age, and the situation, and Japanese is quite particular about this detail.","grammar:31:ex:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:31:ex:words:0:note":"ぼく; a male first-person pronoun","grammar:31:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:31:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:31:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex:words:2:zh":"student","grammar:31:ex:words:2:note":"がくせい","grammar:31:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:31:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:31:ex:points:0":"「僕」: a rather casual masculine way for a man to say \"I\" (women generally use 「私」).","grammar:31:ex:points:1":"noun＋です: polite statement.","grammar:31:ex2:trans":"My name is 太郎.","grammar:31:ex2:structure":"僕の名前は〜です","grammar:31:ex2:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:31:ex2:words:0:note":"ぼく","grammar:31:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:31:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:31:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex2:words:2:zh":"name","grammar:31:ex2:words:2:note":"なまえ","grammar:31:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex2:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:31:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex2:words:4:zh":"Tarō","grammar:31:ex2:words:4:note":"たろう; a personal name","grammar:31:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex2:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:31:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:31:ex2:points:0":"の shows possession: 僕の名前.","grammar:31:ex2:points:1":"The basic pattern for introducing yourself.","grammar:31:ex3:trans":"There are four people in my family.","grammar:31:ex3:structure":"〜は＋number of people＋です","grammar:31:ex3:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:31:ex3:words:0:note":"ぼく","grammar:31:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:31:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:31:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex3:words:2:zh":"family","grammar:31:ex3:words:2:note":"かぞく","grammar:31:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex3:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:31:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex3:words:4:zh":"four people","grammar:31:ex3:words:4:note":"よにん","grammar:31:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex3:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:31:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:31:ex3:points:0":"四人 (よにん): four people (a special reading for counting people).","grammar:31:ex3:points:1":"〜は…人です: states the number of people.","grammar:31:ex4:trans":"I like music.","grammar:31:ex4:structure":"〜は〜が好きです","grammar:31:ex4:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:31:ex4:words:0:note":"ぼく","grammar:31:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:31:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:31:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex4:words:2:zh":"music","grammar:31:ex4:words:2:note":"おんがく","grammar:31:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:31:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object of liking)","grammar:31:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex4:words:4:zh":"to like","grammar:31:ex4:words:4:note":"すき","grammar:31:ex4:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:31:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:31:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:31:ex4:points:0":"The object of 「好き」 takes が (音楽が好き).","grammar:31:ex4:points:1":"は marks the topic (me), が marks the object (music).","grammar:31:ex5:trans":"I'll go.","grammar:31:ex5:structure":"僕が＋verb（よ）","grammar:31:ex5:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:31:ex5:words:0:note":"ぼく","grammar:31:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:31:ex5:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:31:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex5:words:2:zh":"go","grammar:31:ex5:words:2:note":"いく","grammar:31:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:31:ex5:words:3:zh":"(informing)","grammar:31:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:31:ex5:points:0":"❓Why が instead of は? It emphasizes \"I'm the one going\" (が is exclusive and singles out the subject).","grammar:31:ex5:points:1":"よ: sentence-final particle that informs or states your intent."},"33":{"example:33:exzh":"This alone is enough.","example:33:exzh2":"It's a job that takes just one day.","example:33:exzh3":"That alone won't satisfy him.","example:33:exzh4":"The only thing to drink is water.","example:33:exzh5":"Right now, that's all I'm thinking about.","grammar:33:ex:trans":"This is enough.","grammar:33:ex:structure":"〜だけで十分です","grammar:33:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「〜だけで」 to say \"just this is enough.\" 「だけ」 is a limiting particle meaning \"only,\" restricting the scope to 「これ」. The 「で」 after it expresses means or scope here, so 「これだけで」 means \"with just this.\" In the predicate 「十分です」, 「十分」 is a na-adjective meaning \"sufficient\" and attaches directly to 「です」. The tone is \"this is more than enough,\" and it is often used to politely turn down anything extra.","grammar:33:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:33:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:33:ex:words:1:zh":"only","grammar:33:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex:words:2:zh":"(scope)","grammar:33:ex:words:2:note":"just with… is enough","grammar:33:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex:words:3:zh":"enough","grammar:33:ex:words:3:note":"じゅうぶん","grammar:33:ex:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:33:ex:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:33:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:33:ex:points:0":"だけ: a limiting particle, \"only.\"","grammar:33:ex:points:1":"〜だけで: just with… (で marks means / scope).","grammar:33:ex2:trans":"This is a job that takes only one day.","grammar:33:ex2:structure":"〜だけの＋noun","grammar:33:ex2:words:0:zh":"one day","grammar:33:ex2:words:0:note":"いちにち","grammar:33:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex2:words:1:zh":"only","grammar:33:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex2:words:2:zh":"'s","grammar:33:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex2:words:3:zh":"work","grammar:33:ex2:words:3:note":"しごと","grammar:33:ex2:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex2:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:33:ex2:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:33:ex2:points:0":"一日だけの仕事: a job of just one day.","grammar:33:ex2:points:1":"だけ can attach directly to の to modify a noun.","grammar:33:ex3:trans":"That alone won't satisfy him.","grammar:33:ex3:structure":"〜だけでは〜ない","grammar:33:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:33:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:33:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:33:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:33:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex3:words:2:zh":"that","grammar:33:ex3:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:33:ex3:words:3:zh":"only","grammar:33:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex3:words:4:zh":"(by means of)","grammar:33:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex3:words:5:zh":"(contrastive emphasis)","grammar:33:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex3:words:6:zh":"be satisfied","grammar:33:ex3:words:6:note":"まんぞく","grammar:33:ex3:words:6:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex3:words:7:zh":"doesn't do","grammar:33:ex3:words:7:note":"しない: negative form","grammar:33:ex3:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:33:ex3:points:0":"〜だけでは〜ない: just with ... it isn't ... (では strengthens the negative).","grammar:33:ex3:points:1":"満足しない: the plain negative of する.","grammar:33:ex4:trans":"The only drink is water.","grammar:33:ex4:structure":"〜は〜だけです","grammar:33:ex4:words:0:zh":"drink","grammar:33:ex4:words:0:note":"のみもの","grammar:33:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:33:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex4:words:2:zh":"water","grammar:33:ex4:words:2:note":"みず","grammar:33:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex4:words:3:zh":"only","grammar:33:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex4:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:33:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:33:ex4:points:0":"〜だけです: only ... / nothing but ....","grammar:33:ex4:points:1":"だけ comes after a noun and limits it directly.","grammar:33:ex5:trans":"Right now I'm only thinking about that.","grammar:33:ex5:structure":"〜だけ＋verb-ています","grammar:33:ex5:words:0:zh":"now","grammar:33:ex5:words:0:note":"いま","grammar:33:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:33:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:33:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex5:words:2:zh":"that","grammar:33:ex5:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:33:ex5:words:3:zh":"only","grammar:33:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:33:ex5:words:4:zh":"thinking about","grammar:33:ex5:words:4:note":"かんがえています","grammar:33:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:33:ex5:points:0":"だけ can also limit the scope of an action: only thinking about that.","grammar:33:ex5:points:1":"〜ている: ongoing action."},"34":{"example:34:exzh":"If you're going, you'd better leave early.","example:34:exzh2":"If he's coming, let's get ready.","example:34:exzh3":"If you're going to Japan, you need a visa.","example:34:exzh4":"If you're there, help me.","example:34:exzh5":"If you're staying over, that hotel is a good choice.","grammar:34:ex:trans":"If you're going, it's better to leave early.","grammar:34:ex:structure":"〜なら、〜た方がいい","grammar:34:ex:explain":"This sentence combines two patterns. The first half, 「行くなら」, uses the conditional particle 「なら」 to mean 'if you're going'; 「なら」 is especially used when you pick up a topic or premise the other person raised and then give advice. The second half, 「〜た方がいい」, is a fixed pattern for giving advice: a verb in ta-form plus 「方がいい」 means '(doing) ... is better', so 「早めに出発した方がいい」 urges the other person to 'leave early'. The whole sentence sets a condition first, then gives advice.","grammar:34:ex:words:0:zh":"go","grammar:34:ex:words:0:note":"いく","grammar:34:ex:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex:words:1:zh":"if ...","grammar:34:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex:words:2:zh":"a little earlier","grammar:34:ex:words:2:note":"はやめに","grammar:34:ex:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:34:ex:words:3:zh":"depart","grammar:34:ex:words:3:note":"しゅっぱつした","grammar:34:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex:words:4:zh":"it's better to","grammar:34:ex:words:4:note":"ほうがいい","grammar:34:ex:words:4:pos":"set phrase","grammar:34:ex:points:0":"〜なら: the conditional 'if ...'.","grammar:34:ex:points:1":"〜た方がいい: it's better to (do) ... (advice).","grammar:34:ex2:trans":"If he's coming, let's get ready.","grammar:34:ex2:structure":"〜なら、〜ましょう","grammar:34:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:34:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:34:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:34:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:34:ex2:words:1:note":"subject of the subordinate clause","grammar:34:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex2:words:2:zh":"come","grammar:34:ex2:words:2:note":"くる","grammar:34:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex2:words:3:zh":"if","grammar:34:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex2:words:4:zh":"prepare","grammar:34:ex2:words:4:note":"じゅんび","grammar:34:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:34:ex2:words:5:zh":"let's do","grammar:34:ex2:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex2:points:0":"❓Why が? The subject inside the clause (his coming) usually takes が.","grammar:34:ex2:points:1":"〜なら＋ましょう: if ..., let's ....","grammar:34:ex3:trans":"If you're going to Japan, you need a visa.","grammar:34:ex3:structure":"〜なら、〜が必要です","grammar:34:ex3:words:0:zh":"Japan","grammar:34:ex3:words:0:note":"にほん","grammar:34:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:34:ex3:words:1:zh":"to","grammar:34:ex3:words:1:note":"direction","grammar:34:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex3:words:2:zh":"go","grammar:34:ex3:words:2:note":"いく","grammar:34:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex3:words:3:zh":"if","grammar:34:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex3:words:4:zh":"visa","grammar:34:ex3:words:4:note":"loanword","grammar:34:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:34:ex3:words:5:zh":"(object)","grammar:34:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex3:words:6:zh":"necessary","grammar:34:ex3:words:6:note":"ひつよう","grammar:34:ex3:words:6:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:34:ex3:words:7:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:34:ex3:words:7:pos":"copula","grammar:34:ex3:points:0":"へ: marks the direction of movement (≈に).","grammar:34:ex3:points:1":"〜が必要です: ... is needed (the thing needed takes が).","grammar:34:ex4:trans":"If you're there, please help.","grammar:34:ex4:structure":"〜なら、〜て（ください）","grammar:34:ex4:words:0:zh":"you","grammar:34:ex4:words:0:note":"きみ","grammar:34:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:34:ex4:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:34:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex4:words:2:zh":"there","grammar:34:ex4:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:34:ex4:words:3:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:34:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex4:words:4:zh":"exist","grammar:34:ex4:words:4:note":"people / animals","grammar:34:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex4:words:5:zh":"if","grammar:34:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex4:words:6:zh":"help","grammar:34:ex4:words:6:note":"たすけて; te-form request","grammar:34:ex4:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex4:points:0":"いる: 'to be' for people and animals (things take ある).","grammar:34:ex4:points:1":"助けて: te-form used as a casual request (= 助けてください).","grammar:34:ex5:trans":"If you're staying overnight, that hotel is a good choice.","grammar:34:ex5:structure":"〜なら、〜がいい","grammar:34:ex5:words:0:zh":"stay overnight","grammar:34:ex5:words:0:note":"とまる","grammar:34:ex5:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:34:ex5:words:1:zh":"if","grammar:34:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex5:words:2:zh":"that","grammar:34:ex5:words:2:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:34:ex5:words:3:zh":"hotel","grammar:34:ex5:words:3:note":"loanword","grammar:34:ex5:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:34:ex5:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:34:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:34:ex5:words:5:zh":"good","grammar:34:ex5:words:5:pos":"adjective","grammar:34:ex5:points:0":"〜がいい: ... is better / recommended (が used when choosing).","grammar:34:ex5:points:1":"なら states the premise first, then gives advice."},"35":{"example:35:exzh":"This job requires a driver.","example:35:exzh2":"I won't forgive people like that.","example:35:exzh3":"He is an excellent researcher.","example:35:exzh4":"People who love music gathered together.","example:35:exzh5":"This person is extremely important.","grammar:35:ex:trans":"This job needs a driver.","grammar:35:ex:structure":"〜は〜が必要です","grammar:35:ex:explain":"There are two key points. First, the suffix 「者（しゃ）」 attaches after a noun to mean 'a person who ...', so 「運転」＋「者」＝「運転者」 (driver). Second, 「〜が必要です」 means '... is needed', and the thing needed is marked with 「が」 rather than 「を」 — the same が-marking rule as with 「好き・できる」, where an adjective-like predicate takes が. 「は」 makes the whole job the topic, and the sentence says this job requires a driver.","grammar:35:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:35:ex:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:35:ex:words:1:zh":"work","grammar:35:ex:words:1:note":"しごと","grammar:35:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:35:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex:words:3:zh":"driver","grammar:35:ex:words:3:note":"うんてんしゃ","grammar:35:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex:words:4:zh":"(object)","grammar:35:ex:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex:words:5:zh":"necessary","grammar:35:ex:words:5:note":"ひつよう","grammar:35:ex:words:5:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:35:ex:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:35:ex:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:35:ex:points:0":"者（しゃ）: a suffix after a word meaning 'a person who ...' (運転者 = driver).","grammar:35:ex:points:1":"〜が必要です: ... is needed (the thing needed takes が).","grammar:35:ex2:trans":"I won't forgive anyone like that.","grammar:35:ex2:structure":"〜は〜ない","grammar:35:ex2:words:0:zh":"such","grammar:35:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:35:ex2:words:1:zh":"person","grammar:35:ex2:words:1:note":"もの","grammar:35:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex2:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:35:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex2:words:3:zh":"not forgive","grammar:35:ex2:words:3:note":"ゆるさない","grammar:35:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:35:ex2:points:0":"者（もの）: 'person' in written style (kun reading もの).","grammar:35:ex2:points:1":"許さない: the plain negative of 許す.","grammar:35:ex3:trans":"He is an excellent researcher.","grammar:35:ex3:structure":"〜な＋noun＋です","grammar:35:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:35:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:35:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:35:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:35:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex3:words:2:zh":"excellent","grammar:35:ex3:words:2:note":"ゆうしゅう","grammar:35:ex3:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:35:ex3:words:3:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:35:ex3:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:35:ex3:words:4:zh":"researcher","grammar:35:ex3:words:4:note":"けんきゅうしゃ","grammar:35:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex3:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:35:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:35:ex3:points:0":"A na-adjective adds な when it modifies a noun: 優秀な研究者.","grammar:35:ex3:points:1":"者（しゃ）: a person in a professional field.","grammar:35:ex4:trans":"People who love music gathered together.","grammar:35:ex4:structure":"〔verb〕者が〜た","grammar:35:ex4:words:0:zh":"music","grammar:35:ex4:words:0:note":"おんがく","grammar:35:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex4:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:35:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex4:words:2:zh":"love","grammar:35:ex4:words:2:note":"あいする","grammar:35:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:35:ex4:words:3:zh":"person","grammar:35:ex4:words:3:note":"もの","grammar:35:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex4:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:35:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex4:words:5:zh":"gathered","grammar:35:ex4:words:5:note":"あつまった","grammar:35:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:35:ex4:points:0":"Verb＋者: a person who does ... (modifying).","grammar:35:ex4:points:1":"集まる→集まった: plain past.","grammar:35:ex5:trans":"This person is extremely important.","grammar:35:ex5:structure":"〜は非常に〜です","grammar:35:ex5:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:35:ex5:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:35:ex5:words:1:zh":"person","grammar:35:ex5:words:1:note":"もの","grammar:35:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:35:ex5:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:35:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:35:ex5:words:3:zh":"extremely","grammar:35:ex5:words:3:note":"ひじょうに","grammar:35:ex5:words:3:pos":"adverb","grammar:35:ex5:words:4:zh":"important","grammar:35:ex5:words:4:note":"じゅうよう","grammar:35:ex5:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:35:ex5:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:35:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:35:ex5:points:0":"非常に: extremely (adverb of degree).","grammar:35:ex5:points:1":"者（もの）: a formal way of saying 'person'."},"36":{"example:36:exzh":"He met his death in an accident.","example:36:exzh2":"Death is a part of nature.","example:36:exzh3":"What is the world after death like?","example:36:exzh4":"Everyone meets death someday.","example:36:exzh5":"You can hear voices lamenting the death."},"37":{"example:37:exzh":"Now is the time to study.","example:37:exzh2":"I treasure the good times.","example:37:exzh3":"He came at just the right time.","example:37:exzh4":"Time passes quickly.","example:37:exzh5":"Please be careful when you do this job.","grammar:37:ex:trans":"Now is the time to study.","grammar:37:ex:structure":"今はverb dictionary form＋時です","grammar:37:ex:explain":"「今は」 brings 'now' up as the topic. 「勉強する」 goes directly before 「時」 to form 'the time to study', with no 「の」 in between. The whole sentence frames the present as the period when one should study, and depending on context it can also mean it's time to hit the books now.","grammar:37:ex:words:0:zh":"now","grammar:37:ex:words:0:note":"いま","grammar:37:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex:words:1:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:37:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex:words:2:zh":"study","grammar:37:ex:words:2:note":"べんきょう","grammar:37:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex:words:3:zh":"do","grammar:37:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex:words:4:zh":"time","grammar:37:ex:words:4:note":"とき","grammar:37:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex:words:5:zh":"(states it politely)","grammar:37:ex:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:37:ex:points:0":"「勉強する」 is the noun 「勉強」 plus 「する」, meaning to study or learn.","grammar:37:ex:points:1":"A verb can modify 「時」 directly: 「勉強する時」 means the time when you study.","grammar:37:ex2:trans":"I treasure happy times.","grammar:37:ex2:structure":"〜を大切にします","grammar:37:ex2:explain":"「楽しい時」 means happy times, and here 「時」 is read 「とき」. 「大切にする」 means to treat something as important, that is, to treasure it. 「を」 marks the thing treasured, and 「します」 is the polite form of 「する」.","grammar:37:ex2:words:0:zh":"enjoyable","grammar:37:ex2:words:0:note":"たのしい","grammar:37:ex2:words:0:pos":"i-adjective","grammar:37:ex2:words:1:zh":"time","grammar:37:ex2:words:1:note":"とき","grammar:37:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex2:words:2:zh":"(object)","grammar:37:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex2:words:3:zh":"important, precious","grammar:37:ex2:words:3:note":"たいせつ","grammar:37:ex2:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:37:ex2:words:4:zh":"(turns a na-adjective into a form that modifies an action)","grammar:37:ex2:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex2:words:5:zh":"treat","grammar:37:ex2:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex2:words:6:zh":"(polite ending)","grammar:37:ex2:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:37:ex2:points:0":"「楽しい」 is an i-adjective, so it can modify the noun 「時」 directly.","grammar:37:ex2:points:1":"「〜を大切にする」 is a set phrase meaning to treasure or value something.","grammar:37:ex3:trans":"He came at just the right time.","grammar:37:ex3:structure":"ちょうどいい時に来ました","grammar:37:ex3:explain":"「ちょうど」 modifies 「いい」, stressing that the timing was just right. 「ちょうどいい時に」 means at just the right moment, and 「来ました」 follows to say he came. The point is that the timing of his arrival was perfect, not merely that he arrived at an exact time.","grammar:37:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:37:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:37:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:37:ex3:words:1:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:37:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex3:words:2:zh":"just, exactly","grammar:37:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:37:ex3:words:3:zh":"good, suitable","grammar:37:ex3:words:3:pos":"i-adjective","grammar:37:ex3:words:4:zh":"time","grammar:37:ex3:words:4:note":"とき","grammar:37:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex3:words:5:zh":"(time when an action happens)","grammar:37:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex3:words:6:zh":"come","grammar:37:ex3:words:6:note":"き","grammar:37:ex3:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex3:words:7:zh":"(polite ending)","grammar:37:ex3:words:7:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:37:ex3:words:8:zh":"(past)","grammar:37:ex3:words:8:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:37:ex3:points:0":"「ちょうどいい」 means just right, perfectly suitable.","grammar:37:ex3:points:1":"The 「に」 in 「時に」 marks the time when an action happens.","grammar:37:ex3:points:2":"「来る」 is read 「きます」 with 「ます」, and its past form is 「きました」.","grammar:37:ex4:trans":"Time passes so fast.","grammar:37:ex4:structure":"〜のは早いです","grammar:37:ex4:words:0:zh":"time","grammar:37:ex4:words:0:note":"とき","grammar:37:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex4:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:37:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex4:words:2:zh":"pass (of time)","grammar:37:ex4:words:2:note":"たつ","grammar:37:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex4:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:37:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex4:words:4:zh":"(topic)","grammar:37:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex4:words:5:zh":"fast","grammar:37:ex4:words:5:note":"はやい","grammar:37:ex4:words:5:pos":"adjective","grammar:37:ex4:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:37:ex4:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:37:ex4:points:0":"Here 時 is read とき ('time').","grammar:37:ex4:points:1":"〜のは早い: ... (that fact) is fast (の nominalizes ＋ は).","grammar:37:ex5:trans":"Please be careful when you do this job.","grammar:37:ex5:structure":"verb dictionary form＋時は、気をつけてください","grammar:37:ex5:explain":"The whole phrase 「この仕事をする」 modifies 「時」, meaning when you do this job. 「は」 makes that moment the situation the following warning applies to. 「気をつける」 is a set phrase meaning to be careful or pay attention; put it in te-form and add 「ください」 and you get 'please be careful'.","grammar:37:ex5:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:37:ex5:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:37:ex5:words:1:zh":"work","grammar:37:ex5:words:1:note":"しごと","grammar:37:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex5:words:2:zh":"(object)","grammar:37:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex5:words:3:zh":"do","grammar:37:ex5:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex5:words:4:zh":"time","grammar:37:ex5:words:4:note":"とき","grammar:37:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex5:words:5:zh":"(presents the situation as the topic)","grammar:37:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex5:words:6:zh":"attention, mind","grammar:37:ex5:words:6:note":"き","grammar:37:ex5:words:6:pos":"noun","grammar:37:ex5:words:7:zh":"(object)","grammar:37:ex5:words:7:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex5:words:8:zh":"attach, put on; combined with 「気」 here it means paying attention","grammar:37:ex5:words:8:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex5:words:9:zh":"(connects to a request expression)","grammar:37:ex5:words:9:pos":"particle","grammar:37:ex5:words:10:zh":"please","grammar:37:ex5:words:10:pos":"verb","grammar:37:ex5:points:0":"「この」 must be followed by a noun; 「この仕事」 means this job.","grammar:37:ex5:points:1":"「〜する時は」 means when doing something, and presents that situation as the topic.","grammar:37:ex5:points:2":"「気をつけてください」 is a common way to tell someone to be careful.","exam:37:zh":"As a child, I often played in this park.","exam:37:why":"「子どもの時」 means when I was a child and is the natural way to describe a stage of life. 「時間」 refers to a length of time and so on, so it can't simply replace 「時」 here."},"38":{"example:38:exzh":"Is this information necessary?","example:38:exzh2":"Please bring only what you need.","example:38:exzh3":"I felt that his opinion was needed.","example:38:exzh4":"New skills are necessary.","example:38:exzh5":"Let's make sure we set aside the time we need.","grammar:38:ex:trans":"Is this information necessary?","grammar:38:ex:structure":"〜は必要ですか","grammar:38:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「〜は必要ですか」 to ask whether something is necessary. 「必要」 is a na-adjective; as a predicate it takes 「です」 directly (必要です), and it adds な only when modifying a noun (必要な情報). 「は」 makes 「この情報」 the topic, and the question particle 「か」 at the end turns the sentence into a question asking whether this information is necessary. This 「AはＸですか」 frame is the most basic yes-no question pattern.","grammar:38:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:38:ex:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:38:ex:words:1:zh":"information","grammar:38:ex:words:1:note":"じょうほう","grammar:38:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:38:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex:words:3:zh":"necessary","grammar:38:ex:words:3:note":"ひつよう","grammar:38:ex:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:38:ex:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:38:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:38:ex:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:38:ex:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex:points:0":"必要 is a na-adjective; as a predicate it takes です directly.","grammar:38:ex:points:1":"か: question particle at the end.","grammar:38:ex2:trans":"Please bring only what you need.","grammar:38:ex2:structure":"〜なもの＋だけ〜てください","grammar:38:ex2:words:0:zh":"necessary","grammar:38:ex2:words:0:note":"ひつよう","grammar:38:ex2:words:0:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:38:ex2:words:1:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:38:ex2:words:1:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:38:ex2:words:2:zh":"things","grammar:38:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex2:words:3:zh":"only","grammar:38:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex2:words:4:zh":"bring","grammar:38:ex2:words:4:note":"もってきて","grammar:38:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:38:ex2:words:5:zh":"please","grammar:38:ex2:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:38:ex2:points:0":"A na-adjective adds な when modifying a noun: 必要なもの.","grammar:38:ex2:points:1":"持ってくる: 持って＋くる = to bring.","grammar:38:ex3:trans":"I felt that his opinion was necessary.","grammar:38:ex3:structure":"〜だと感じました","grammar:38:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:38:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:38:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:38:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:38:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex3:words:2:zh":"opinion","grammar:38:ex3:words:2:note":"いけん","grammar:38:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex3:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:38:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex3:words:4:zh":"necessary","grammar:38:ex3:words:4:note":"ひつよう","grammar:38:ex3:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:38:ex3:words:5:zh":"is (plain form)","grammar:38:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:38:ex3:words:6:zh":"(quotation)","grammar:38:ex3:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex3:words:7:zh":"think","grammar:38:ex3:words:7:note":"かんじました","grammar:38:ex3:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:38:ex3:points:0":"〜と感じる: to feel that ... (と quotes the thought).","grammar:38:ex3:points:1":"A na-adjective uses だ for plain assertion: 必要だ.","grammar:38:ex4:trans":"A new skill is necessary.","grammar:38:ex4:structure":"〜は必要です (〜 is necessary)","grammar:38:ex4:words:0:zh":"new","grammar:38:ex4:words:0:note":"あたらしい","grammar:38:ex4:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:38:ex4:words:1:zh":"skill","grammar:38:ex4:words:1:note":"loanword","grammar:38:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex4:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:38:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex4:words:3:zh":"necessary","grammar:38:ex4:words:3:note":"ひつよう","grammar:38:ex4:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:38:ex4:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:38:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:38:ex4:points:0":"新しい: an i-adjective modifies a noun directly.","grammar:38:ex4:points:1":"必要です: na-adjective in polite form.","grammar:38:ex5:trans":"Let's make sure we set aside the time we need.","grammar:38:ex5:structure":"〜を確保しましょう (let's secure 〜)","grammar:38:ex5:words:0:zh":"necessary","grammar:38:ex5:words:0:note":"ひつよう","grammar:38:ex5:words:0:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:38:ex5:words:1:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:38:ex5:words:1:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:38:ex5:words:2:zh":"time","grammar:38:ex5:words:2:note":"じかん","grammar:38:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex5:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:38:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:38:ex5:words:4:zh":"secure","grammar:38:ex5:words:4:note":"かくほ","grammar:38:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:38:ex5:words:5:zh":"let's do","grammar:38:ex5:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:38:ex5:points:0":"必要な時間: the time needed (na-adjective + noun).","grammar:38:ex5:points:1":"確保する → 確保しましょう: a suggestion."},"39":{"example:39:exzh":"There's a cat in the room.","example:39:exzh2":"He succeeded in his work.","example:39:exzh3":"I'm in the room now.","example:39:exzh4":"Please choose from these.","example:39:exzh5":"Please come inside.","grammar:39:ex:trans":"There's a cat in the room.","grammar:39:ex:structure":"〜の中に〜がいます (there is 〜 in 〜)","grammar:39:ex:explain":"This sentence is about location and existence. 「中（なか）」 is a noun of position, 「〜の中に」 means 'inside 〜', and 「に」 marks the place where something exists. The key point is choosing the existence verb: a cat is alive, so you use 「います」 (いる); 「あります」 is only for inanimate things. 「が」 marks the thing that exists, 「猫」. The whole sentence means 'there's a cat in the room', and it reviews both position nouns and existence sentences for living things.","grammar:39:ex:words:0:zh":"room","grammar:39:ex:words:0:note":"へや","grammar:39:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:39:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex:words:2:zh":"inside","grammar:39:ex:words:2:note":"なか","grammar:39:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex:words:3:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:39:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex:words:4:zh":"cat","grammar:39:ex:words:4:note":"ねこ","grammar:39:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:39:ex:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex:words:6:zh":"there is (living things)","grammar:39:ex:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:39:ex:points:0":"中（なか）: inside; 〜の中に = inside 〜.","grammar:39:ex:points:1":"❓います vs あります? Use います for living things (a cat).","grammar:39:ex2:trans":"He succeeded in his work.","grammar:39:ex2:structure":"〜の中で〜しました (did 〜 within 〜)","grammar:39:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:39:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:39:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:39:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:39:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex2:words:2:zh":"work","grammar:39:ex2:words:2:note":"しごと","grammar:39:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:39:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex2:words:4:zh":"inside","grammar:39:ex2:words:4:note":"なか","grammar:39:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex2:words:5:zh":"(scope)","grammar:39:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex2:words:6:zh":"success","grammar:39:ex2:words:6:note":"せいこう","grammar:39:ex2:words:6:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex2:words:7:zh":"did","grammar:39:ex2:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:39:ex2:points:0":"〜の中で: within 〜 (で marks a scope or field).","grammar:39:ex2:points:1":"成功する → 成功しました.","grammar:39:ex3:trans":"I'm in the room right now.","grammar:39:ex3:structure":"今は〜の中にいます (right now I'm in 〜)","grammar:39:ex3:explain":"「部屋の中」 means the inside of the room, and 「に」 marks the location. 「います」 is the polite form of 「いる」; here it simply says a person is somewhere, not the progressive 「〜ています」 pattern. The subject is omitted, and from the given situation it means I'm in the room right now.","grammar:39:ex3:words:0:zh":"now","grammar:39:ex3:words:0:note":"いま","grammar:39:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex3:words:1:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:39:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex3:words:2:zh":"room","grammar:39:ex3:words:2:note":"へや","grammar:39:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex3:words:3:zh":"(attaches to a noun to show a positional relationship)","grammar:39:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex3:words:4:zh":"inside","grammar:39:ex3:words:4:note":"なか","grammar:39:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex3:words:5:zh":"(the location where something exists)","grammar:39:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex3:words:6:zh":"to be, to exist","grammar:39:ex3:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:39:ex3:words:7:zh":"(polite ending)","grammar:39:ex3:words:7:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:39:ex3:points:0":"「〜の中」 means the inside of some space, and 「中」 is read なか here.","grammar:39:ex3:points:1":"For the existence of people or animals you usually use 「いる」, and 「に」 marks where they are.","grammar:39:ex4:trans":"Please choose from among these.","grammar:39:ex4:structure":"〜の中から選んでください (please choose from among 〜)","grammar:39:ex4:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:39:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:39:ex4:words:1:zh":"inside","grammar:39:ex4:words:1:note":"なか","grammar:39:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex4:words:2:zh":"from","grammar:39:ex4:words:2:note":"starting point","grammar:39:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex4:words:3:zh":"choose","grammar:39:ex4:words:3:note":"えらんで","grammar:39:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:39:ex4:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:39:ex4:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:39:ex4:points:0":"〜の中から: from inside 〜 (から marks the starting point).","grammar:39:ex4:points:1":"選ぶ → 選んで (te-form) + ください.","grammar:39:ex5:trans":"Please go inside.","grammar:39:ex5:structure":"中に入ってください (please go inside)","grammar:39:ex5:words:0:zh":"inside","grammar:39:ex5:words:0:note":"なか","grammar:39:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:39:ex5:words:1:zh":"(direction)","grammar:39:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:39:ex5:words:2:zh":"enter","grammar:39:ex5:words:2:note":"はいって","grammar:39:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:39:ex5:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:39:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:39:ex5:points:0":"中に入る: to go inside (に marks direction / point of arrival).","grammar:39:ex5:points:1":"入る → 入って (te-form).","exam:39:zh":"When I opened the box, there was a small doll inside it.","exam:39:why":"「中」 means the inside and matches 「箱に入っている」. 「上」 means on top of the box, not inside it."},"40":{"example:40:exzh":"There's a bus in front of the station.","example:40:exzh2":"He's standing in front of me.","example:40:exzh3":"Please move forward.","example:40:exzh4":"I brush my teeth before bed.","example:40:exzh5":"I'm waiting in front of the store.","grammar:40:ex:trans":"There's a bus in front of the station.","grammar:40:ex:structure":"〜の前に〜があります (there is 〜 in front of 〜)","grammar:40:ex:explain":"This sentence contrasts with the previous set and is about the existence of inanimate things. 「前（まえ）」 is a noun of position, 「〜の前に」 means 'in front of 〜', and 「に」 marks the place of existence. The key is the verb: a bus is inanimate, so you use 「あります」 (ある); 「います」 is only for people or animals. 「が」 marks the thing that exists, 「バス」. Remembering 「います／あります」 by whether something is alive is the most important point in this lesson.","grammar:40:ex:words:0:zh":"station","grammar:40:ex:words:0:note":"えき","grammar:40:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:40:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex:words:2:zh":"front","grammar:40:ex:words:2:note":"まえ","grammar:40:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex:words:3:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:40:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex:words:4:zh":"bus","grammar:40:ex:words:4:note":"loanword","grammar:40:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:40:ex:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex:words:6:zh":"there is (inanimate things)","grammar:40:ex:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex:points:0":"前（まえ）: front; 〜の前に = in front of 〜.","grammar:40:ex:points:1":"❓あります vs います? Use あります for inanimate things (a bus).","grammar:40:ex2:trans":"He's standing in front of me.","grammar:40:ex2:structure":"〜の前に立っています (is standing in front of 〜)","grammar:40:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:40:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:40:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:40:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:40:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex2:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:40:ex2:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:40:ex2:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:40:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:40:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex2:words:4:zh":"front","grammar:40:ex2:words:4:note":"まえ","grammar:40:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex2:words:5:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:40:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex2:words:6:zh":"standing","grammar:40:ex2:words:6:note":"たっています","grammar:40:ex2:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex2:points:0":"〜ている: describes a continuing state (standing).","grammar:40:ex2:points:1":"立つ → 立って + いる.","grammar:40:ex3:trans":"Please go forward.","grammar:40:ex3:structure":"前に進んでください (please go forward)","grammar:40:ex3:words:0:zh":"front","grammar:40:ex3:words:0:note":"まえ","grammar:40:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex3:words:1:zh":"(direction)","grammar:40:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex3:words:2:zh":"move forward","grammar:40:ex3:words:2:note":"すすんで","grammar:40:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex3:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:40:ex3:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:40:ex3:points:0":"前に進む: to move forward (に marks direction).","grammar:40:ex3:points:1":"進む → 進んで (te-form).","grammar:40:ex4:trans":"I brush my teeth before bed.","grammar:40:ex4:structure":"verb dictionary form + 前に + action","grammar:40:ex4:words:0:zh":"sleep","grammar:40:ex4:words:0:note":"ねる","grammar:40:ex4:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex4:words:1:zh":"before","grammar:40:ex4:words:1:note":"まえ","grammar:40:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex4:words:2:zh":"(point in time)","grammar:40:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex4:words:3:zh":"teeth","grammar:40:ex4:words:3:note":"は","grammar:40:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex4:words:4:zh":"(object)","grammar:40:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex4:words:5:zh":"brush","grammar:40:ex4:words:5:note":"みがきます; masu-form","grammar:40:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex4:points:0":"「寝る前に」: 「前」 after a verb's dictionary form means 'before doing something', not just the spatial 'in front of'.","grammar:40:ex4:points:1":"The verb must be in dictionary form (寝る); you can't attach 「前に」 to the masu-form or ta-form.","grammar:40:ex4:points:2":"「歯をみがきます」: を marks the object of the action, and みがきます is the masu-form of みがく, showing a habit.","grammar:40:ex5:trans":"I'm waiting in front of the shop.","grammar:40:ex5:structure":"〜の前で待っています (waiting in front of 〜)","grammar:40:ex5:words:0:zh":"shop","grammar:40:ex5:words:0:note":"おみせ","grammar:40:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex5:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:40:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex5:words:2:zh":"front","grammar:40:ex5:words:2:note":"まえ","grammar:40:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:40:ex5:words:3:zh":"(place of the action)","grammar:40:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:40:ex5:words:4:zh":"waiting","grammar:40:ex5:words:4:note":"まっています","grammar:40:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:40:ex5:points:0":"❓Why で and not に? 'Waiting' is an action, and で marks the place where an action happens.","grammar:40:ex5:points:1":"〜ている: is waiting (ongoing).","exam:40:zh":"I'm second and Tanaka-san is first, so he's standing one spot ahead of me.","exam:40:why":"In a line, the first spot is 「前」 — in front of the second spot. 「上」 means above and isn't used to describe a place in a line like this."},"42":{"example:42:exzh":"They are friends.","example:42:exzh2":"We'll go together.","example:42:exzh3":"The children are playing.","example:42:exzh4":"The teachers are in the classroom.","example:42:exzh5":"I get along well with them.","grammar:42:ex:trans":"They are friends.","grammar:42:ex:structure":"〜は〜達です (〜 are 〜たち)","grammar:42:ex:explain":"This sentence shows the plural suffix 「達（たち）」. 「達」 attaches to nouns for people to make them plural (〜s, 〜たち), so 「友達」 plus 「達」 becomes 「友達達」 ('friends'). Interestingly, the 「ら」 in the subject 「彼ら」 is itself a plural ending, so 「彼ら」 already means 'they'. 「は」 makes 「彼ら」 the topic, and the predicate 「友達達です」 states what they are. The sentence says 'they are friends' and reviews two ways of showing plural.","grammar:42:ex:words:0:zh":"they","grammar:42:ex:words:0:note":"かれら","grammar:42:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:42:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:42:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex:words:2:zh":"friend","grammar:42:ex:words:2:note":"ともだち","grammar:42:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:42:ex:words:3:zh":"plural marker","grammar:42:ex:words:3:note":"たち","grammar:42:ex:words:3:pos":"suffix","grammar:42:ex:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:42:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:42:ex:points:0":"達（たち）: attaches to nouns for people to show the plural ('〜s').","grammar:42:ex:points:1":"彼ら is already plural (ら is also a plural ending).","grammar:42:ex2:trans":"We'll go together.","grammar:42:ex2:structure":"私達は〜ます (we will 〜)","grammar:42:ex2:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:42:ex2:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:42:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:42:ex2:words:1:zh":"plural marker","grammar:42:ex2:words:1:note":"たち","grammar:42:ex2:words:1:pos":"suffix","grammar:42:ex2:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:42:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex2:words:3:zh":"together","grammar:42:ex2:words:3:note":"いっしょに","grammar:42:ex2:words:3:pos":"adverb","grammar:42:ex2:words:4:zh":"go","grammar:42:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:42:ex2:points:0":"私達（わたしたち）: we.","grammar:42:ex2:points:1":"一緒に: together.","grammar:42:ex3:trans":"The children are playing.","grammar:42:ex3:structure":"〜達が〜ています (〜たち are 〜ing)","grammar:42:ex3:words:0:zh":"child","grammar:42:ex3:words:0:note":"こども","grammar:42:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:42:ex3:words:1:zh":"plural marker","grammar:42:ex3:words:1:note":"たち","grammar:42:ex3:words:1:pos":"suffix","grammar:42:ex3:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:42:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex3:words:3:zh":"playing","grammar:42:ex3:words:3:note":"あそんでいます","grammar:42:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:42:ex3:points:0":"子供達: children.","grammar:42:ex3:points:1":"〜ている: an action in progress (playing).","grammar:42:ex4:trans":"The teachers are in the classroom.","grammar:42:ex4:structure":"〜達は〜にいます (〜たち are in 〜)","grammar:42:ex4:words:0:zh":"teacher","grammar:42:ex4:words:0:note":"せんせい","grammar:42:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:42:ex4:words:1:zh":"plural marker","grammar:42:ex4:words:1:note":"たち","grammar:42:ex4:words:1:pos":"suffix","grammar:42:ex4:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:42:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex4:words:3:zh":"classroom","grammar:42:ex4:words:3:note":"きょうしつ","grammar:42:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:42:ex4:words:4:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:42:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex4:words:5:zh":"exist","grammar:42:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:42:ex4:points:0":"先生達: teachers.","grammar:42:ex4:points:1":"に + います: (a person) is somewhere.","grammar:42:ex5:trans":"I'm on good terms with them.","grammar:42:ex5:structure":"〜達とは仲良しです (I'm close with 〜たち)","grammar:42:ex5:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:42:ex5:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:42:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:42:ex5:words:1:zh":"plural marker","grammar:42:ex5:words:1:note":"たち","grammar:42:ex5:words:1:pos":"suffix","grammar:42:ex5:words:2:zh":"with","grammar:42:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex5:words:3:zh":"(contrast)","grammar:42:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:42:ex5:words:4:zh":"close, friendly","grammar:42:ex5:words:4:note":"なかよし","grammar:42:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:42:ex5:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:42:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:42:ex5:points:0":"とは = と + は: with 〜 (with added contrastive emphasis).","grammar:42:ex5:points:1":"仲良し: close, friendly.","exam:42:zh":"When referring to several friends together, you say 「友達たち」, just like 「たち」 in 「私たち」.","exam:42:why":"「たち」 attaches to pronouns or nouns that refer to people to show the plural. 「だけ」 shows limitation and does not mean several people."},"43":{"example:43:exzh":"I'm going to school.","example:43:exzh2":"I wrote a letter to my friend.","example:43:exzh3":"Please go down that road.","example:43:exzh4":"I'm planning to go to Tokyo tomorrow.","example:43:exzh5":"Please come here.","grammar:43:ex:trans":"I'm going to school.","grammar:43:ex:structure":"〜へ行きます (go to 〜)","grammar:43:ex:explain":"Here 「へ」 shows the direction of movement. As a particle, 「へ」 is read え — a point beginners often get wrong. 「学校へ行きます」 means 'go toward school'. When showing the direction of movement, 「へ」 and 「に」 are often interchangeable; the slight difference is that 「へ」 emphasizes the sense of heading in a direction and the process, while 「に」 emphasizes arriving at an endpoint. In everyday conversation the two are almost interchangeable, and for exams just remember that 「へ」 is read え.","grammar:43:ex:words:0:zh":"school","grammar:43:ex:words:0:note":"がっこう","grammar:43:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex:words:1:zh":"to","grammar:43:ex:words:1:note":"direction (read え)","grammar:43:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex:words:2:zh":"go","grammar:43:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:43:ex:points:0":"へ: marks the 'direction' of movement (read え).","grammar:43:ex:points:1":"❓へ vs に? Either works for direction; へ emphasizes direction while に emphasizes the point of arrival.","grammar:43:ex2:trans":"I wrote a letter to my friend.","grammar:43:ex2:structure":"〜へ〜を書きました (wrote 〜 to 〜)","grammar:43:ex2:words:0:zh":"friend","grammar:43:ex2:words:0:note":"ともだち","grammar:43:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex2:words:1:zh":"to","grammar:43:ex2:words:1:note":"recipient","grammar:43:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex2:words:2:zh":"letter","grammar:43:ex2:words:2:note":"てがみ","grammar:43:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex2:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:43:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex2:words:4:zh":"wrote","grammar:43:ex2:words:4:note":"かきました","grammar:43:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:43:ex2:points:0":"へ can also mark 'the person an action is directed at' (writing to a friend).","grammar:43:ex2:points:1":"書く → 書きました.","grammar:43:ex3:trans":"Please take that road.","grammar:43:ex3:structure":"〜へ進んでください (please go along 〜)","grammar:43:ex3:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:43:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:43:ex3:words:1:zh":"road","grammar:43:ex3:words:1:note":"みち","grammar:43:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex3:words:2:zh":"to","grammar:43:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex3:words:3:zh":"move forward","grammar:43:ex3:words:3:note":"すすんで","grammar:43:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:43:ex3:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:43:ex3:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:43:ex3:points:0":"へ: toward (the direction of that road).","grammar:43:ex3:points:1":"進む → 進んで (te-form) + ください.","grammar:43:ex4:trans":"I'm planning to go to Tokyo tomorrow.","grammar:43:ex4:structure":"〜へ行く予定です (I'm planning to go to 〜)","grammar:43:ex4:words:0:zh":"tomorrow","grammar:43:ex4:words:0:note":"あした","grammar:43:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:43:ex4:words:1:zh":"Tokyo","grammar:43:ex4:words:1:note":"とうきょう","grammar:43:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex4:words:2:zh":"to","grammar:43:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex4:words:3:zh":"go","grammar:43:ex4:words:3:note":"いく","grammar:43:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:43:ex4:words:4:zh":"plan","grammar:43:ex4:words:4:note":"よてい","grammar:43:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:43:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:43:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:43:ex4:points:0":"〜予定です: be scheduled to / plan to 〜.","grammar:43:ex4:points:1":"へ: toward Tokyo (direction).","grammar:43:ex5:trans":"Please come here.","grammar:43:ex5:structure":"ここへ来てください (please come here)","grammar:43:ex5:words:0:zh":"here","grammar:43:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:43:ex5:words:1:zh":"to","grammar:43:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:43:ex5:words:2:zh":"come","grammar:43:ex5:words:2:note":"きて","grammar:43:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:43:ex5:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:43:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:43:ex5:points:0":"ここへ: to here.","grammar:43:ex5:points:1":"来る → 来て (te-form, irregular) + ください.","exam:43:zh":"Tomorrow I'm going to Kyoto by train with a friend.","exam:43:why":"「へ」 follows a destination and shows the direction of movement. 「で」 can mark a means of transport or the place where an action happens, so it can't mark the destination of 「行く」 here."},"44":{"example:44:exzh":"Whose thing is that?","example:44:exzh2":"Please take a look at this thing.","example:44:exzh3":"I have something important.","example:44:exzh4":"He has something interesting.","example:44:exzh5":"That's mine.","grammar:44:ex:trans":"Whose is that?","grammar:44:ex:structure":"〜は誰のですか (whose is 〜?)","grammar:44:ex:explain":"This is a possessive question. 「あの」 is the 'a' series pre-noun adjectival in the こそあど system, pointing to something far from both speaker and listener. The predicate 「誰のですか」 uses 「誰の」 to ask who it belongs to, and the noun after 「の」 (もの) is left out because the context makes it clear. 「は」 makes 「あのもの」 the topic, and the final 「か」 turns it into a question. The whole sentence asks 'whose is that thing?', showing how 「〜のですか」 asks about ownership.","grammar:44:ex:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:44:ex:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:44:ex:words:1:zh":"things","grammar:44:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:44:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:44:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex:words:3:zh":"who","grammar:44:ex:words:3:note":"だれ","grammar:44:ex:words:3:pos":"question word","grammar:44:ex:words:4:zh":"'s","grammar:44:ex:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:44:ex:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:44:ex:words:6:zh":"(question)","grammar:44:ex:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex:points:0":"あの: that (far from both speaker and listener).","grammar:44:ex:points:1":"誰の: whose (the noun is omitted).","grammar:44:ex2:trans":"Please look at this.","grammar:44:ex2:structure":"〜を見てください (please look at 〜)","grammar:44:ex2:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:44:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:44:ex2:words:1:zh":"things","grammar:44:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:44:ex2:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:44:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex2:words:3:zh":"look","grammar:44:ex2:words:3:note":"みて","grammar:44:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:44:ex2:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:44:ex2:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:44:ex2:points:0":"もの: a concrete 'thing'.","grammar:44:ex2:points:1":"見て + ください: please look.","grammar:44:ex3:trans":"I have something important.","grammar:44:ex3:structure":"〜には〜があります (〜 has 〜)","grammar:44:ex3:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:44:ex3:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:44:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:44:ex3:words:1:zh":"(the one who has it)","grammar:44:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex3:words:2:zh":"(contrast)","grammar:44:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex3:words:3:zh":"important","grammar:44:ex3:words:3:note":"たいせつ","grammar:44:ex3:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:44:ex3:words:4:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:44:ex3:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:44:ex3:words:5:zh":"things","grammar:44:ex3:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:44:ex3:words:6:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:44:ex3:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex3:words:7:zh":"there is / are","grammar:44:ex3:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:44:ex3:points:0":"〜には〜がある: (for someone) there is 〜 (には = に + は).","grammar:44:ex3:points:1":"大切なもの: something important (na-adjective + noun).","grammar:44:ex4:trans":"He has something interesting.","grammar:44:ex4:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:44:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:44:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:44:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:44:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:44:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex4:words:2:zh":"interesting","grammar:44:ex4:words:2:note":"おもしろい","grammar:44:ex4:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:44:ex4:words:3:zh":"things","grammar:44:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:44:ex4:words:4:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:44:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex4:words:5:zh":"own, have","grammar:44:ex4:words:5:note":"もっています","grammar:44:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:44:ex4:points:0":"〜を持っている: to have / carry 〜 (持つ + ている shows a state).","grammar:44:ex4:points:1":"面白いもの: something interesting.","grammar:44:ex5:trans":"That's mine.","grammar:44:ex5:structure":"〜は〜のものです (〜 belongs to 〜)","grammar:44:ex5:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:44:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:44:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:44:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex5:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:44:ex5:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:44:ex5:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:44:ex5:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:44:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:44:ex5:words:4:zh":"things","grammar:44:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:44:ex5:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:44:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:44:ex5:points:0":"〜のもの: 〜's thing / possession.","grammar:44:ex5:points:1":"私のもの: mine (my thing).","exam:44:zh":"This shop sells various things, such as bags and watches.","exam:44:why":"「物」 refers to concrete things like bags and watches. 「こと」 mainly means matters or actions and cannot cover these products."},"46":{"example:46:exzh":"That guy is a real jerk.","example:46:exzh2":"That guy is pretty interesting.","example:46:exzh3":"That guy is coming.","example:46:exzh4":"That guy has big dreams.","example:46:exzh5":"I don't like that guy."},"47":{"example:47:exzh":"I don't have money.","example:47:exzh2":"I don't have time, so I'll hurry.","example:47:exzh3":"There's no food.","example:47:exzh4":"Wishing for what you don't have.","example:47:exzh5":"It's an experience he doesn't have.","grammar:47:ex:trans":"I don't have any money.","grammar:47:ex:structure":"〜が無いです (there is no 〜)","grammar:47:ex:explain":"This sentence is about how 「ない」 works. 「無い（ない）」 is the negative of the existence verb 「ある」, and it behaves like an i-adjective, so both 「無いです」 and 「ありません」 mean 'there is no / don't have', with the former more casual. 「が」 marks the thing that exists or is possessed, so 「お金が無い」 means 'there's no money'. Note that although 「ない」 is a negative, it inflects by i-adjective rules (the past is 「なかった」), which often confuses beginners.","grammar:47:ex:words:0:zh":"money","grammar:47:ex:words:0:note":"おかね","grammar:47:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:47:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex:words:2:zh":"don't have","grammar:47:ex:words:2:note":"ない","grammar:47:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:47:ex:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:47:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:47:ex:points:0":"❓Why が? The thing that exists or is possessed takes が (お金が無い).","grammar:47:ex:points:1":"無い: the negative of ある, used like an i-adjective (無いです / ありません).","grammar:47:ex2:trans":"I'm in a hurry because there's no time.","grammar:47:ex2:structure":"〜ので〜ます (because 〜, 〜)","grammar:47:ex2:words:0:zh":"time","grammar:47:ex2:words:0:note":"じかん","grammar:47:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:47:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex2:words:2:zh":"don't have","grammar:47:ex2:words:2:note":"ない","grammar:47:ex2:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:47:ex2:words:3:zh":"because","grammar:47:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex2:words:4:zh":"hurry","grammar:47:ex2:words:4:note":"いそぎます","grammar:47:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:47:ex2:points:0":"〜ので: because 〜 (an objective reason, softer than から).","grammar:47:ex2:points:1":"急ぐ → 急ぎます.","grammar:47:ex3:trans":"There's no food.","grammar:47:ex3:structure":"〜が無い (there is no 〜)","grammar:47:ex3:words:0:zh":"food","grammar:47:ex3:words:0:note":"たべもの","grammar:47:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex3:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:47:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex3:words:2:zh":"don't have","grammar:47:ex3:words:2:note":"ない","grammar:47:ex3:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:47:ex3:points:0":"無い: the plain form meaning \"there is not / to not have\" (polite form 無いです).","grammar:47:ex3:points:1":"が marks the subject that does not exist.","grammar:47:ex4:trans":"Wanting what you don't have.","grammar:47:ex4:structure":"無い物ねだり (idiomatic expression)","grammar:47:ex4:words:0:zh":"not existing","grammar:47:ex4:words:0:note":"ない","grammar:47:ex4:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:47:ex4:words:1:zh":"things","grammar:47:ex4:words:1:note":"もの","grammar:47:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex4:words:2:zh":"demanding (something unattainable)","grammar:47:ex4:words:2:note":"ねだり","grammar:47:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex4:points:0":"無い物ねだり: craving what you can never have (a set phrase).","grammar:47:ex4:points:1":"無い＋物: a thing that doesn't exist (i-adjective in its noun-modifying form).","grammar:47:ex5:trans":"An experience he doesn't have.","grammar:47:ex5:structure":"〜には無い〜だ","grammar:47:ex5:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:47:ex5:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:47:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:47:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object)","grammar:47:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex5:words:2:zh":"(contrast)","grammar:47:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:47:ex5:words:3:zh":"not existing","grammar:47:ex5:words:3:note":"ない","grammar:47:ex5:words:3:pos":"adjective","grammar:47:ex5:words:4:zh":"experience","grammar:47:ex5:words:4:note":"けいけん","grammar:47:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:47:ex5:words:5:zh":"is (plain form)","grammar:47:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:47:ex5:points:0":"〜には無い: something that (a certain person) doesn't have.","grammar:47:ex5:points:1":"無い＋経験: an experience he doesn't have (noun-modifying use).","exam:47:zh":"There isn't even a single yen in the wallet, so I can't buy anything.","exam:47:why":"「一円もない」 means there isn't even one yen. 「少ない」 only means a small amount, and it can't pair with 「一円も」 here to mean having none at all."},"49":{"example:49:exzh":"Please believe in yourself.","example:49:exzh2":"Taking good care of yourself is important.","example:49:exzh3":"I want to be honest with myself.","example:49:exzh4":"I'll chase my own dreams.","example:49:exzh5":"Don't lose yourself.","grammar:49:ex:trans":"Please believe in yourself.","grammar:49:ex:structure":"自分を〜てください","grammar:49:ex:explain":"This is a request sentence using 「〜てください」. 「自分」 means \"oneself\" and can refer to any person; here it means the listener. 「を」 marks the object of the action. The verb 「信じる」 is an ichidan (ru-) verb, and its te-form is 「信じて」 (drop る and add て), which combines with 「ください」 to form the polite request \"please (do)…\". The whole sentence 「自分を信じてください」 is a gentle way of encouraging someone, \"please believe in yourself\" — a common phrase of support.","grammar:49:ex:words:0:zh":"oneself","grammar:49:ex:words:0:note":"じぶん","grammar:49:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:49:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:49:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex:words:2:zh":"believe","grammar:49:ex:words:2:note":"しんじて","grammar:49:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:49:ex:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:49:ex:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:49:ex:points:0":"自分: oneself (a person's own self, whoever it is).","grammar:49:ex:points:1":"信じる→信じて (te-form)＋ください。","grammar:49:ex2:trans":"It's important to take good care of yourself.","grammar:49:ex2:structure":"〜にすることが大事です","grammar:49:ex2:words:0:zh":"oneself","grammar:49:ex2:words:0:note":"じぶん","grammar:49:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:49:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:49:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex2:words:2:zh":"with care","grammar:49:ex2:words:2:note":"たいせつに","grammar:49:ex2:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:49:ex2:words:3:zh":"do","grammar:49:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:49:ex2:words:4:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:49:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:49:ex2:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:49:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex2:words:6:zh":"important","grammar:49:ex2:words:6:note":"だいじ","grammar:49:ex2:words:6:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:49:ex2:words:7:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:49:ex2:words:7:pos":"copula","grammar:49:ex2:points:0":"〜を大切にする: to treasure… (na-adjective＋に＋する turns it into an adverb).","grammar:49:ex2:points:1":"verb＋こと: nominalizes the verb so it can serve as the subject (marked by が).","grammar:49:ex3:trans":"I want to be honest with myself.","grammar:49:ex3:structure":"〜に正直でありたい","grammar:49:ex3:words:0:zh":"oneself","grammar:49:ex3:words:0:note":"じぶん","grammar:49:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:49:ex3:words:1:zh":"(object)","grammar:49:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex3:words:2:zh":"honest","grammar:49:ex3:words:2:note":"しょうじき","grammar:49:ex3:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:49:ex3:words:3:zh":"(te-form)","grammar:49:ex3:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:49:ex3:words:4:zh":"want to be","grammar:49:ex3:words:4:note":"〜たい","grammar:49:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:49:ex3:points:0":"〜に正直: honest with… (the target is marked by に).","grammar:49:ex3:points:1":"〜でありたい: to want to be in the state of… (である＋たい).","grammar:49:ex4:trans":"I'll chase my own dream.","grammar:49:ex4:structure":"自分の〜を動詞ます","grammar:49:ex4:words:0:zh":"oneself","grammar:49:ex4:words:0:note":"じぶん","grammar:49:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:49:ex4:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:49:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex4:words:2:zh":"dream","grammar:49:ex4:words:2:note":"ゆめ","grammar:49:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:49:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:49:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex4:words:4:zh":"chase","grammar:49:ex4:words:4:note":"おいかけます","grammar:49:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:49:ex4:points:0":"自分の: one's own (の marks possession).","grammar:49:ex4:points:1":"追いかける→追いかけます。","grammar:49:ex5:trans":"Don't lose yourself.","grammar:49:ex5:structure":"〜を〜ないで","grammar:49:ex5:words:0:zh":"oneself","grammar:49:ex5:words:0:note":"じぶん","grammar:49:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:49:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:49:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:49:ex5:words:2:zh":"don't lose","grammar:49:ex5:words:2:note":"みうしなわないで；〜ないで","grammar:49:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:49:ex5:points:0":"〜ないで (ください): please don't (do)….","grammar:49:ex5:points:1":"見失う→見失わないで (negative request)."},"50":{"example:50:exzh":"I have a book.","example:50:exzh2":"He has a bag.","example:50:exzh3":"She has a child.","example:50:exzh4":"What do you have?","example:50:exzh5":"We have hope.","grammar:50:ex:trans":"I have a book.","grammar:50:ex:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:50:ex:explain":"This sentence shows how 「〜ている」 expresses a state. The verb 「持つ」 ends in 「つ」, so its te-form is 「持って」 (a geminate sound change); adding 「いる」 gives 「持っている／持っています」. Here 「〜ている」 does not mean an action in progress — it expresses the continuing state of owning, so 「本を持っています」 means 'have a book'. 「を」 marks what is owned. Watch out for verbs like 「持つ・知る・住む」, which often use 「ている」 to express a state.","grammar:50:ex:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:50:ex:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:50:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:50:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:50:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex:words:2:zh":"book","grammar:50:ex:words:2:note":"ほん","grammar:50:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:50:ex:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:50:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex:words:4:zh":"own, have","grammar:50:ex:words:4:note":"もっています","grammar:50:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:50:ex:points:0":"❗持つ（もつ）: to hold, to have; 〜ている expresses the state of owning.","grammar:50:ex:points:1":"本を持っている: to have a book.","grammar:50:ex2:trans":"He has a bag.","grammar:50:ex2:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:50:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:50:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:50:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:50:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:50:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex2:words:2:zh":"bag","grammar:50:ex2:words:2:note":"loanword","grammar:50:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:50:ex2:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:50:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex2:words:4:zh":"own, have","grammar:50:ex2:words:4:note":"もっています","grammar:50:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:50:ex2:points:0":"バッグを持つ: to carry / have a bag.","grammar:50:ex2:points:1":"〜ている: a state.","grammar:50:ex3:trans":"She has a child.","grammar:50:ex3:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:50:ex3:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:50:ex3:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:50:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:50:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:50:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex3:words:2:zh":"child","grammar:50:ex3:words:2:note":"こども","grammar:50:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:50:ex3:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:50:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex3:words:4:zh":"own, have","grammar:50:ex3:words:4:note":"もっています","grammar:50:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:50:ex3:points:0":"❗「子供を持つ」 = to have a child (people also often say 子供がいる).","grammar:50:ex3:points:1":"持っている: to own, to have.","grammar:50:ex4:trans":"What do you have?","grammar:50:ex4:structure":"何を持っていますか","grammar:50:ex4:words:0:zh":"you","grammar:50:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:50:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:50:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex4:words:2:zh":"what","grammar:50:ex4:words:2:note":"なに","grammar:50:ex4:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:50:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:50:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex4:words:4:zh":"own, have","grammar:50:ex4:words:4:note":"もっています","grammar:50:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:50:ex4:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:50:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex4:points:0":"何を持っている: what one has.","grammar:50:ex4:points:1":"あなたは: you (topic).","grammar:50:ex5:trans":"We have hope.","grammar:50:ex5:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:50:ex5:words:0:zh":"we","grammar:50:ex5:words:0:note":"わたしたち","grammar:50:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:50:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:50:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex5:words:2:zh":"hope","grammar:50:ex5:words:2:note":"きぼう","grammar:50:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:50:ex5:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:50:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:50:ex5:words:4:zh":"own, have","grammar:50:ex5:words:4:note":"もっています","grammar:50:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:50:ex5:points:0":"❗希望を持つ: to hold hope (abstract usage).","grammar:50:ex5:points:1":"希望: hope.","exam:50:zh":"This bag is heavy when I hold it in my hand, so I carry it on my shoulder.","exam:50:why":"「手で持つ」 means holding something in your hand. 「着る」 is used for wearing clothes and cannot mean carrying a bag by hand."},"51":{"example:51:exzh":"A year has twelve months.","example:51:exzh2":"There's one student in the classroom.","example:51:exzh3":"He's the best at it.","example:51:exzh4":"A day has twenty-four hours.","example:51:exzh5":"Let's go together at one o'clock tomorrow.","grammar:51:ex:trans":"A year has twelve months.","grammar:51:ex:structure":"一年 + は + 十二か月 + です","grammar:51:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「一年」 to show how 「一」 is read before counting and time nouns. To say a year has twelve months in Japanese, you can use the basic explanatory sentence 「一年は十二か月です」. Here 「か月」 is the counter for months.","grammar:51:ex:words:0:zh":"one year","grammar:51:ex:words:0:note":"いちねん; refers to the span of one whole year","grammar:51:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex:words:1:zh":"marks the topic","grammar:51:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex:words:2:zh":"twelve months","grammar:51:ex:words:2:note":"じゅうにかげつ; the number of months","grammar:51:ex:words:2:pos":"numeral with counter","grammar:51:ex:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:51:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:51:ex:points:0":"The 「一」 in 「一年」 is read 「いち」; before a time noun it expresses one complete unit.","grammar:51:ex:points:1":"「は」 marks the topic, showing that what follows is a statement about the time unit \"one year\".","grammar:51:ex:points:2":"「十二か月です」 states the number of months with a numeral plus its counter and 「です」.","grammar:51:ex2:trans":"There is one student in the classroom.","grammar:51:ex2:structure":"〜に〜がいます","grammar:51:ex2:words:0:zh":"classroom","grammar:51:ex2:words:0:note":"きょうしつ","grammar:51:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex2:words:1:zh":"(location of existence)","grammar:51:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex2:words:2:zh":"one person","grammar:51:ex2:words:2:note":"ひとり","grammar:51:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:51:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex2:words:4:zh":"student","grammar:51:ex2:words:4:note":"がくせい","grammar:51:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex2:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:51:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex2:words:6:zh":"there is (a person)","grammar:51:ex2:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:51:ex2:points:0":"一人 (ひとり): one person.","grammar:51:ex2:points:1":"に＋がいます: (a person) is / there is (います is used for living things).","grammar:51:ex3:trans":"He's the best.","grammar:51:ex3:structure":"〜は一番〜です","grammar:51:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:51:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:51:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:51:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:51:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex3:words:2:zh":"the most","grammar:51:ex3:words:2:note":"いちばん","grammar:51:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:51:ex3:words:3:zh":"good at / skilled","grammar:51:ex3:words:3:note":"じょうず","grammar:51:ex3:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:51:ex3:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:51:ex3:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:51:ex3:points:0":"一番: the most… (superlative).","grammar:51:ex3:points:1":"上手 (じょうず): skilled / good at (na-adjective).","grammar:51:ex4:trans":"A day has twenty-four hours.","grammar:51:ex4:structure":"〜が〜です","grammar:51:ex4:words:0:zh":"one day","grammar:51:ex4:words:0:note":"いちにち","grammar:51:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex4:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:51:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex4:words:2:zh":"twenty-four","grammar:51:ex4:words:2:note":"にじゅうよん","grammar:51:ex4:words:2:pos":"numeral","grammar:51:ex4:words:3:zh":"hours","grammar:51:ex4:words:3:note":"じかん","grammar:51:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex4:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:51:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:51:ex4:points:0":"一日 (いちにち): one day.","grammar:51:ex4:points:1":"二十四時間: twenty-four hours (時間 means \"…hours\").","grammar:51:ex5:trans":"Let's go together at one o'clock tomorrow.","grammar:51:ex5:structure":"明日は〜時に一緒に行きましょう","grammar:51:ex5:explain":"「明日は」 brings tomorrow up as the topic, and 「一時に」 specifies the time you leave. 「時」 follows a number to mean \"o'clock\" and is read 「じ」, unlike 「とき」, which means \"time/when\". 「行きましょう」 is the polite suggestion form, and 「一緒に」 makes it an invitation to go together.","grammar:51:ex5:words:0:zh":"tomorrow","grammar:51:ex5:words:0:note":"あした","grammar:51:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex5:words:1:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:51:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex5:words:2:zh":"one","grammar:51:ex5:words:2:note":"いち","grammar:51:ex5:words:2:pos":"numeral","grammar:51:ex5:words:3:zh":"o'clock","grammar:51:ex5:words:3:note":"じ","grammar:51:ex5:words:3:pos":"suffix","grammar:51:ex5:words:4:zh":"(time when an action happens)","grammar:51:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex5:words:5:zh":"together","grammar:51:ex5:words:5:note":"いっしょ","grammar:51:ex5:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:51:ex5:words:6:zh":"(expresses doing something together)","grammar:51:ex5:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:51:ex5:words:7:zh":"go","grammar:51:ex5:words:7:note":"いき","grammar:51:ex5:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:51:ex5:words:8:zh":"(polite invitation / suggestion)","grammar:51:ex5:words:8:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:51:ex5:points:0":"「一時」 means one o'clock and is read 「いちじ」; a specific time is marked by 「に」.","grammar:51:ex5:points:1":"「一緒に」 is the common set phrase for doing something together.","grammar:51:ex5:points:2":"Here 「〜ましょう」 expresses an invitation, like \"let's…\".","exam:51:zh":"There were three apples, and two of them were eaten, so one is left.","exam:51:why":"Three minus two leaves one, so the answer is 「一」, giving 「一つ（ひとつ）」. 「二つ」 wouldn't match the number given earlier."},"53":{"example:53:exzh":"This is a true story.","example:53:exzh2":"He's a true friend.","example:53:exzh3":"I want to tell you how I really feel.","example:53:exzh4":"What's the real meaning?","example:53:exzh5":"I think that's true.","grammar:53:ex:trans":"This is a true story.","grammar:53:ex:structure":"〜は本当の〜です","grammar:53:ex:explain":"This sentence shows a noun modifying another noun with 「の」. 「本当」 is a noun, so to modify the noun after it you need 「の」, giving 「本当の話」 (a true story, the truth). This differs from how adjectives modify nouns, so don't mistakenly add な or い. 「これは⋯です」 is the noun-judgment frame, and 「は」 marks the topic. The whole sentence stresses \"this really happened, it isn't made up\", and 「本当の」 is often used in conversation to vouch that something is true.","grammar:53:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:53:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:53:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:53:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex:words:2:zh":"really","grammar:53:ex:words:2:note":"ほんとう","grammar:53:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:53:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex:words:4:zh":"story / talk","grammar:53:ex:words:4:note":"はなし","grammar:53:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:53:ex:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:53:ex:points:0":"本当の＋noun: a true… (本当 takes の to modify a noun).","grammar:53:ex:points:1":"話 (はなし): story / topic.","grammar:53:ex2:trans":"He's a true friend.","grammar:53:ex2:structure":"〜は本当の〜です","grammar:53:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:53:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:53:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:53:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:53:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex2:words:2:zh":"really","grammar:53:ex2:words:2:note":"ほんとう","grammar:53:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:53:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex2:words:4:zh":"friend","grammar:53:ex2:words:4:note":"ともだち","grammar:53:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex2:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:53:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:53:ex2:points:0":"本当の友達: a true friend.","grammar:53:ex2:points:1":"の links 本当 to the noun.","grammar:53:ex3:trans":"I want to convey my true feelings.","grammar:53:ex3:structure":"〜を伝えたい","grammar:53:ex3:words:0:zh":"really","grammar:53:ex3:words:0:note":"ほんとう","grammar:53:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:53:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex3:words:2:zh":"feelings","grammar:53:ex3:words:2:note":"きもち","grammar:53:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex3:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:53:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex3:words:4:zh":"want to convey","grammar:53:ex3:words:4:note":"つたえたい","grammar:53:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:53:ex3:points:0":"本当の気持ち: true feelings.","grammar:53:ex3:points:1":"伝える→伝えたい (〜たい expresses desire).","grammar:53:ex4:trans":"What is the real meaning?","grammar:53:ex4:structure":"〜は何ですか","grammar:53:ex4:words:0:zh":"really","grammar:53:ex4:words:0:note":"ほんとう","grammar:53:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex4:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:53:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex4:words:2:zh":"meaning","grammar:53:ex4:words:2:note":"いみ","grammar:53:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex4:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:53:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex4:words:4:zh":"what","grammar:53:ex4:words:4:note":"なに","grammar:53:ex4:words:4:pos":"question word","grammar:53:ex4:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:53:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:53:ex4:words:6:zh":"(question)","grammar:53:ex4:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex4:points:0":"本当の意味: the real meaning.","grammar:53:ex4:points:1":"何ですか: asks what something is.","grammar:53:ex5:trans":"I think that's true.","grammar:53:ex5:structure":"〜だと思います","grammar:53:ex5:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:53:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:53:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:53:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex5:words:2:zh":"really","grammar:53:ex5:words:2:note":"ほんとう","grammar:53:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex5:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:53:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex5:words:4:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:53:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:53:ex5:words:5:zh":"is (plain form)","grammar:53:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:53:ex5:words:6:zh":"(quotation)","grammar:53:ex5:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:53:ex5:words:7:zh":"thinks","grammar:53:ex5:words:7:note":"おもいます","grammar:53:ex5:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:53:ex5:points:0":"〜と思います: I think that… (と quotes the thought).","grammar:53:ex5:points:1":"noun＋だ＋と思う: to think that something is….","exam:53:zh":"This story is not a lie; it is a true story.","exam:53:why":"「本当」 means true and echoes 「うそではなく」. 「丈夫」 means sturdy or durable and cannot be used to judge whether something is true."},"54":{"example:54:exzh":"I haven't finished my homework yet.","example:54:exzh2":"She hasn't come yet.","example:54:exzh3":"We haven't eaten yet.","example:54:exzh4":"There's still time.","example:54:exzh5":"I don't want to go to bed yet.","grammar:54:ex:trans":"I haven't finished my homework yet.","grammar:54:ex:structure":"まだ〜ていません","grammar:54:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「まだ〜ていません」 to mean \"not finished yet\". 「まだ」 means \"still / yet\", and with the negative 「〜ていません」 it stresses that a state has not been reached — \"not done yet\". The verb 「終わる」 is a godan (u-) verb; its te-form 「終わって」 plus 「いません」 gives 「宿題が終わっていません」, \"the homework isn't finished yet\". 「が」 marks the subject. Note that 「終わりません」 doesn't work here, because that means it will not end in the future — a completely different nuance.","grammar:54:ex:words:0:zh":"still / yet","grammar:54:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:54:ex:words:1:zh":"homework","grammar:54:ex:words:1:note":"しゅくだい","grammar:54:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:54:ex:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:54:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:54:ex:words:3:zh":"not finished yet","grammar:54:ex:words:3:note":"おわっていません","grammar:54:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:54:ex:points:0":"まだ〜ていません: hasn't (been) done yet (the state is not yet complete).","grammar:54:ex:points:1":"終わる→終わって＋いません。","grammar:54:ex2:trans":"She hasn't come yet.","grammar:54:ex2:structure":"まだ〜ていません","grammar:54:ex2:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:54:ex2:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:54:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:54:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:54:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:54:ex2:words:2:zh":"still / yet","grammar:54:ex2:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:54:ex2:words:3:zh":"hasn't come yet","grammar:54:ex2:words:3:note":"きていません","grammar:54:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:54:ex2:points:0":"まだ来ていません: hasn't come yet.","grammar:54:ex2:points:1":"来る→来て＋いません。","grammar:54:ex3:trans":"We haven't eaten yet.","grammar:54:ex3:structure":"まだ〜ていない","grammar:54:ex3:words:0:zh":"we","grammar:54:ex3:words:0:note":"わたしたち","grammar:54:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:54:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:54:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:54:ex3:words:2:zh":"still / yet","grammar:54:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:54:ex3:words:3:zh":"haven't eaten yet","grammar:54:ex3:words:3:note":"たべていない","grammar:54:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:54:ex3:points:0":"まだ〜ていない: hasn't (done) yet (plain form).","grammar:54:ex3:points:1":"食べる→食べて＋いない。","grammar:54:ex4:trans":"There's still time.","grammar:54:ex4:structure":"まだ〜がある","grammar:54:ex4:words:0:zh":"still / yet","grammar:54:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:54:ex4:words:1:zh":"time","grammar:54:ex4:words:1:note":"じかん","grammar:54:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:54:ex4:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:54:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:54:ex4:words:3:zh":"there is / are","grammar:54:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:54:ex4:points:0":"まだ〜がある: there is still… (something remains).","grammar:54:ex4:points:1":"時間がある: there is time.","grammar:54:ex5:trans":"I don't want to sleep yet.","grammar:54:ex5:structure":"まだ〜たくないです","grammar:54:ex5:words:0:zh":"still / yet","grammar:54:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:54:ex5:words:1:zh":"don't want to sleep","grammar:54:ex5:words:1:note":"ねたくない","grammar:54:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:54:ex5:words:2:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:54:ex5:words:2:pos":"copula","grammar:54:ex5:points:0":"〜たくない: don't want to (do)… (the negative of たい).","grammar:54:ex5:points:1":"寝る→寝たい→寝たくない。","exam:54:zh":"I'm doing my homework right now, and I haven't finished it yet.","exam:54:why":"「まだ〜ていません」 means something isn't finished yet. 「もう」 usually means already, which doesn't fit this situation of still working on something that isn't done."},"55":{"example:55:exzh":"That's not true.","example:55:exzh2":"It's not that expensive.","example:55:exzh3":"I've never thought about anything like that.","example:55:exzh4":"Don't say it like that.","example:55:exzh5":"It's not that hard.","grammar:55:ex:trans":"That's not the case.","grammar:55:ex:structure":"そんなことはありません","grammar:55:ex:explain":"「そんなことはありません」 is a very common negative idiom in conversation, used to deny what the other person said or to respond modestly to praise — roughly \"no such thing\" or \"not at all\". 「そんな」 is a pre-noun adjectival, so it can only attach to a noun and means \"that kind of\"; 「そんなこと」 = \"that kind of thing\". 「は」 marks the topic, and 「ありません」 is the polite negative of 「ある」. The whole sentence sounds gentle and indirect, making it a handy buffer phrase in social situations.","grammar:55:ex:words:0:zh":"such","grammar:55:ex:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:55:ex:words:1:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:55:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:55:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:55:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:55:ex:words:3:zh":"don't have","grammar:55:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:55:ex:points:0":"そんなことはありません: no such thing / not at all (a common negative response).","grammar:55:ex:points:1":"そんな: that kind of (pre-noun adjectival; attaches only to nouns).","grammar:55:ex2:trans":"It's not that expensive.","grammar:55:ex2:structure":"そんなに〜くない","grammar:55:ex2:words:0:zh":"that much","grammar:55:ex2:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:55:ex2:words:1:zh":"not expensive","grammar:55:ex2:words:1:note":"たかくない","grammar:55:ex2:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:55:ex2:words:2:zh":"(tone)","grammar:55:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:55:ex2:points:0":"そんなに〜ない: not that… (negating degree).","grammar:55:ex2:points:1":"高い→高くない (negative of an i-adjective).","grammar:55:ex3:trans":"I've never thought of such a thing.","grammar:55:ex3:structure":"〜たことがない","grammar:55:ex3:words:0:zh":"such","grammar:55:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:55:ex3:words:1:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:55:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:55:ex3:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:55:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:55:ex3:words:3:zh":"thought of","grammar:55:ex3:words:3:note":"かんがえた","grammar:55:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:55:ex3:words:4:zh":"(experience)","grammar:55:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:55:ex3:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:55:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:55:ex3:words:6:zh":"don't have","grammar:55:ex3:words:6:pos":"adjective","grammar:55:ex3:points:0":"〜たことがない: have never (done)… (experience).","grammar:55:ex3:points:1":"が marks the non-existence of the \"experience\" (こと).","grammar:55:ex4:trans":"Don't say that.","grammar:55:ex4:structure":"そんな風に〜ないで","grammar:55:ex4:words:0:zh":"such","grammar:55:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:55:ex4:words:1:zh":"in that way","grammar:55:ex4:words:1:note":"ふうに","grammar:55:ex4:words:1:pos":"adverb","grammar:55:ex4:words:2:zh":"don't say","grammar:55:ex4:words:2:note":"いわないで","grammar:55:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:55:ex4:points:0":"そんな風に: in that way (風に = in the manner of…).","grammar:55:ex4:points:1":"〜ないで: please don't….","grammar:55:ex5:trans":"It's not that difficult.","grammar:55:ex5:structure":"そんなに〜くない","grammar:55:ex5:words:0:zh":"that much","grammar:55:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:55:ex5:words:1:zh":"not difficult","grammar:55:ex5:words:1:note":"むずかしくない","grammar:55:ex5:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:55:ex5:points:0":"そんなに〜ない: not that….","grammar:55:ex5:points:1":"難しい→難しくない。"},"56":{"example:56:exzh":"This is a Japanese-style dish.","example:56:exzh2":"He has a scientific way of thinking.","example:56:exzh3":"She has a cultural background.","example:56:exzh4":"This book has historical value.","example:56:exzh5":"This is a natural phenomenon."},"58":{"example:58:exzh":"We're going home.","example:58:exzh2":"He went back to work.","example:58:exzh3":"She went back to where she was.","example:58:exzh4":"It's time to go back to school.","example:58:exzh5":"I'll be right back.","grammar:58:ex:trans":"We're going home.","grammar:58:ex:structure":"〜に戻ります","grammar:58:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the intransitive verb 「戻る」 with 「に」. 「戻る（もどる）」 means 'to return, to go back to where you were' and is an intransitive verb, so the action has no object; the place you return to is marked with 「に」, as in 「家に戻る」 = 'to return home'. Its nuance differs slightly from 「帰る」: 「帰る」 leans toward returning to where you belong (home, your hometown), while 「戻る」 leans toward going back to a place you were at or started from. The polite form is 「戻ります」. 「は」 marks 「私たち」 as the topic.","grammar:58:ex:words:0:zh":"we","grammar:58:ex:words:0:note":"わたしたち","grammar:58:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:58:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:58:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex:words:2:zh":"house","grammar:58:ex:words:2:note":"いえ","grammar:58:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex:words:3:zh":"(destination)","grammar:58:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex:words:4:zh":"return","grammar:58:ex:words:4:note":"もどります","grammar:58:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:58:ex:points:0":"❗戻る（もどる）: to return, to go back (intransitive verb).","grammar:58:ex:points:1":"〜に戻る: to return to ...","grammar:58:ex2:trans":"He got back to work.","grammar:58:ex2:structure":"〜に戻った","grammar:58:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:58:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:58:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:58:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:58:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex2:words:2:zh":"work","grammar:58:ex2:words:2:note":"しごと","grammar:58:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex2:words:3:zh":"(destination)","grammar:58:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex2:words:4:zh":"went home","grammar:58:ex2:words:4:note":"もどった","grammar:58:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:58:ex2:points:0":"仕事に戻る: to get back to work.","grammar:58:ex2:points:1":"戻る→戻った。","grammar:58:ex3:trans":"She went back to the original spot.","grammar:58:ex3:structure":"元の〜に戻った","grammar:58:ex3:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:58:ex3:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:58:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:58:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:58:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex3:words:2:zh":"original","grammar:58:ex3:words:2:note":"もと","grammar:58:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex3:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:58:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex3:words:4:zh":"location","grammar:58:ex3:words:4:note":"ばしょ","grammar:58:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex3:words:5:zh":"(destination)","grammar:58:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex3:words:6:zh":"went home","grammar:58:ex3:words:6:note":"もどった","grammar:58:ex3:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:58:ex3:points:0":"❗元の場所: the original place.","grammar:58:ex3:points:1":"元の〜に戻る: to return to the original ...","grammar:58:ex4:trans":"It's time to go back to school.","grammar:58:ex4:structure":"〜に戻る時間です","grammar:58:ex4:words:0:zh":"school","grammar:58:ex4:words:0:note":"がっこう","grammar:58:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex4:words:1:zh":"(destination)","grammar:58:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:58:ex4:words:2:zh":"return","grammar:58:ex4:words:2:note":"もどる","grammar:58:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:58:ex4:words:3:zh":"time","grammar:58:ex4:words:3:note":"じかん","grammar:58:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:58:ex4:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:58:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:58:ex4:points:0":"戻る時間: time to go back (modifies a noun).","grammar:58:ex4:points:1":"〜時間です: it's time to …","grammar:58:ex5:trans":"I'll be right back.","grammar:58:ex5:structure":"すぐに戻ります","grammar:58:ex5:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:58:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:58:ex5:words:1:zh":"come back","grammar:58:ex5:words:1:note":"もどります","grammar:58:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:58:ex5:points:0":"すぐに戻る: to be right back.","grammar:58:ex5:points:1":"戻る→戻ります。"},"60":{"example:60:exzh":"Please wait a moment.","example:60:exzh2":"I'm a bit tired.","example:60:exzh3":"Please let me have a quick look at this.","example:60:exzh4":"I'll just give it a quick try.","example:60:exzh5":"Come just a little earlier.","grammar:60:ex:trans":"Please wait a moment.","grammar:60:ex:structure":"ちょっと〜てください","grammar:60:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「ちょっと＋〜てください」 to make a polite request. 「ちょっと」 literally means \"a little / briefly\", but its real job is to soften the tone so the request doesn't sound harsh. The te-form of the verb 「待つ」 is 「待って」 (with the small っ sound change), and adding 「ください」 makes the polite request \"please wait\". The whole sentence 「ちょっと待ってください」 = \"please wait a moment\" — an extremely common everyday phrase, where 「ちょっと」 keeps the command feeling as mild as possible.","grammar:60:ex:words:0:zh":"a little","grammar:60:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex:words:1:zh":"wait","grammar:60:ex:words:1:note":"まって","grammar:60:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:60:ex:words:2:zh":"please","grammar:60:ex:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:60:ex:points:0":"ちょっと: a little / just a moment (softens the tone).","grammar:60:ex:points:1":"待つ→待って＋ください。","grammar:60:ex2:trans":"I'm a little tired.","grammar:60:ex2:structure":"ちょっと〜ました","grammar:60:ex2:words:0:zh":"a little","grammar:60:ex2:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex2:words:1:zh":"tired","grammar:60:ex2:words:1:note":"つかれました","grammar:60:ex2:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:60:ex2:points:0":"ちょっと: a little (degree).","grammar:60:ex2:points:1":"疲れる→疲れました (past state change).","grammar:60:ex3:trans":"Please let me have a quick look at this.","grammar:60:ex3:structure":"〜をちょっと見せてください","grammar:60:ex3:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:60:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:60:ex3:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:60:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:60:ex3:words:2:zh":"a quick look","grammar:60:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex3:words:3:zh":"show (someone)","grammar:60:ex3:words:3:note":"みせて","grammar:60:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:60:ex3:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:60:ex3:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:60:ex3:points:0":"見せる: to show (someone) (≠見る, to look yourself).","grammar:60:ex3:points:1":"ちょっと: softens the request.","grammar:60:ex4:trans":"I'll just try it a little.","grammar:60:ex4:structure":"ちょっとだけ〜てみます","grammar:60:ex4:words:0:zh":"just a little bit","grammar:60:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex4:words:1:zh":"only","grammar:60:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:60:ex4:words:2:zh":"try","grammar:60:ex4:words:2:note":"ためして","grammar:60:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:60:ex4:words:3:zh":"try it and see","grammar:60:ex4:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:60:ex4:points:0":"ちょっとだけ: just a tiny bit (だけ limits it).","grammar:60:ex4:points:1":"〜てみる: to try doing (something) to see how it goes.","grammar:60:ex5:trans":"Come a little earlier.","grammar:60:ex5:structure":"ちょっとだけ早く来て","grammar:60:ex5:words:0:zh":"just a little bit","grammar:60:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex5:words:1:zh":"only","grammar:60:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:60:ex5:words:2:zh":"early (as an adverb)","grammar:60:ex5:words:2:note":"はやく","grammar:60:ex5:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:60:ex5:words:3:zh":"come","grammar:60:ex5:words:3:note":"きて","grammar:60:ex5:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:60:ex5:points:0":"早く: early (早い→早く, turned into an adverb).","grammar:60:ex5:points:1":"来て: come (te-form, casual request).","exam:60:zh":"I am washing my hands right now, so please wait just a minute.","exam:60:why":"「ちょっと」 can express a short amount of time. 「ずっと」 means continuing for a long time, which does not fit the short wait emphasized by 「一分だけ」."},"63":{"example:63:exzh":"I think that's wrong.","example:63:exzh2":"It's different from what I think.","example:63:exzh3":"It's only the wording that's different.","example:63:exzh4":"He and I have different opinions.","example:63:exzh5":"Is this different from yours?","grammar:63:ex:trans":"I think that's wrong.","grammar:63:ex:structure":"〔plain-form sentence〕＋と思います. The quotation particle 「と」 marks the content of the thought, and 「思います」 follows to express a personal judgment.","grammar:63:ex:explain":"This sentence demonstrates the quotation pattern 「〜と思います」. 「と」 is the quotation particle: it frames the content of the thought, and 「思います」 follows to express that you feel or think something. The key point is that what comes before 「と」 must be in the plain form, so it is 「違うと思います」, not 「違いますと」. The verb 「違う」 here means not right or different. The whole sentence states a disagreement politely—I think that's wrong—and it is a very useful way to soften your opinion in a discussion.","grammar:63:ex:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:63:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:63:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex:words:2:zh":"not right / different","grammar:63:ex:words:2:note":"ちがう; dictionary form (plain)","grammar:63:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex:words:3:zh":"(quotation)","grammar:63:ex:words:3:note":"marks the content of the thought","grammar:63:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex:words:4:zh":"feel / think","grammar:63:ex:words:4:note":"おもいます","grammar:63:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex:points:0":"〜と思います: expresses I feel / I think that…","grammar:63:ex:points:1":"What comes before と takes the plain form: 違うと思います","grammar:63:ex2:trans":"It's different from what I think.","grammar:63:ex2:structure":"noun + と + 違います. 「と」 marks the standard of comparison, meaning from or with …, and 「違う」 means to differ from it.","grammar:63:ex2:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:63:ex2:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:63:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:63:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex2:words:2:zh":"idea","grammar:63:ex2:words:2:note":"かんがえ; the noun form of 考える","grammar:63:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:63:ex2:words:3:zh":"with / from","grammar:63:ex2:words:3:note":"the standard of comparison","grammar:63:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex2:words:4:zh":"differ","grammar:63:ex2:words:4:note":"ちがいます; masu-form","grammar:63:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex2:points:0":"〜と違います: to be different from …","grammar:63:ex2:points:1":"Besides meaning and, と also marks the basis of a comparison","grammar:63:ex3:trans":"It's just that the language is different.","grammar:63:ex3:structure":"noun + が + verb + だけです. 「だけ」 follows a plain-form verb to mean just or only, and です at the end makes it polite.","grammar:63:ex3:words:0:zh":"language / word","grammar:63:ex3:words:0:note":"ことば","grammar:63:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:63:ex3:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:63:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex3:words:2:zh":"differ","grammar:63:ex3:words:2:note":"ちがう; dictionary form","grammar:63:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex3:words:3:zh":"only / just","grammar:63:ex3:words:3:note":"limitation","grammar:63:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex3:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:63:ex3:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:63:ex3:points:0":"〜だけです: just … (limiting)","grammar:63:ex3:points:1":"だけ attaches directly to a plain-form verb: 違うだけ","grammar:63:ex4:trans":"He and I have different opinions.","grammar:63:ex4:structure":"A と B は + noun + が + 違う. 「AとBは」 lines the two up as the topic, and 「が」 points out the respect in which they differ (their opinions).","grammar:63:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:63:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:63:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex4:words:1:zh":"with","grammar:63:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex4:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:63:ex4:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:63:ex4:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex4:words:3:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:63:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex4:words:4:zh":"opinion","grammar:63:ex4:words:4:note":"いけん","grammar:63:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:63:ex4:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:63:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex4:words:6:zh":"differ","grammar:63:ex4:words:6:note":"ちがう; plain form","grammar:63:ex4:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex4:points:0":"big topic は + small subject が: 意見が違う","grammar:63:ex4:points:1":"AとB: lines up two things side by side","grammar:63:ex5:trans":"Is this different from yours?","grammar:63:ex5:structure":"noun + と + 違いますか. 「〜のもの」 means the thing belonging to …, and 「と違いますか」 asks whether it is different.","grammar:63:ex5:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:63:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic marker)","grammar:63:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex5:words:2:zh":"you","grammar:63:ex5:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:63:ex5:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:63:ex5:words:3:note":"Here の stands in for a noun = your thing","grammar:63:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex5:words:4:zh":"things","grammar:63:ex5:words:4:note":"a physical thing","grammar:63:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:63:ex5:words:5:zh":"with","grammar:63:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex5:words:6:zh":"differ","grammar:63:ex5:words:6:note":"ちがいます","grammar:63:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:63:ex5:words:7:zh":"(question)","grammar:63:ex5:words:7:pos":"particle","grammar:63:ex5:points:0":"〜のもの: …'s thing (の + もの)","grammar:63:ex5:points:1":"〜と違いますか: asks whether it is different from …"},"64":{"example:64:exzh":"I'll call you later.","example:64:exzh2":"I'll take a walk after dinner.","example:64:exzh3":"He'll come later.","example:64:exzh4":"Please look at this photo later.","example:64:exzh5":"Let's talk later.","grammar:64:ex:trans":"I'll call later.","grammar:64:ex:structure":"後で〜します","grammar:64:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「後で」 to show the order in time. 「後で」 means 'after a bit, later' and refers to doing something else once one thing is finished. The verb 「電話する」 is a 'noun + する' verb, and its polite form is 「電話します」. The whole sentence 「後で電話します」 means 'I'll call (you) later,' and it's often used to put an action off. Note that 「後で」 is read 「あとで」 — don't mix it up with 「後ろ（うしろ）」, which refers to physical position.","grammar:64:ex:words:0:zh":"later, afterwards","grammar:64:ex:words:0:note":"あとで","grammar:64:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:64:ex:words:1:zh":"make a phone call","grammar:64:ex:words:1:note":"でんわします","grammar:64:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex:points:0":"後で: after (a while), later.","grammar:64:ex:points:1":"電話する→電話します。","grammar:64:ex2:trans":"I'll take a walk after dinner.","grammar:64:ex2:structure":"〜の後に〜します","grammar:64:ex2:words:0:zh":"dinner","grammar:64:ex2:words:0:note":"ばんごはん","grammar:64:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:64:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:64:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex2:words:2:zh":"later, afterwards","grammar:64:ex2:words:2:note":"あと","grammar:64:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:64:ex2:words:3:zh":"(point in time)","grammar:64:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex2:words:4:zh":"take a walk","grammar:64:ex2:words:4:note":"さんぽします","grammar:64:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex2:points:0":"〜の後に: after… (order in time).","grammar:64:ex2:points:1":"散歩する→散歩します。","grammar:64:ex3:trans":"He'll come later.","grammar:64:ex3:structure":"後から〜ます","grammar:64:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:64:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:64:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:64:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:64:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex3:words:2:zh":"later, afterwards","grammar:64:ex3:words:2:note":"あとから","grammar:64:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:64:ex3:words:3:zh":"come","grammar:64:ex3:words:3:note":"きます","grammar:64:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex3:points:0":"後から: afterwards, later (から marks the starting point).","grammar:64:ex3:points:1":"来る→来ます。","grammar:64:ex4:trans":"Please look at this photo later.","grammar:64:ex4:structure":"後で〜を見てください","grammar:64:ex4:explain":"「後で」 says you want the other person to do this later; the 「で」 here is not a tool or a place of action. 「この」 modifies 「写真」, and 「を」 marks the object of looking. 「見てください」 is a polite request meaning 'please look.'","grammar:64:ex4:words:0:zh":"afterwards, later","grammar:64:ex4:words:0:note":"あと","grammar:64:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:64:ex4:words:1:zh":"(indicates a later time)","grammar:64:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex4:words:2:zh":"this","grammar:64:ex4:words:2:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:64:ex4:words:3:zh":"photo","grammar:64:ex4:words:3:note":"しゃしん","grammar:64:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:64:ex4:words:4:zh":"(object)","grammar:64:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex4:words:5:zh":"look","grammar:64:ex4:words:5:note":"み","grammar:64:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex4:words:6:zh":"(connects to a request expression)","grammar:64:ex4:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:64:ex4:words:7:zh":"please","grammar:64:ex4:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex4:points:0":"「後で」 is read 「あとで」 and is a common time expression meaning later or afterwards.","grammar:64:ex4:points:1":"The te-form of 「見る」 is 「見て」; adding 「ください」 means 'please look.'","grammar:64:ex5:trans":"Let's talk later.","grammar:64:ex5:structure":"後で〜ましょう","grammar:64:ex5:words:0:zh":"later, afterwards","grammar:64:ex5:words:0:note":"あとで","grammar:64:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:64:ex5:words:1:zh":"let's talk","grammar:64:ex5:words:1:note":"はなしましょう","grammar:64:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:64:ex5:points:0":"後で: later.","grammar:64:ex5:points:1":"話す→話しましょう: a suggestion.","exam:64:zh":"After I finish dinner, I'll wash the dishes.","exam:64:why":"「食べ終わった後で」 means doing something else after finishing eating. 「前」 means before, which doesn't match the order here of doing the dishes after the meal is finished."},"65":{"example:65:exzh":"Other people besides him.","example:65:exzh2":"Are there other options?","example:65:exzh3":"I want to learn about other countries.","example:65:exzh4":"He chose another road.","example:65:exzh5":"Are other people coming too?","grammar:65:ex:trans":"Other people besides him.","grammar:65:ex:structure":"〜以外の他の人","grammar:65:ex:explain":"This sentence strings together two 「の」. 「〜以外」 means 'except…,' so 「彼以外の」 is 'other than him,' with 「の」 after 「以外」 modifying a noun. Then 「他の人」 links again with 「の」, where 「他の」 means 'other.' The two 「の」 stack up layer by layer and land on 「人」, so the whole noun phrase is 'other people besides him.' This sentence practices how nouns use 「の」 to build layered modification.","grammar:65:ex:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:65:ex:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:65:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:65:ex:words:1:zh":"other than / except","grammar:65:ex:words:1:note":"いがい","grammar:65:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex:words:2:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex:words:3:zh":"other","grammar:65:ex:words:3:note":"ほか","grammar:65:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex:words:4:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex:words:5:zh":"person","grammar:65:ex:words:5:note":"ひと","grammar:65:ex:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex:points:0":"〜以外: except…, other than…","grammar:65:ex:points:1":"他の: other (＋の＋noun).","grammar:65:ex2:trans":"Are there any other options?","grammar:65:ex2:structure":"他の〜がありますか","grammar:65:ex2:words:0:zh":"other","grammar:65:ex2:words:0:note":"ほか","grammar:65:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex2:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex2:words:2:zh":"option","grammar:65:ex2:words:2:note":"せんたくし","grammar:65:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex2:words:3:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:65:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex2:words:4:zh":"there is / are","grammar:65:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:65:ex2:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:65:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex2:points:0":"他の＋noun: other…","grammar:65:ex2:points:1":"〜がありますか: is there…? (existence)","grammar:65:ex3:trans":"I want to learn about other countries.","grammar:65:ex3:structure":"〜について知りたいです","grammar:65:ex3:words:0:zh":"other","grammar:65:ex3:words:0:note":"ほか","grammar:65:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex3:words:2:zh":"country","grammar:65:ex3:words:2:note":"くに","grammar:65:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex3:words:3:zh":"about","grammar:65:ex3:words:3:pos":"set phrase","grammar:65:ex3:words:4:zh":"want to know","grammar:65:ex3:words:4:note":"しりたい","grammar:65:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:65:ex3:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:65:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:65:ex3:points:0":"〜について: about…","grammar:65:ex3:points:1":"知る→知りたい (〜たい expresses desire).","grammar:65:ex4:trans":"He chose another road.","grammar:65:ex4:structure":"他の〜を選んだ","grammar:65:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:65:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:65:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:65:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:65:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex4:words:2:zh":"other","grammar:65:ex4:words:2:note":"ほか","grammar:65:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex4:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex4:words:4:zh":"road","grammar:65:ex4:words:4:note":"どうろ","grammar:65:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex4:words:5:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:65:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex4:words:6:zh":"chose","grammar:65:ex4:words:6:note":"えらんだ","grammar:65:ex4:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:65:ex4:points:0":"他の道路: another road.","grammar:65:ex4:points:1":"選ぶ→選んだ (past plain form).","grammar:65:ex5:trans":"Will other people come too?","grammar:65:ex5:structure":"他の人も〜ますか","grammar:65:ex5:words:0:zh":"other","grammar:65:ex5:words:0:note":"ほか","grammar:65:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex5:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:65:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex5:words:2:zh":"person","grammar:65:ex5:words:2:note":"ひと","grammar:65:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:65:ex5:words:3:zh":"also, too","grammar:65:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex5:words:4:zh":"come","grammar:65:ex5:words:4:note":"きます","grammar:65:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:65:ex5:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:65:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:65:ex5:points:0":"も: also (adds one more).","grammar:65:ex5:points:1":"他の人も: other people too…"},"67":{"example:67:exzh":"Let's go together.","example:67:exzh2":"I hang out with my friends.","example:67:exzh3":"I watched a movie with her.","example:67:exzh4":"I had a meal with my family.","example:67:exzh5":"Let's study together.","grammar:67:ex:trans":"Let's go together.","grammar:67:ex:structure":"一緒に〜ましょう","grammar:67:ex:explain":"This sentence invites someone with 「一緒に〜ましょう」. 「一緒に」 is an adverb meaning 'together' that modifies the action that follows. 「〜ましょう」 is an invitation or suggestion, roughly 'let's…,' used to invite the other person to act with you. The verb 「行く」 becomes 「行きましょう」. The whole sentence 「一緒に行きましょう」 means 'Let's go together' — the most natural way to invite a friend or colleague along, friendly without being rude.","grammar:67:ex:words:0:zh":"together","grammar:67:ex:words:0:note":"いっしょに","grammar:67:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:67:ex:words:1:zh":"let's go","grammar:67:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:67:ex:points:0":"一緒に: together (adverb).","grammar:67:ex:points:1":"〜ましょう: a suggestion.","grammar:67:ex2:trans":"I hang out with my friends.","grammar:67:ex2:structure":"〜と一緒に〜ます","grammar:67:ex2:words:0:zh":"friend","grammar:67:ex2:words:0:note":"ともだち","grammar:67:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:67:ex2:words:1:zh":"with","grammar:67:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:67:ex2:words:2:zh":"together","grammar:67:ex2:words:2:note":"いっしょに","grammar:67:ex2:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:67:ex2:words:3:zh":"hang out","grammar:67:ex2:words:3:note":"あそびます","grammar:67:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:67:ex2:points:0":"〜と一緒に: together with… (と marks the counterpart).","grammar:67:ex2:points:1":"遊ぶ→遊びます。","grammar:67:ex3:trans":"I watched a movie with her.","grammar:67:ex3:structure":"〜と一緒に〜を〜ました","grammar:67:ex3:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:67:ex3:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:67:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:67:ex3:words:1:zh":"with","grammar:67:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:67:ex3:words:2:zh":"together","grammar:67:ex3:words:2:note":"いっしょに","grammar:67:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:67:ex3:words:3:zh":"movie","grammar:67:ex3:words:3:note":"えいが","grammar:67:ex3:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:67:ex3:words:4:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:67:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:67:ex3:words:5:zh":"watched","grammar:67:ex3:words:5:note":"みました","grammar:67:ex3:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:67:ex3:points:0":"〜と一緒に: together with…","grammar:67:ex3:points:1":"見る→見ました (past).","grammar:67:ex4:trans":"I had a meal with my family.","grammar:67:ex4:structure":"〜と一緒に〜をしました","grammar:67:ex4:words:0:zh":"family","grammar:67:ex4:words:0:note":"かぞく","grammar:67:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:67:ex4:words:1:zh":"with","grammar:67:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:67:ex4:words:2:zh":"together","grammar:67:ex4:words:2:note":"いっしょに","grammar:67:ex4:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:67:ex4:words:3:zh":"have a meal","grammar:67:ex4:words:3:note":"しょくじ","grammar:67:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:67:ex4:words:4:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:67:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:67:ex4:words:5:zh":"did","grammar:67:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:67:ex4:points:0":"食事をする: to have a meal (noun＋を＋する).","grammar:67:ex4:points:1":"〜と一緒に: together with…","grammar:67:ex5:trans":"Let's study together.","grammar:67:ex5:structure":"一緒に〜しよう","grammar:67:ex5:words:0:zh":"together","grammar:67:ex5:words:0:note":"いっしょに","grammar:67:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:67:ex5:words:1:zh":"let's study","grammar:67:ex5:words:1:note":"べんきょうしよう","grammar:67:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:67:ex5:points:0":"〜しよう: volitional form, 'let's do…' (the plain form of ましょう).","grammar:67:ex5:points:1":"勉強する→勉強しよう。","exam:67:zh":"Let's not go separately; let's go to the station together, just the two of us.","exam:67:why":"「一緒に」 means doing something together, which matches 「別々に行かず」. 「先に」 means going first and does not express the two of them going together."},"68":{"example:68:exzh":"I'll make a phone call.","example:68:exzh2":"He's on the phone.","example:68:exzh3":"What's your phone number?","example:68:exzh4":"The phone is ringing.","example:68:exzh5":"Please answer the phone.","grammar:68:ex:trans":"I make a phone call.","grammar:68:ex:structure":"電話をかけます","grammar:68:ex:explain":"This sentence shows a fixed verb–object pairing. 「電話をかける」 is the standard way to say 'make a phone call,' and the verb is fixed as 「かける」 (to hang, to dial) — not する or any other verb. 「を」 marks 「電話」 as the object. The verb 「かける」 is an ichidan (ru-) verb, so its polite form drops る and adds ます, giving 「かけます」. The whole sentence 「電話をかけます」 means '(I) make a phone call.' Pairings of a noun with a specific verb like this should be memorized as a set so you don't pick the wrong verb.","grammar:68:ex:words:0:zh":"phone call","grammar:68:ex:words:0:note":"でんわ","grammar:68:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:68:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:68:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex:words:2:zh":"make (a call)","grammar:68:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:68:ex:points:0":"電話をかける: to make a phone call (fixed pairing, using かける).","grammar:68:ex:points:1":"かける→かけます。","grammar:68:ex2:trans":"He's on the phone.","grammar:68:ex2:structure":"〜をしています","grammar:68:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:68:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:68:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:68:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:68:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex2:words:2:zh":"phone call","grammar:68:ex2:words:2:note":"でんわ","grammar:68:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:68:ex2:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:68:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex2:words:4:zh":"is doing","grammar:68:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:68:ex2:points:0":"電話をする: to make a phone call (= 電話する).","grammar:68:ex2:points:1":"〜ている: ongoing action.","grammar:68:ex3:trans":"What's your phone number?","grammar:68:ex3:structure":"〜は何ですか","grammar:68:ex3:words:0:zh":"phone number","grammar:68:ex3:words:0:note":"でんわばんごう","grammar:68:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:68:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:68:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex3:words:2:zh":"what","grammar:68:ex3:words:2:note":"なに","grammar:68:ex3:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:68:ex3:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:68:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:68:ex3:words:4:zh":"(question)","grammar:68:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex3:points:0":"電話番号: phone number.","grammar:68:ex3:points:1":"何ですか: asks what something is.","grammar:68:ex4:trans":"The phone is ringing.","grammar:68:ex4:structure":"〜が鳴っています","grammar:68:ex4:words:0:zh":"phone call","grammar:68:ex4:words:0:note":"でんわ","grammar:68:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:68:ex4:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:68:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex4:words:2:zh":"is ringing","grammar:68:ex4:words:2:note":"なっています","grammar:68:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:68:ex4:points:0":"❓Why が? When describing a phenomenon (the phone ringing), the subject takes が.","grammar:68:ex4:points:1":"鳴る: (intransitive verb) to ring; 〜ている shows it's ongoing.","grammar:68:ex5:trans":"Please answer the phone.","grammar:68:ex5:structure":"電話に出てください","grammar:68:ex5:explain":"「出る」 usually means 'to go out,' but in the pairing 「電話に出る」 it means to answer the phone. 「に」 marks what you are responding to, so don't change it to 「電話を出る」. 「出てください」 asks the other person to answer the phone.","grammar:68:ex5:words:0:zh":"phone call","grammar:68:ex5:words:0:note":"でんわ","grammar:68:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:68:ex5:words:1:zh":"(what you respond to)","grammar:68:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex5:words:2:zh":"answer (the phone)","grammar:68:ex5:words:2:note":"で","grammar:68:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:68:ex5:words:3:zh":"(connects to a request expression)","grammar:68:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:68:ex5:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:68:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:68:ex5:points:0":"「電話に出る」 is the fixed expression for answering the phone, using the particle 「に」.","grammar:68:ex5:points:1":"The te-form of 「出る」 is 「出て」; adding 「ください」 makes a request.","exam:68:zh":"I wanted to hear my mother's voice since she lives far away, so I gave her a call.","exam:68:why":"Making a phone call is 「電話をかける」, which also fits the purpose of wanting to hear the other person's voice. 「手紙」 goes with 「書く」 or 「送る」; you can't say 「手紙をかける」."},"69":{"example:69:exzh":"He is a man.","example:69:exzh2":"A boy is playing.","example:69:exzh3":"That man is kind.","example:69:exzh4":"Men are said to be strong.","example:69:exzh5":"He grew into a fine man.","grammar:69:ex:trans":"He's a man.","grammar:69:ex:structure":"〜は男です","grammar:69:ex:explain":"This is the noun-predicate sentence 「彼は男です」. 「男」 is a noun meaning 'man, male.' 「は」 makes 「彼」 the subject, and the predicate 「男です」 uses 「です」 for a polite statement. The whole sentence states 'he is a man.' Note that 「男」 on its own sounds blunt; in formal or polite settings people often say 「男性」. Likewise 「女」 corresponds to 「女性」 — pick the register to match the situation.","grammar:69:ex:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:69:ex:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:69:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:69:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:69:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex:words:2:zh":"man","grammar:69:ex:words:2:note":"おとこ","grammar:69:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:69:ex:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:69:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:69:ex:points:0":"男: man / male.","grammar:69:ex:points:1":"noun＋です.","grammar:69:ex2:trans":"A boy is playing.","grammar:69:ex2:structure":"〜が遊んでいる","grammar:69:ex2:words:0:zh":"boy","grammar:69:ex2:words:0:note":"おとこのこ","grammar:69:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:69:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:69:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex2:words:2:zh":"playing","grammar:69:ex2:words:2:note":"あそんでいる","grammar:69:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:69:ex2:points:0":"男の子: boy (男＋の＋子).","grammar:69:ex2:points:1":"〜ている: ongoing action.","grammar:69:ex3:trans":"That man is kind.","grammar:69:ex3:structure":"その男は〜です","grammar:69:ex3:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:69:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:69:ex3:words:1:zh":"man","grammar:69:ex3:words:1:note":"おとこ","grammar:69:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:69:ex3:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:69:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex3:words:3:zh":"kind","grammar:69:ex3:words:3:note":"しんせつ","grammar:69:ex3:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:69:ex3:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:69:ex3:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:69:ex3:points:0":"親切: kind (na-adjective).","grammar:69:ex3:points:1":"その男: that man.","grammar:69:ex4:trans":"Men are said to be strong.","grammar:69:ex4:structure":"〜と言われている","grammar:69:ex4:words:0:zh":"man","grammar:69:ex4:words:0:note":"おとこ","grammar:69:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:69:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:69:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex4:words:2:zh":"strong","grammar:69:ex4:words:2:note":"つよい","grammar:69:ex4:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:69:ex4:words:3:zh":"(quotation)","grammar:69:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex4:words:4:zh":"is said","grammar:69:ex4:words:4:note":"いわれている (passive form＋ている)","grammar:69:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:69:ex4:points:0":"〜と言われている: it is said that… (passive form＋ている states a general view).","grammar:69:ex4:points:1":"言う→言われる (passive form)→言われている.","grammar:69:ex5:trans":"He grew into a fine man.","grammar:69:ex5:structure":"〜な男に成長した","grammar:69:ex5:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:69:ex5:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:69:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:69:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:69:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex5:words:2:zh":"fine, admirable","grammar:69:ex5:words:2:note":"りっぱ","grammar:69:ex5:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:69:ex5:words:3:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:69:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:69:ex5:words:4:zh":"man","grammar:69:ex5:words:4:note":"おとこ","grammar:69:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:69:ex5:words:5:zh":"(result of the change)","grammar:69:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:69:ex5:words:6:zh":"grew","grammar:69:ex5:words:6:note":"せいちょうした","grammar:69:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:69:ex5:points:0":"立派な: fine / admirable (な＋noun).","grammar:69:ex5:points:1":"〜に成長する: to grow into… (に marks the result).","exam:69:zh":"Both my father and my grandfather are men, not women.","exam:69:why":"「男」 means male, the counterpart of 「女」. 「子供」 means child, so it can't describe the father and grandfather here."},"70":{"example:70:exzh":"I have a good idea.","example:70:exzh2":"Please try to organize your thoughts.","example:70:exzh3":"His ideas are interesting.","example:70:exzh4":"Won't you share your thoughts?","example:70:exzh5":"That idea isn't supported.","grammar:70:ex:trans":"I have a good idea.","grammar:70:ex:structure":"いい考えがあります","grammar:70:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the existence pattern 「〜があります」 to express having an idea. 「考え」 is the noun form of the verb 「考える」 and means 'idea, thought.' In 「いい考え」 the i-adjective modifies the noun directly. 「が」 marks what exists, and 「〜がある」 means 'there is…,' here extended to 'an idea is in my head.' The whole sentence 「いい考えがあります」 means 'I have a good idea,' a common opener when making a suggestion or when something just clicks.","grammar:70:ex:words:0:zh":"good","grammar:70:ex:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:70:ex:words:1:zh":"idea","grammar:70:ex:words:1:note":"かんがえ","grammar:70:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:70:ex:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:70:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex:words:3:zh":"there is / are","grammar:70:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:70:ex:points:0":"考え: idea (the noun form of 考える).","grammar:70:ex:points:1":"〜がある: to have… (an idea).","grammar:70:ex2:trans":"Please organize your thoughts.","grammar:70:ex2:structure":"〜をまとめてみてください","grammar:70:ex2:words:0:zh":"idea","grammar:70:ex2:words:0:note":"かんがえ","grammar:70:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:70:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:70:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex2:words:2:zh":"organize","grammar:70:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:70:ex2:words:3:zh":"try","grammar:70:ex2:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:70:ex2:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:70:ex2:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:70:ex2:points:0":"まとめる: to organize, to put in order.","grammar:70:ex2:points:1":"〜てみてください: please try doing… (and see).","grammar:70:ex3:trans":"His idea is interesting.","grammar:70:ex3:structure":"〜の考えは〜です","grammar:70:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:70:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:70:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:70:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:70:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex3:words:2:zh":"idea","grammar:70:ex3:words:2:note":"かんがえ","grammar:70:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:70:ex3:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:70:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex3:words:4:zh":"interesting","grammar:70:ex3:words:4:note":"おもしろい","grammar:70:ex3:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:70:ex3:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:70:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:70:ex3:points:0":"彼の考え: his idea (の shows possession).","grammar:70:ex3:points:1":"面白いです: polite form of an i-adjective.","grammar:70:ex4:trans":"Would you share your thoughts?","grammar:70:ex4:structure":"〜をしませんか","grammar:70:ex4:words:0:zh":"idea","grammar:70:ex4:words:0:note":"かんがえ","grammar:70:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:70:ex4:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:70:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex4:words:2:zh":"won't you share","grammar:70:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:70:ex4:points:0":"シェアする: to share (loanword＋する).","grammar:70:ex4:points:1":"〜ませんか: a gentle invitation, 'won't you…?'","grammar:70:ex5:trans":"That idea isn't supported.","grammar:70:ex5:structure":"〜は支持されていません","grammar:70:ex5:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:70:ex5:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:70:ex5:words:1:zh":"idea","grammar:70:ex5:words:1:note":"かんがえ","grammar:70:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:70:ex5:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:70:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:70:ex5:words:3:zh":"is not supported","grammar:70:ex5:words:3:note":"しじされていません (passive form, negative)","grammar:70:ex5:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:70:ex5:points:0":"支持される: to be supported (passive form).","grammar:70:ex5:points:1":"〜されていません: has not been… (passive form＋negative ongoing state)."},"72":{"example:72:exzh":"This year is a busy year.","example:72:exzh2":"I haven't decided on next year's plans yet.","example:72:exzh3":"He's the same age as me.","example:72:exzh4":"We travel every summer.","example:72:exzh5":"I want to make this year a special one.","grammar:72:ex:trans":"This year is a busy year.","grammar:72:ex:structure":"〜は〜い年です","grammar:72:ex:explain":"This sentence shows an i-adjective modifying a noun, with a time word as the subject. 「今年」 is a time noun with an irregular reading. 「忙しい」 is an i-adjective that attaches directly to a noun to make 「忙しい年」 ('a busy year'). 「は」 makes 「今年」 the subject, and the predicate 「忙しい年です」 uses 「です」 for a polite statement. The whole sentence means 'this year is a busy year.' The 「AはＢです」 pattern, linking a time with its characteristic, is a common way to comment on something.","grammar:72:ex:words:0:zh":"this year","grammar:72:ex:words:0:note":"ことし","grammar:72:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:72:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex:words:2:zh":"busy","grammar:72:ex:words:2:note":"いそがしい","grammar:72:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:72:ex:words:3:zh":"year","grammar:72:ex:words:3:note":"とし","grammar:72:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:72:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:72:ex:points:0":"今年: this year.","grammar:72:ex:points:1":"忙しい年: a busy year (i-adjective＋noun).","grammar:72:ex2:trans":"Next year's plans haven't been decided yet.","grammar:72:ex2:structure":"〜はまだ決めていません","grammar:72:ex2:explain":"「次の年の予定」 links through two 「の」 to mean 'next year's plans.' 「決める」 means a person makes a decision; the person who decides is left out here, and the plans are brought up as the subject. 「まだ決めていません」 means it hasn't been decided yet — the 「〜ていません」 here stresses that it isn't done, not merely that no one is deciding right now.","grammar:72:ex2:words:0:zh":"next","grammar:72:ex2:words:0:note":"つぎ","grammar:72:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex2:words:1:zh":"(links nouns)","grammar:72:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex2:words:2:zh":"year","grammar:72:ex2:words:2:note":"とし","grammar:72:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex2:words:3:zh":"(connects to a noun, showing a time relation)","grammar:72:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex2:words:4:zh":"plan, schedule","grammar:72:ex2:words:4:note":"よてい","grammar:72:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex2:words:5:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:72:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex2:words:6:zh":"still / yet","grammar:72:ex2:words:6:pos":"adverb","grammar:72:ex2:words:7:zh":"decide","grammar:72:ex2:words:7:note":"きめ","grammar:72:ex2:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:72:ex2:words:8:zh":"(links to the completed-state expression)","grammar:72:ex2:words:8:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex2:words:9:zh":"(shows whether something is done)","grammar:72:ex2:words:9:pos":"verb","grammar:72:ex2:words:10:zh":"(negative form of the polite ending)","grammar:72:ex2:words:10:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:72:ex2:words:11:zh":"(negative)","grammar:72:ex2:words:11:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:72:ex2:points:0":"「まだ〜ていません」 means something hasn't been done up to now.","grammar:72:ex2:points:1":"「決める」 is a transitive verb; here 「予定」, which could be marked with 「を」, is marked with 「は」 instead to make it the subject.","grammar:72:ex2:points:2":"「次の年」 is the year after some reference year, which isn't necessarily next year counted from now.","grammar:72:ex3:trans":"He's the same age as me.","grammar:72:ex3:structure":"人は人と同じ年です","grammar:72:ex3:explain":"「彼は」 brings up the person being described, and 「私と」 marks the one being compared with. 「同じ年」 here means the same age, so the sentence says he and I are the same age. Although 「同じ」 is usually classed as a na-adjective, it normally takes no 「な」 when modifying an ordinary noun — worth remembering.","grammar:72:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:72:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:72:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:72:ex3:words:1:zh":"(introduces the topic)","grammar:72:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex3:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:72:ex3:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:72:ex3:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:72:ex3:words:3:zh":"(the one being compared with)","grammar:72:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex3:words:4:zh":"the same","grammar:72:ex3:words:4:note":"おなじ","grammar:72:ex3:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:72:ex3:words:5:zh":"age","grammar:72:ex3:words:5:note":"とし","grammar:72:ex3:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex3:words:6:zh":"(states it politely)","grammar:72:ex3:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:72:ex3:points:0":"In 「〜と同じ」, 「と」 marks the object of comparison, meaning \"the same as\" a particular person or thing.","grammar:72:ex3:points:1":"「同じ」 normally attaches directly to a noun, so you say 「同じ年」, not 「同じな年」.","grammar:72:ex3:points:2":"Here 「年」 is read 「とし」 and means age.","grammar:72:ex4:trans":"We travel every summer.","grammar:72:ex4:structure":"毎年〜に〜します","grammar:72:ex4:words:0:zh":"every year","grammar:72:ex4:words:0:note":"まいとし","grammar:72:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:72:ex4:words:1:zh":"summer","grammar:72:ex4:words:1:note":"なつ","grammar:72:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex4:words:2:zh":"(point in time)","grammar:72:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex4:words:3:zh":"travel / trip","grammar:72:ex4:words:3:note":"りょこうします","grammar:72:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:72:ex4:points:0":"毎年（まいとし／まいねん）: every year.","grammar:72:ex4:points:1":"夏に: in summer (season ＋ に).","grammar:72:ex5:trans":"I want to make this year a special year.","grammar:72:ex5:structure":"〜を〜にしたい","grammar:72:ex5:words:0:zh":"this year","grammar:72:ex5:words:0:note":"ことし","grammar:72:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:72:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex5:words:2:zh":"special","grammar:72:ex5:words:2:note":"とくべつ","grammar:72:ex5:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:72:ex5:words:3:zh":"(attributive form)","grammar:72:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:72:ex5:words:4:zh":"year","grammar:72:ex5:words:4:note":"とし","grammar:72:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:72:ex5:words:5:zh":"(result of the change)","grammar:72:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:72:ex5:words:6:zh":"want to do","grammar:72:ex5:words:6:note":"〜たい","grammar:72:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:72:ex5:points:0":"〜にする: to turn (something) into … (に marks the resulting state).","grammar:72:ex5:points:1":"特別な年: a special year (な ＋ noun).","exam:72:zh":"The twelve months from January to December add up to one year.","exam:72:why":"Twelve months make one 「年」. 「月」 is a single month and can't express the total length of twelve months."},"73":{"example:73:exzh":"Today is a good day.","example:73:exzh2":"Tomorrow will be a sunny day.","example:73:exzh3":"Sunday is the day I do what I like.","example:73:exzh4":"I study on my days off.","example:73:exzh5":"The memory of that day is precious.","grammar:73:ex:trans":"Today is a good day.","grammar:73:ex:structure":"〜はいい日です","grammar:73:ex:explain":"This sentence has the same pattern as the previous one and practices using an i-adjective to modify a noun. 「日（ひ）」 is a noun meaning a day or a day of the week. 「いい」 is an i-adjective, and it attaches directly to a noun to form 「いい日」 (a good day). 「今日は」 raises today as the topic, and adding 「です」 to the predicate makes the tone polite. The whole sentence 「今日はいい日です」 means \"Today is a good day.\" Note that 「日」 has several readings (ひ／にち／か); here, where it means a day, it is read 「ひ」.","grammar:73:ex:words:0:zh":"today","grammar:73:ex:words:0:note":"きょう","grammar:73:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:73:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex:words:2:zh":"good","grammar:73:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:73:ex:words:3:zh":"day","grammar:73:ex:words:3:note":"ひ","grammar:73:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:73:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:73:ex:points:0":"日（ひ）: a day.","grammar:73:ex:points:1":"いい日: a good day.","grammar:73:ex2:trans":"Tomorrow will be a sunny day.","grammar:73:ex2:structure":"〜は〜日です","grammar:73:ex2:words:0:zh":"tomorrow","grammar:73:ex2:words:0:note":"あした","grammar:73:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:73:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex2:words:2:zh":"to clear up","grammar:73:ex2:words:2:note":"はれる","grammar:73:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:73:ex2:words:3:zh":"day","grammar:73:ex2:words:3:note":"ひ","grammar:73:ex2:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex2:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:73:ex2:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:73:ex2:points:0":"晴れる: to clear up (a verb modifying 「日」).","grammar:73:ex2:points:1":"Verb dictionary form ＋ noun: the verb modifies the noun directly.","grammar:73:ex3:trans":"Sunday is the day for doing the things you like.","grammar:73:ex3:structure":"〜は［好きなことをする］日です","grammar:73:ex3:explain":"「日曜日は」 presents Sunday as the topic. 「好きなこと」 means the things you like, and 「を」 marks the object of 「する」. Japanese allows a verb phrase to sit directly before a noun, so 「好きなことをする日」 is the day on which you do the things you like. Finally, 「です」 politely states what kind of day Sunday is.","grammar:73:ex3:words:0:zh":"Sunday","grammar:73:ex3:words:0:note":"にちようび","grammar:73:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:73:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex3:words:2:zh":"liked / favorite","grammar:73:ex3:words:2:note":"すき","grammar:73:ex3:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:73:ex3:words:3:zh":"(links a na-adjective to a noun)","grammar:73:ex3:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:73:ex3:words:4:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:73:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex3:words:5:zh":"(object)","grammar:73:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex3:words:6:zh":"do","grammar:73:ex3:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:73:ex3:words:7:zh":"day","grammar:73:ex3:words:7:note":"ひ","grammar:73:ex3:words:7:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex3:words:8:zh":"is (polite tone)","grammar:73:ex3:words:8:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:73:ex3:points:0":"「好き」 is a na-adjective; when it modifies a noun, you use 「好きな＋noun」.","grammar:73:ex3:points:1":"The whole phrase 「好きなことをする」 modifies 「日」, meaning the day for doing the things you like.","grammar:73:ex4:trans":"I study on my days off.","grammar:73:ex4:structure":"休みの日に〜します","grammar:73:ex4:explain":"「休み」 here is a noun, and 「の」 links it to 「日」 to form a day off. 「休みの日に」 states when the studying happens. 「勉強する」 means to study, and its polite form is 「勉強します」. The subject is omitted from the sentence; following the given translation, it is understood as \"I\".","grammar:73:ex4:words:0:zh":"day off","grammar:73:ex4:words:0:note":"やすみ","grammar:73:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex4:words:1:zh":"(modifies the noun that follows)","grammar:73:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex4:words:2:zh":"day","grammar:73:ex4:words:2:note":"ひ","grammar:73:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex4:words:3:zh":"(time when an action happens)","grammar:73:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex4:words:4:zh":"study","grammar:73:ex4:words:4:note":"べんきょう","grammar:73:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex4:words:5:zh":"do","grammar:73:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:73:ex4:words:6:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:73:ex4:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:73:ex4:points:0":"「休みの日」 joins two nouns with 「の」 to mean a day off.","grammar:73:ex4:points:1":"「に」 after a time noun marks when the action happens.","grammar:73:ex5:trans":"The memory of that day is important.","grammar:73:ex5:structure":"〜の記憶が大切です","grammar:73:ex5:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:73:ex5:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:73:ex5:words:1:zh":"day","grammar:73:ex5:words:1:note":"ひ","grammar:73:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex5:words:2:zh":"'s","grammar:73:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex5:words:3:zh":"memory","grammar:73:ex5:words:3:note":"きおく","grammar:73:ex5:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:73:ex5:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:73:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:73:ex5:words:5:zh":"important","grammar:73:ex5:words:5:note":"たいせつ","grammar:73:ex5:words:5:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:73:ex5:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:73:ex5:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:73:ex5:points:0":"あの日: that day.","grammar:73:ex5:points:1":"記憶が大切: the memory is important (が marks the subject).","exam:73:zh":"The day we leave for the trip is October 7.","exam:73:why":"「日」 means the day, and here it is answered with a full date. 「月」 only means the month and cannot correspond to a date that includes the 7th."},"74":{"example:74:exzh":"Please go to the right.","example:74:exzh2":"This way is safer.","example:74:exzh3":"A cold wind blew in from the north.","example:74:exzh4":"Please choose the correct one.","example:74:exzh5":"I like winter more than summer.","grammar:74:ex:trans":"Please go to the right.","grammar:74:ex:structure":"〜の方に行ってください","grammar:74:ex:explain":"This sentence uses a direction noun with 「に」 to show direction. 「方（ほう）」 is a noun meaning direction, and 「右の方」 means the right-hand side, with 「の」 linking the direction word. 「に」 marks the direction of movement. The te-form of 「行く」 is the irregular 「行って」 (with a double consonant sound change), and adding 「ください」 makes a polite request. The whole sentence 「右の方に行ってください」 means \"Please go to the right\"; it is a common phrase when giving directions, and 「〜の方」 makes the direction more specific and a little softer.","grammar:74:ex:words:0:zh":"the right side","grammar:74:ex:words:0:note":"みぎ","grammar:74:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:74:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex:words:2:zh":"direction","grammar:74:ex:words:2:note":"ほう","grammar:74:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex:words:3:zh":"(direction)","grammar:74:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex:words:4:zh":"go","grammar:74:ex:words:4:note":"いって","grammar:74:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:74:ex:words:5:zh":"please","grammar:74:ex:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:74:ex:points:0":"方（ほう）: direction / that side.","grammar:74:ex:points:1":"〜の方に: in the direction of … (に marks direction).","grammar:74:ex2:trans":"This way is safer.","grammar:74:ex2:structure":"この方が〜です","grammar:74:ex2:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:74:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:74:ex2:words:1:zh":"way / method","grammar:74:ex2:words:1:note":"ほう","grammar:74:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex2:words:2:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:74:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex2:words:3:zh":"safe","grammar:74:ex2:words:3:note":"あんぜん","grammar:74:ex2:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:74:ex2:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:74:ex2:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:74:ex2:points:0":"〜方（ほう）が〜: … is more … (comparative sentence).","grammar:74:ex2:points:1":"この方が安全: this one is safer.","grammar:74:ex3:trans":"A cold wind came blowing from the north.","grammar:74:ex3:structure":"〜の方から〜てきた","grammar:74:ex3:words:0:zh":"north","grammar:74:ex3:words:0:note":"きた","grammar:74:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:74:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex3:words:2:zh":"direction, that side","grammar:74:ex3:words:2:note":"ほう","grammar:74:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex3:words:3:zh":"from","grammar:74:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex3:words:4:zh":"cold","grammar:74:ex3:words:4:note":"つめたい","grammar:74:ex3:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:74:ex3:words:5:zh":"wind","grammar:74:ex3:words:5:note":"かぜ","grammar:74:ex3:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex3:words:6:zh":"(subject)","grammar:74:ex3:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex3:words:7:zh":"blow","grammar:74:ex3:words:7:note":"ふいて; the te-form of 「吹く」","grammar:74:ex3:words:7:pos":"verb","grammar:74:ex3:words:8:zh":"(coming toward the speaker)","grammar:74:ex3:words:8:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:74:ex3:points:0":"❗北の方（ほう）: 「direction word ＋ の方」 means that area or that direction and is read ほう; when it is read かた, it is a respectful word for a person.","grammar:74:ex3:points:1":"から: marks the starting point, \"from …\".","grammar:74:ex3:points:2":"吹いてきた: 「te-form ＋ くる」 shows an action moving toward the speaker.","grammar:74:ex4:trans":"Please choose the correct one.","grammar:74:ex4:structure":"〜方を選んでください","grammar:74:ex4:words:0:zh":"correct","grammar:74:ex4:words:0:note":"ただしい","grammar:74:ex4:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:74:ex4:words:1:zh":"one (of them) / one side","grammar:74:ex4:words:1:note":"ほう","grammar:74:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:74:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex4:words:3:zh":"choose","grammar:74:ex4:words:3:note":"えらんで","grammar:74:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:74:ex4:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:74:ex4:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:74:ex4:points:0":"正しい方: the correct one (方 ＝ ほう).","grammar:74:ex4:points:1":"選ぶ → 選んで ＋ ください.","grammar:74:ex5:trans":"I like winter more than summer.","grammar:74:ex5:structure":"AよりBの方が〜です","grammar:74:ex5:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:74:ex5:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:74:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:74:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:74:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex5:words:2:zh":"summer","grammar:74:ex5:words:2:note":"なつ","grammar:74:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex5:words:3:zh":"than","grammar:74:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex5:words:4:zh":"winter","grammar:74:ex5:words:4:note":"ふゆ","grammar:74:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex5:words:5:zh":"'s","grammar:74:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex5:words:6:zh":"(the comparative) one","grammar:74:ex5:words:6:note":"ほう","grammar:74:ex5:words:6:pos":"noun","grammar:74:ex5:words:7:zh":"(object)","grammar:74:ex5:words:7:pos":"particle","grammar:74:ex5:words:8:zh":"to like","grammar:74:ex5:words:8:note":"すき","grammar:74:ex5:words:8:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:74:ex5:words:9:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:74:ex5:words:9:pos":"copula","grammar:74:ex5:points:0":"❗冬の方が: in the comparative pattern 「AよりBの方が〜」, 方（ほう） refers to the one picked out.","grammar:74:ex5:points:1":"より: marks the basis of comparison, \"than A\".","grammar:74:ex5:points:2":"好きです: the thing you like is marked with が."},"75":{"example:75:exzh":"I'm studying Japanese. And I'm also learning English.","example:75:exzh2":"He runs. And she walks.","example:75:exzh3":"It's sunny today. And the wind is strong too.","example:75:exzh4":"I bought a new house. And then I moved in.","example:75:exzh5":"I finished studying. And then I played with my friends.","grammar:75:ex:trans":"I am studying Japanese, and I also study English.","grammar:75:ex:structure":"〜。そして、〜も〜。","grammar:75:ex:explain":"This sentence demonstrates the conjunction 「そして」 and the particle 「も」. 「そして」 connects two sentences and means \"and then, and moreover\", lining up or sequencing two things. 「も」 means \"also\" and replaces particles such as 「を」, so 「英語も」 means \"English too\", implying that English is added on top of Japanese. In the first sentence, 「勉強しています」 uses 「ている」 to show an ongoing state of studying. The whole sentence says \"I am studying Japanese, and I also study English.\"","grammar:75:ex:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:75:ex:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:75:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:75:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:75:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex:words:2:zh":"Japanese","grammar:75:ex:words:2:note":"にほんご","grammar:75:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:75:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex:words:4:zh":"am studying","grammar:75:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex:words:5:zh":"and then","grammar:75:ex:words:5:pos":"conjunction","grammar:75:ex:words:6:zh":"English","grammar:75:ex:words:6:note":"えいご","grammar:75:ex:words:6:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex:words:7:zh":"also, too","grammar:75:ex:words:7:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex:words:8:zh":"study / learn","grammar:75:ex:words:8:note":"まなびます","grammar:75:ex:words:8:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex:points:0":"そして: and then / and moreover (connects two sentences).","grammar:75:ex:points:1":"も: also (英語も ＝ English too).","grammar:75:ex2:trans":"He is running, and she is walking.","grammar:75:ex2:structure":"〜。そして、〜。","grammar:75:ex2:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:75:ex2:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:75:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:75:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:75:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex2:words:2:zh":"run","grammar:75:ex2:words:2:note":"はしります","grammar:75:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex2:words:3:zh":"and / while","grammar:75:ex2:words:3:pos":"conjunction","grammar:75:ex2:words:4:zh":"she","grammar:75:ex2:words:4:note":"かのじょ","grammar:75:ex2:words:4:pos":"pronoun","grammar:75:ex2:words:5:zh":"(topic)","grammar:75:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex2:words:6:zh":"walk","grammar:75:ex2:words:6:note":"あるきます","grammar:75:ex2:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex2:points:0":"そして: connects two contrasting sentences.","grammar:75:ex2:points:1":"走る → 走ります／歩く → 歩きます.","grammar:75:ex3:trans":"It is sunny today, and the wind is strong too.","grammar:75:ex3:structure":"〜。そして、〜も〜。","grammar:75:ex3:words:0:zh":"today","grammar:75:ex3:words:0:note":"きょう","grammar:75:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:75:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex3:words:2:zh":"sunny weather / clear skies","grammar:75:ex3:words:2:note":"はれ","grammar:75:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex3:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:75:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:75:ex3:words:4:zh":"and moreover","grammar:75:ex3:words:4:pos":"conjunction","grammar:75:ex3:words:5:zh":"wind","grammar:75:ex3:words:5:note":"かぜ","grammar:75:ex3:words:5:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex3:words:6:zh":"also, too","grammar:75:ex3:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex3:words:7:zh":"strong","grammar:75:ex3:words:7:note":"つよい","grammar:75:ex3:words:7:pos":"adjective","grammar:75:ex3:words:8:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:75:ex3:words:8:pos":"copula","grammar:75:ex3:points:0":"そして: and moreover (adding information).","grammar:75:ex3:points:1":"風も強い: the wind is strong too (も adds it).","grammar:75:ex4:trans":"I bought a new house, and then I moved.","grammar:75:ex4:structure":"〜ました。そして、〜ました。","grammar:75:ex4:words:0:zh":"new","grammar:75:ex4:words:0:note":"あたらしい","grammar:75:ex4:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:75:ex4:words:1:zh":"house","grammar:75:ex4:words:1:note":"いえ","grammar:75:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:75:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex4:words:3:zh":"bought","grammar:75:ex4:words:3:note":"かいました","grammar:75:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex4:words:4:zh":"and then","grammar:75:ex4:words:4:pos":"conjunction","grammar:75:ex4:words:5:zh":"moved","grammar:75:ex4:words:5:note":"ひっこしました","grammar:75:ex4:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex4:points:0":"そして: and then (one thing after another in time).","grammar:75:ex4:points:1":"引っ越す → 引っ越しました.","grammar:75:ex5:trans":"Studying finished, and then I hung out with friends.","grammar:75:ex5:structure":"〜ました。そして、〜ました。","grammar:75:ex5:words:0:zh":"study","grammar:75:ex5:words:0:note":"べんきょう","grammar:75:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex5:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:75:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex5:words:2:zh":"finished","grammar:75:ex5:words:2:note":"おわりました","grammar:75:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex5:words:3:zh":"and then","grammar:75:ex5:words:3:pos":"conjunction","grammar:75:ex5:words:4:zh":"friend","grammar:75:ex5:words:4:note":"ともだち","grammar:75:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:75:ex5:words:5:zh":"with","grammar:75:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:75:ex5:words:6:zh":"hung out / played","grammar:75:ex5:words:6:note":"あそびました","grammar:75:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:75:ex5:points:0":"そして: and then.","grammar:75:ex5:points:1":"終わる → 終わりました (intransitive verb; the subject takes が).","exam:75:zh":"This room has a bed, and there's a desk too.","exam:75:why":"「そして」 can link items listed side by side; here it adds that there's also a desk in the room. 「だから」 shows cause and effect, but having a bed isn't the reason there's a desk."},"76":{"example:76:exzh":"My hand hurts.","example:76:exzh2":"I washed my hands.","example:76:exzh3":"Her hands are beautiful.","example:76:exzh4":"Please use this hand.","example:76:exzh5":"I wrote a letter by hand.","grammar:76:ex:trans":"My hand hurts.","grammar:76:ex:structure":"〜が痛いです","grammar:76:ex:explain":"This sentence is about expressing physical discomfort, and the key is 「が」. The part that hurts or feels something is treated as the subject and marked with 「が」, so it is 「手が痛い」 (the hand hurts), not 「を」. 「痛い」 is an i-adjective, and adding 「です」 makes the tone polite. The whole sentence 「手が痛いです」 means \"My hand hurts.\" This body part ＋ が ＋ sensation adjective frame is fixed for describing how your body feels; 「頭が痛い」 and 「お腹が空いた」 work the same way.","grammar:76:ex:words:0:zh":"hand","grammar:76:ex:words:0:note":"て","grammar:76:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:76:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex:words:2:zh":"hurt / painful","grammar:76:ex:words:2:note":"いたい","grammar:76:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:76:ex:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:76:ex:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:76:ex:points:0":"❓Why が? The part that hurts (the subject) takes が.","grammar:76:ex:points:1":"痛い: to hurt (i-adjective).","grammar:76:ex2:trans":"I washed my hands.","grammar:76:ex2:structure":"手を洗いました","grammar:76:ex2:words:0:zh":"hand","grammar:76:ex2:words:0:note":"て","grammar:76:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:76:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex2:words:2:zh":"washed","grammar:76:ex2:words:2:note":"あらいました","grammar:76:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:76:ex2:points:0":"を marks the object (washing 「手」).","grammar:76:ex2:points:1":"洗う → 洗いました.","grammar:76:ex3:trans":"Her hands are beautiful.","grammar:76:ex3:structure":"〜の手は〜です","grammar:76:ex3:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:76:ex3:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:76:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:76:ex3:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:76:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex3:words:2:zh":"hand","grammar:76:ex3:words:2:note":"て","grammar:76:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex3:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:76:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex3:words:4:zh":"beautiful","grammar:76:ex3:words:4:note":"うつくしい","grammar:76:ex3:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:76:ex3:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:76:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:76:ex3:points:0":"彼女の手: her hands (の shows possession).","grammar:76:ex3:points:1":"美しいです: polite form of an i-adjective.","grammar:76:ex4:trans":"Please use this hand.","grammar:76:ex4:structure":"〜を使ってください","grammar:76:ex4:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:76:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:76:ex4:words:1:zh":"hand","grammar:76:ex4:words:1:note":"て","grammar:76:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:76:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex4:words:3:zh":"use","grammar:76:ex4:words:3:note":"つかって","grammar:76:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:76:ex4:words:4:zh":"please","grammar:76:ex4:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:76:ex4:points:0":"使う → 使って (te-form) ＋ ください.","grammar:76:ex4:points:1":"「手」 can also extend to mean a method or a means.","grammar:76:ex5:trans":"I wrote a letter by hand.","grammar:76:ex5:structure":"〜で〜を書きました","grammar:76:ex5:explain":"「手で」 means by hand, and 「で」 here marks the means. 「手紙を」 uses 「を」 to mark what is being written. 「書く」 becomes 「書きます」 in the polite form, and 「書きました」 then shows a completed action in the past. The Japanese does not state how many letters, so \"a letter\" is simply the natural English rendering.","grammar:76:ex5:words:0:zh":"hand","grammar:76:ex5:words:0:note":"て","grammar:76:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex5:words:1:zh":"(tool, means)","grammar:76:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex5:words:2:zh":"letter","grammar:76:ex5:words:2:note":"てがみ","grammar:76:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:76:ex5:words:3:zh":"(object)","grammar:76:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:76:ex5:words:4:zh":"write","grammar:76:ex5:words:4:note":"かき","grammar:76:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:76:ex5:words:5:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:76:ex5:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:76:ex5:words:6:zh":"(past, completed)","grammar:76:ex5:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:76:ex5:points:0":"The 「で」 in 「手で」 marks the tool or means used.","grammar:76:ex5:points:1":"「書きました」 is the polite past form of 「書く」, showing that the writing is already done.","exam:76:zh":"Before eating, please wash both hands with soap.","exam:76:why":"What you wash with soap before eating is 「手」 (hands). You could wash 「足」 (feet) as well, but that doesn't fit the situation of washing before a meal."},"77":{"example:77:exzh":"I found a wallet.","example:77:exzh2":"I found a new friend.","example:77:exzh3":"He found success.","example:77:exzh4":"Finding a good job is hard.","example:77:exzh5":"I found the book and was happy.","grammar:77:ex:trans":"Found a wallet.","grammar:77:ex:structure":"〜を見つけました","grammar:77:ex:explain":"The key point here is the difference between transitive and intransitive verbs. 「見つける」 is a transitive verb meaning '(actively) to find'; the action has an object, marked with 「を」, so 「財布を見つける」 = 'to find a wallet'. Its intransitive counterpart is 「見つかる」 (to be found, to turn up on its own), whose subject takes 「が」. The verb 「見つける」 is an ichidan (ru-) verb, and its past polite form is 「見つけました」. The whole sentence 「財布を見つけました」 = 'found a wallet' — remember to memorize transitive and intransitive verbs in pairs.","grammar:77:ex:words:0:zh":"wallet","grammar:77:ex:words:0:note":"さいふ","grammar:77:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:77:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:77:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex:words:2:zh":"found","grammar:77:ex:words:2:note":"みつけました","grammar:77:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:77:ex:points:0":"❗見つける (transitive verb, to find) vs 見つかる (intransitive verb, to be found).","grammar:77:ex:points:1":"財布を見つける: to find a wallet.","grammar:77:ex2:trans":"Found a new friend.","grammar:77:ex2:structure":"〜を見つけました","grammar:77:ex2:words:0:zh":"new","grammar:77:ex2:words:0:note":"あたらしい","grammar:77:ex2:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:77:ex2:words:1:zh":"friend","grammar:77:ex2:words:1:note":"ともだち","grammar:77:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:77:ex2:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:77:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex2:words:3:zh":"found","grammar:77:ex2:words:3:note":"みつけました","grammar:77:ex2:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:77:ex2:points:0":"新しい友達: a new friend.","grammar:77:ex2:points:1":"見つける: to discover, to find.","grammar:77:ex3:trans":"He found success.","grammar:77:ex3:structure":"〜を見つけました","grammar:77:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:77:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:77:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:77:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:77:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex3:words:2:zh":"success","grammar:77:ex3:words:2:note":"せいこう","grammar:77:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:77:ex3:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:77:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex3:words:4:zh":"found","grammar:77:ex3:words:4:note":"みつけました","grammar:77:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:77:ex3:points:0":"※ 「成功を見つける」 sounds slightly stiff (better: 「成功をつかむ」).","grammar:77:ex3:points:1":"成功: success.","grammar:77:ex4:trans":"Finding a good job is hard.","grammar:77:ex4:structure":"〜のは難しい","grammar:77:ex4:words:0:zh":"good","grammar:77:ex4:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:77:ex4:words:1:zh":"work","grammar:77:ex4:words:1:note":"しごと","grammar:77:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:77:ex4:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:77:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex4:words:3:zh":"find","grammar:77:ex4:words:3:note":"みつける","grammar:77:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:77:ex4:words:4:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:77:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex4:words:5:zh":"(topic)","grammar:77:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex4:words:6:zh":"difficult","grammar:77:ex4:words:6:note":"むずかしい","grammar:77:ex4:words:6:pos":"adjective","grammar:77:ex4:points:0":"いい仕事を見つける: to find a good job.","grammar:77:ex4:points:1":"〜のは難しい: it is hard to…","grammar:77:ex5:trans":"I was happy to find a book.","grammar:77:ex5:structure":"〜を見つけて、〜かった","grammar:77:ex5:words:0:zh":"book","grammar:77:ex5:words:0:note":"ほん","grammar:77:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:77:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:77:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:77:ex5:words:2:zh":"find","grammar:77:ex5:words:2:note":"みつけて","grammar:77:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:77:ex5:words:3:zh":"(past) was happy","grammar:77:ex5:words:3:note":"うれしかった","grammar:77:ex5:words:3:pos":"adjective","grammar:77:ex5:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:77:ex5:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:77:ex5:points:0":"❗〜て、〜: found ... and (then) was happy (the te-form shows cause).","grammar:77:ex5:points:1":"嬉しかった: was happy (past)."},"78":{"example:78:exzh":"I'll go right away.","example:78:exzh2":"I'll call right away.","example:78:exzh3":"Once I eat, I go right to sleep.","example:78:exzh4":"I'll go home right away.","example:78:exzh5":"It's a job that can be done right away.","grammar:78:ex:trans":"I'll go right away.","grammar:78:ex:structure":"すぐ〜ます","grammar:78:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the adverb 「すぐ」 to modify the action. 「すぐ」 means \"right away, immediately\" and stresses that the action happens at once; 「すぐに」 is also possible and sounds much the same. The verb 「行く」 is a godan (u-) verb, and its polite form 「行きます」 expresses going now or in the future. The whole sentence 「すぐ行きます」 means \"I'll go right away\"; it is often used to answer someone who calls or urges you, showing that you will act at once. Time adverbs like this go before the verb, which makes the immediacy of the action obvious.","grammar:78:ex:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:78:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:78:ex:words:1:zh":"go","grammar:78:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex:points:0":"すぐ: right away, immediately.","grammar:78:ex:points:1":"行く → 行きます.","grammar:78:ex2:trans":"I'll call right away.","grammar:78:ex2:structure":"すぐに〜します","grammar:78:ex2:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:78:ex2:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:78:ex2:words:1:zh":"make a phone call","grammar:78:ex2:words:1:note":"でんわします","grammar:78:ex2:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex2:points:0":"すぐに: immediately (＝ すぐ; adding に adds emphasis).","grammar:78:ex2:points:1":"電話する→電話します。","grammar:78:ex3:trans":"Once I have eaten, I go straight to bed.","grammar:78:ex3:structure":"〜たらすぐ〜","grammar:78:ex3:words:0:zh":"once (I) eat","grammar:78:ex3:words:0:note":"たべたら","grammar:78:ex3:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex3:words:1:zh":"soon","grammar:78:ex3:words:1:pos":"adverb","grammar:78:ex3:words:2:zh":"sleep","grammar:78:ex3:words:2:note":"ねる","grammar:78:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex3:points:0":"〜たら: once (you) have done …, then … (condition / time).","grammar:78:ex3:points:1":"食べる → 食べたら; 寝る in plain form.","grammar:78:ex4:trans":"I'll go home right away.","grammar:78:ex4:structure":"すぐに〜ます","grammar:78:ex4:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:78:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:78:ex4:words:1:zh":"go home / return","grammar:78:ex4:words:1:note":"かえります","grammar:78:ex4:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex4:points:0":"すぐに: immediately.","grammar:78:ex4:points:1":"帰る → 帰ります.","grammar:78:ex5:trans":"This is a job that can be done right away.","grammar:78:ex5:structure":"〜できる仕事です","grammar:78:ex5:words:0:zh":"soon","grammar:78:ex5:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:78:ex5:words:1:zh":"can do","grammar:78:ex5:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:78:ex5:words:2:zh":"work","grammar:78:ex5:words:2:note":"しごと","grammar:78:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:78:ex5:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:78:ex5:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:78:ex5:points:0":"できる: to be able to (potential verb).","grammar:78:ex5:points:1":"A verb modifies a noun: できる ＋ 仕事.","exam:78:zh":"There are only two minutes until the train, so let's leave right now.","exam:78:why":"「すぐ」 means acting right away. 「あとで」 means later, which doesn't fit having only two minutes left."},"79":{"example:79:exzh":"You must not do bad things.","example:79:exzh2":"This dish tastes bad.","example:79:exzh3":"I heard some bad news.","example:79:exzh4":"He isn't a bad person.","example:79:exzh5":"This movie has a bad reputation.","grammar:79:ex:trans":"You must not do bad things.","grammar:79:ex:structure":"〜てはいけません","grammar:79:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the prohibition pattern 「〜てはいけません」. 「悪いこと」 is the i-adjective 「悪い」 modifying the noun 「こと」 directly, meaning bad things. The te-form of 「する」 is 「して」, and adding 「はいけません」 forms a prohibition meaning \"you must not (do) …\". The whole sentence 「悪いことはしてはいけません」 means \"You must not do bad things.\" This 「〜てはいけません」 sounds fairly formal and rule-like; in casual speech it often shrinks to 「〜ちゃいけない」.","grammar:79:ex:words:0:zh":"bad","grammar:79:ex:words:0:note":"わるい","grammar:79:ex:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:79:ex:words:1:zh":"thing / matter","grammar:79:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:79:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex:words:3:zh":"do","grammar:79:ex:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:79:ex:words:4:zh":"must not","grammar:79:ex:words:4:pos":"set phrase","grammar:79:ex:points:0":"悪いこと: a bad thing (i-adjective ＋ noun).","grammar:79:ex:points:1":"〜てはいけません: must not (do) … (prohibition).","grammar:79:ex2:trans":"This dish tastes bad.","grammar:79:ex2:structure":"〜は味が悪いです","grammar:79:ex2:explain":"「この料理は」 brings up this dish as the topic, and 「味が悪い」 then says that its taste is bad. 「は」 and 「が」 play different roles: the first marks what is being talked about, the second marks the thing described as bad. 「この」 must attach to a noun and cannot be used alone. 「悪いです」 is the polite adjectival predicate.","grammar:79:ex2:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:79:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:79:ex2:words:1:zh":"dish / cuisine","grammar:79:ex2:words:1:note":"りょうり","grammar:79:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex2:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:79:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex2:words:3:zh":"taste","grammar:79:ex2:words:3:note":"あじ","grammar:79:ex2:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex2:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:79:ex2:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex2:words:5:zh":"bad / not good","grammar:79:ex2:words:5:note":"わるい","grammar:79:ex2:words:5:pos":"i-adjective","grammar:79:ex2:words:6:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:79:ex2:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:79:ex2:points:0":"With 「〜は〜が＋adjective」, you first present the topic and then describe one part or feature of it.","grammar:79:ex2:points:1":"「悪い」 is itself an i-adjective, and adding 「です」 after it makes the sentence polite.","grammar:79:ex3:trans":"I heard bad news.","grammar:79:ex3:structure":"悪い〜を聞いた","grammar:79:ex3:words:0:zh":"bad","grammar:79:ex3:words:0:note":"わるい","grammar:79:ex3:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:79:ex3:words:1:zh":"news","grammar:79:ex3:words:1:note":"しらせ","grammar:79:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex3:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:79:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex3:words:3:zh":"heard","grammar:79:ex3:words:3:note":"きいた","grammar:79:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:79:ex3:points:0":"知らせ: news, notice.","grammar:79:ex3:points:1":"聞く → 聞いた (plain past).","grammar:79:ex4:trans":"He is not a bad person.","grammar:79:ex4:structure":"〜ではありません","grammar:79:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:79:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:79:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:79:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:79:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex4:words:2:zh":"bad","grammar:79:ex4:words:2:note":"わるい","grammar:79:ex4:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:79:ex4:words:3:zh":"person","grammar:79:ex4:words:3:note":"ひと","grammar:79:ex4:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex4:words:4:zh":"is not","grammar:79:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:79:ex4:points:0":"ではありません: is not … (polite negative of a noun sentence).","grammar:79:ex4:points:1":"悪い人: a bad person.","grammar:79:ex5:trans":"This movie has a bad reputation.","grammar:79:ex5:structure":"〜は評判が悪いです","grammar:79:ex5:explain":"「この映画は」 shows that the topic is this movie. 「評判」 means the reputation or word of mouth that people have about someone or something, and once it is marked with 「が」 it takes 「悪い」 to say the reputation is bad. The sentence describes the movie's reputation; it does not directly claim that the movie itself is bad. The final 「です」 makes the tone more polite.","grammar:79:ex5:words:0:zh":"this (one)","grammar:79:ex5:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:79:ex5:words:1:zh":"movie","grammar:79:ex5:words:1:note":"えいが","grammar:79:ex5:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex5:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:79:ex5:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex5:words:3:zh":"reputation, word of mouth","grammar:79:ex5:words:3:note":"ひょうばん","grammar:79:ex5:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:79:ex5:words:4:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:79:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:79:ex5:words:5:zh":"bad / not good","grammar:79:ex5:words:5:note":"わるい","grammar:79:ex5:words:5:pos":"i-adjective","grammar:79:ex5:words:6:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:79:ex5:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:79:ex5:points:0":"「評判が悪い」 means the reputation or word of mouth is bad.","grammar:79:ex5:points:1":"「映画は」 presents the topic, and 「評判が」 points out the specific feature being described.","exam:79:zh":"This milk smells off, so please don't drink it — throw it out.","exam:79:why":"「においが悪い」 means the smell is bad, which explains why it can't be drunk. 「甘い」 means sweet, and a sweet smell on its own doesn't explain why the milk has to be thrown out."},"80":{"example:80:exzh":"I enter the room.","example:80:exzh2":"I went inside the school.","example:80:exzh3":"The money came in.","example:80:exzh4":"He went into the house.","example:80:exzh5":"The train enters the station.","grammar:80:ex:trans":"I enter the room.","grammar:80:ex:structure":"〜に入ります","grammar:80:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the intransitive verb 「入る」 with 「に」. 「入る（はいる）」 means 'to enter' and is intransitive; the place you enter is marked with 「に」, so 「部屋に入る」 = 'to enter the room'. Its transitive counterpart is 「入れる」 (to put in, to insert), which takes an object with 「を」 — keep the two apart. Although 「入る」 ends in 「る」, it is a godan (u-) verb (an exception), and its polite form is 「入ります」. The whole sentence 「部屋に入ります」 = '(I) enter the room'.","grammar:80:ex:words:0:zh":"room","grammar:80:ex:words:0:note":"へや","grammar:80:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex:words:1:zh":"(destination)","grammar:80:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex:words:2:zh":"enter","grammar:80:ex:words:2:note":"はいります","grammar:80:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:80:ex:points:0":"❗入る（はいる）: to enter (intransitive verb); vs 入れる (transitive verb, to put in).","grammar:80:ex:points:1":"〜に入る: to enter ...","grammar:80:ex2:trans":"I walked into the school.","grammar:80:ex2:structure":"〜の中に入りました","grammar:80:ex2:explain":"「学校の中」 uses 「の」 to link the school and 'inside', meaning the inside of the school. 「に」 marks the destination being entered. 「入る」 is read 「はいる」; even though it ends in 「る」, it is still a godan (u-) verb, with the polite form 「入ります」 and the past form 「入りました」. The original sentence only says 'enter'; the idea of walking in is supplied by the Chinese translation.","grammar:80:ex2:words:0:zh":"school","grammar:80:ex2:words:0:note":"がっこう","grammar:80:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex2:words:1:zh":"(modifies the noun that follows)","grammar:80:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex2:words:2:zh":"inside","grammar:80:ex2:words:2:note":"なか","grammar:80:ex2:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex2:words:3:zh":"(the destination being entered)","grammar:80:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex2:words:4:zh":"enter","grammar:80:ex2:words:4:note":"はいり","grammar:80:ex2:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:80:ex2:words:5:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:80:ex2:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:80:ex2:words:6:zh":"(past, completed)","grammar:80:ex2:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:80:ex2:points:0":"「〜の中」 means the inside of a place or object.","grammar:80:ex2:points:1":"「入る」 is an intransitive verb, and the destination entered is usually marked with 「に」.","grammar:80:ex3:trans":"Money came in.","grammar:80:ex3:structure":"〜が入った","grammar:80:ex3:words:0:zh":"money","grammar:80:ex3:words:0:note":"おかね","grammar:80:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex3:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:80:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex3:words:2:zh":"came up","grammar:80:ex3:words:2:note":"はいった","grammar:80:ex3:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:80:ex3:points:0":"❗お金が入る: money comes in, to get paid (intransitive verb, takes が).","grammar:80:ex3:points:1":"入る→入った。","grammar:80:ex4:trans":"He went into the house.","grammar:80:ex4:structure":"〜に入った","grammar:80:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:80:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:80:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:80:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:80:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex4:words:2:zh":"house","grammar:80:ex4:words:2:note":"いえ","grammar:80:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex4:words:3:zh":"(destination)","grammar:80:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex4:words:4:zh":"went in","grammar:80:ex4:words:4:note":"はいった","grammar:80:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:80:ex4:points:0":"家に入る: to go into the house.","grammar:80:ex4:points:1":"入る→入った。","grammar:80:ex5:trans":"The train enters the station.","grammar:80:ex5:structure":"〜が〜に入ります","grammar:80:ex5:words:0:zh":"train","grammar:80:ex5:words:0:note":"でんしゃ","grammar:80:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex5:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:80:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex5:words:2:zh":"station","grammar:80:ex5:words:2:note":"えき","grammar:80:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:80:ex5:words:3:zh":"(destination)","grammar:80:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:80:ex5:words:4:zh":"enter","grammar:80:ex5:words:4:note":"はいります","grammar:80:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:80:ex5:points:0":"電車が駅に入る: the train enters the station.","grammar:80:ex5:points:1":"が marks the subject.","exam:80:zh":"It started to rain, so I decided to stop playing outside and go into the house.","exam:80:why":"「入る」 means going from outside to inside, which fits 「家の中に」. 「出る」 means going out, the opposite direction."},"81":{"example:81:exzh":"I'll help him.","example:81:exzh2":"Please help me.","example:81:exzh3":"I helped someone in trouble.","example:81:exzh4":"She helped me out.","example:81:exzh5":"Helping friends is important.","grammar:81:ex:trans":"I'll help him.","grammar:81:ex:structure":"〜を助けます","grammar:81:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the transitive verb 「助ける」 with 「を」. 「助ける（たすける）」 means 'to help, to rescue' and is transitive; the person being helped is marked with 「を」, so 「彼を助ける」 = 'to help him'. 「助ける」 is an ichidan (ru-) verb; drop 「る」 and add 「ます」 to get the polite form 「助けます」, which refers to the present or future. The whole sentence 「彼を助けます」 = 'I'll help him'. Note that the person helped takes 「を」 — don't confuse this with verbs like 「頼む」, which appears later and takes 「に」.","grammar:81:ex:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:81:ex:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:81:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:81:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:81:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex:words:2:zh":"help","grammar:81:ex:words:2:note":"たすけます","grammar:81:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex:points:0":"❗助ける（たすける）: to help, to rescue (transitive verb) + を.","grammar:81:ex:points:1":"彼を助ける: to help him.","grammar:81:ex2:trans":"Please help me.","grammar:81:ex2:structure":"助けてください","grammar:81:ex2:words:0:zh":"help","grammar:81:ex2:words:0:note":"たすけて","grammar:81:ex2:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex2:words:1:zh":"please","grammar:81:ex2:words:1:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:81:ex2:points:0":"❗助けて（ください）: please help / help!","grammar:81:ex2:points:1":"助ける→助けて。","grammar:81:ex3:trans":"I helped someone in trouble.","grammar:81:ex3:structure":"〜を助けた","grammar:81:ex3:words:0:zh":"was in trouble","grammar:81:ex3:words:0:note":"こまっている","grammar:81:ex3:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex3:words:1:zh":"person","grammar:81:ex3:words:1:note":"ひと","grammar:81:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:81:ex3:words:2:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:81:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex3:words:3:zh":"helped","grammar:81:ex3:words:3:note":"たすけた","grammar:81:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex3:points:0":"困っている人: a person in trouble (modifies a noun).","grammar:81:ex3:points:1":"助ける→助けた。","grammar:81:ex4:trans":"She helped me out.","grammar:81:ex4:structure":"〜を助けてくれた","grammar:81:ex4:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:81:ex4:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:81:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:81:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:81:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex4:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:81:ex4:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:81:ex4:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:81:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:81:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex4:words:4:zh":"help","grammar:81:ex4:words:4:note":"たすけて","grammar:81:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex4:words:5:zh":"did (for me)","grammar:81:ex4:words:5:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:81:ex4:points:0":"❗〜てくれた: (someone else) did ... for me.","grammar:81:ex4:points:1":"私を助けてくれた: helped me.","grammar:81:ex5:trans":"Helping friends is important.","grammar:81:ex5:structure":"〜のは大事です","grammar:81:ex5:words:0:zh":"friend","grammar:81:ex5:words:0:note":"ともだち","grammar:81:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:81:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:81:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex5:words:2:zh":"help","grammar:81:ex5:words:2:note":"たすける","grammar:81:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:81:ex5:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:81:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex5:words:4:zh":"(topic)","grammar:81:ex5:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:81:ex5:words:5:zh":"important","grammar:81:ex5:words:5:note":"だいじ","grammar:81:ex5:words:5:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:81:ex5:words:6:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:81:ex5:words:6:pos":"copula","grammar:81:ex5:points:0":"友達を助ける: to help a friend.","grammar:81:ex5:points:1":"〜のは大事です: doing ... is important."},"82":{"example:82:exzh":"I'll stop doing that.","example:82:exzh2":"I decided to quit smoking.","example:82:exzh3":"He quit his job.","example:82:exzh4":"It's already late, so let's stop.","example:82:exzh5":"It's better not to push yourself too hard.","grammar:82:ex:trans":"I'll stop doing that.","grammar:82:ex:structure":"〜をやめます","grammar:82:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the transitive verb 「やめる」 with 「を」. 「やめる」 can be written 「止める／辞める」 in kanji and means to stop, give up, or quit. It is a transitive verb, and the thing you stop takes 「を」, so 「それをやめる」 means to stop doing that. 「やめる」 is an ichidan (ru-) verb, polite form 「やめます」. The whole sentence 「それをやめます」 means I'll stop doing that. It's a very useful word, handy for quitting smoking, leaving a job, or abandoning a plan.","grammar:82:ex:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:82:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:82:ex:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:82:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex:words:2:zh":"stop","grammar:82:ex:words:2:note":"やめます","grammar:82:ex:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex:points:0":"❗やめる（止める／辞める）: to stop, give up, quit (transitive verb); それをやめる = stop doing that.","grammar:82:ex:points:1":"やめる: stop / give up.","grammar:82:ex2:trans":"I decided to quit smoking.","grammar:82:ex2:structure":"〜をやめることにしました","grammar:82:ex2:words:0:zh":"cigarettes","grammar:82:ex2:words:0:note":"loanword","grammar:82:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:82:ex2:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:82:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex2:words:2:zh":"quit","grammar:82:ex2:words:2:note":"やめる","grammar:82:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex2:words:3:zh":"(nominalizer)","grammar:82:ex2:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:82:ex2:words:4:zh":"(result)","grammar:82:ex2:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex2:words:5:zh":"decide","grammar:82:ex2:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex2:points:0":"❗タバコをやめる: to quit smoking; 〜ことにする = decide to …","grammar:82:ex2:points:1":"タバコをやめる: quit smoking.","grammar:82:ex3:trans":"He quit his job.","grammar:82:ex3:structure":"〜をやめた","grammar:82:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:82:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:82:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:82:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:82:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex3:words:2:zh":"work","grammar:82:ex3:words:2:note":"しごと","grammar:82:ex3:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:82:ex3:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:82:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex3:words:4:zh":"quit","grammar:82:ex3:words:4:note":"やめた","grammar:82:ex3:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex3:points:0":"❗仕事をやめる: to quit a job (in this sense usually written 「辞める」).","grammar:82:ex3:points:1":"仕事をやめる: quit a job.","grammar:82:ex4:trans":"It's already late, so let's stop here.","grammar:82:ex4:structure":"〜のでやめましょう","grammar:82:ex4:words:0:zh":"already","grammar:82:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:82:ex4:words:1:zh":"late","grammar:82:ex4:words:1:note":"おそい","grammar:82:ex4:words:1:pos":"adjective","grammar:82:ex4:words:2:zh":"because","grammar:82:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex4:words:3:zh":"let's stop","grammar:82:ex4:words:3:note":"やめましょう","grammar:82:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex4:points:0":"❗〜ので: because …; やめましょう = let's stop (a suggestion).","grammar:82:ex4:points:1":"やめましょう: let's call it a day.","grammar:82:ex5:trans":"You'd better stop forcing yourself.","grammar:82:ex5:structure":"無理をやめた方がいい","grammar:82:ex5:words:0:zh":"pushing yourself too hard","grammar:82:ex5:words:0:note":"むり","grammar:82:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:82:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:82:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:82:ex5:words:2:zh":"stop","grammar:82:ex5:words:2:note":"やめた","grammar:82:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:82:ex5:words:3:zh":"it's better to","grammar:82:ex5:words:3:note":"ほうがいい","grammar:82:ex5:words:3:pos":"set phrase","grammar:82:ex5:points:0":"❗無理をやめる: stop overdoing it, stop forcing yourself; 〜た方がいい = you'd better …","grammar:82:ex5:points:1":"無理をやめる: stop forcing yourself."},"83":{"example:83:exzh":"She has big eyes.","example:83:exzh2":"My eyes are tired.","example:83:exzh3":"My eyes hurt.","example:83:exzh4":"Please close your eyes.","example:83:exzh5":"To wake up.","grammar:83:ex:trans":"She has big eyes.","grammar:83:ex:structure":"〜を持っています (has 〜)","grammar:83:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「〜を持っています」 to describe a physical feature. 「大きな」 is a pre-noun adjectival and can only attach to a noun: 「大きな目」 means big eyes. It is close in meaning to the i-adjective 「大きい」, but a pre-noun adjectival cannot stand alone as a predicate. 「を」 marks the object, and 「持っている」 here shows an ongoing state of possessing rather than an action. The whole sentence 「大きな目を持っています」 means \"She has big eyes\", a common way to describe someone's looks.","grammar:83:ex:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:83:ex:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:83:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:83:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:83:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex:words:2:zh":"big","grammar:83:ex:words:2:note":"おおきな","grammar:83:ex:words:2:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:83:ex:words:3:zh":"eye(s)","grammar:83:ex:words:3:note":"め","grammar:83:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:83:ex:words:4:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:83:ex:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex:words:5:zh":"own, have","grammar:83:ex:words:5:note":"もっています","grammar:83:ex:words:5:pos":"verb","grammar:83:ex:points:0":"大きな: big (pre-noun adjectival, attaches only to nouns).","grammar:83:ex:points:1":"〜を持っている: to have … (a feature).","grammar:83:ex2:trans":"My eyes are tired.","grammar:83:ex2:structure":"〜が疲れた","grammar:83:ex2:words:0:zh":"eye(s)","grammar:83:ex2:words:0:note":"め","grammar:83:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:83:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:83:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex2:words:2:zh":"tired","grammar:83:ex2:words:2:note":"つかれた","grammar:83:ex2:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:83:ex2:points:0":"❓Why が? The part that is tired (the subject) takes が.","grammar:83:ex2:points:1":"疲れる → 疲れた (plain past).","grammar:83:ex3:trans":"My eyes hurt.","grammar:83:ex3:structure":"〜が痛いです","grammar:83:ex3:words:0:zh":"eye(s)","grammar:83:ex3:words:0:note":"め","grammar:83:ex3:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:83:ex3:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:83:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex3:words:2:zh":"hurt / painful","grammar:83:ex3:words:2:note":"いたい","grammar:83:ex3:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:83:ex3:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:83:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:83:ex3:points:0":"Body part ＋ が痛い: something hurts.","grammar:83:ex3:points:1":"痛い: to hurt (i-adjective).","grammar:83:ex4:trans":"Please close your eyes.","grammar:83:ex4:structure":"目を閉じてください","grammar:83:ex4:words:0:zh":"eye(s)","grammar:83:ex4:words:0:note":"め","grammar:83:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:83:ex4:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:83:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex4:words:2:zh":"close","grammar:83:ex4:words:2:note":"とじて","grammar:83:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:83:ex4:words:3:zh":"please","grammar:83:ex4:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:83:ex4:points:0":"閉じる: to close, to shut.","grammar:83:ex4:points:1":"閉じる → 閉じて ＋ ください.","grammar:83:ex5:trans":"wake up","grammar:83:ex5:structure":"目を覚ます (idiomatic)","grammar:83:ex5:words:0:zh":"eye(s)","grammar:83:ex5:words:0:note":"め","grammar:83:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:83:ex5:words:1:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:83:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:83:ex5:words:2:zh":"wake (someone) up","grammar:83:ex5:words:2:note":"さます","grammar:83:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:83:ex5:points:0":"目を覚ます: to open one's eyes / to wake up (idiomatic).","grammar:83:ex5:points:1":"覚ます: to wake (someone) up (transitive verb).","exam:83:zh":"Because I looked at a light that was too bright, it dazzled my eyes and I closed them.","exam:83:why":"「目を閉じる」 means to close your eyes, which fits the situation of blinding light. 「口を閉じる」 means to close your mouth, which has nothing to do with being dazzled."},"84":{"example:84:exzh":"Where is the place you want to go?","example:84:exzh2":"This is my place.","example:84:exzh3":"This is a nice place, isn't it?","example:84:exzh4":"I'm looking forward to going to that place.","example:84:exzh5":"A place that stays in my memory.","grammar:84:ex:trans":"Where is the place you want to go?","grammar:84:ex:structure":"〜所はどこですか","grammar:84:ex:explain":"This sentence shows a verb modifying a noun directly. The verb 「行きたい」 (want to go) sits directly before the noun 「所」 to modify it, giving 「行きたい所」, the place you want to go; Japanese verbs (including the たい form) can modify a noun without adding any particle. 「所（ところ）」 means place. The sentence ends with 「どこですか」 to ask about a location. The whole sentence asks \"Where is the place you want to go?\", practicing how verbs modify nouns just like adjectives.","grammar:84:ex:words:0:zh":"want to go","grammar:84:ex:words:0:note":"いきたい","grammar:84:ex:words:0:pos":"verb","grammar:84:ex:words:1:zh":"place","grammar:84:ex:words:1:note":"ところ","grammar:84:ex:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:84:ex:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex:words:3:zh":"where","grammar:84:ex:words:3:pos":"question word","grammar:84:ex:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:84:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:84:ex:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:84:ex:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex:points:0":"所（ところ）: place.","grammar:84:ex:points:1":"行きたい所: the place you want to go (a verb modifying a noun directly).","grammar:84:ex2:trans":"This is my place.","grammar:84:ex2:structure":"ここは〜の所です","grammar:84:ex2:words:0:zh":"here","grammar:84:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:84:ex2:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:84:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex2:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:84:ex2:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:84:ex2:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:84:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:84:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex2:words:4:zh":"place","grammar:84:ex2:words:4:note":"ところ","grammar:84:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex2:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:84:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:84:ex2:points:0":"私の所: my place.","grammar:84:ex2:points:1":"の shows possession.","grammar:84:ex3:trans":"This is a nice place, isn't it?","grammar:84:ex3:structure":"良い所ですね","grammar:84:ex3:words:0:zh":"good","grammar:84:ex3:words:0:note":"よい","grammar:84:ex3:words:0:pos":"adjective","grammar:84:ex3:words:1:zh":"place","grammar:84:ex3:words:1:note":"ところ","grammar:84:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex3:words:2:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:84:ex3:words:2:pos":"copula","grammar:84:ex3:words:3:zh":"right?","grammar:84:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex3:points:0":"良い所: a good place.","grammar:84:ex3:points:1":"ね: seeking agreement.","grammar:84:ex4:trans":"I am looking forward to going to that place.","grammar:84:ex4:structure":"〜に行くのが楽しみです","grammar:84:ex4:explain":"「その所に行く」 means going to that place, and 「に」 marks the destination. 「の」 turns the whole action into a noun, and 「が」 then marks what is being looked forward to. 「楽しみです」 here expresses anticipation for something in the future.","grammar:84:ex4:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:84:ex4:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:84:ex4:words:1:zh":"place","grammar:84:ex4:words:1:note":"ところ","grammar:84:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex4:words:2:zh":"(destination of movement)","grammar:84:ex4:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex4:words:3:zh":"go","grammar:84:ex4:words:3:note":"いく","grammar:84:ex4:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:84:ex4:words:4:zh":"(nominalizes the action)","grammar:84:ex4:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex4:words:5:zh":"(what is being looked forward to)","grammar:84:ex4:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex4:words:6:zh":"something to look forward to","grammar:84:ex4:words:6:note":"たのしみ","grammar:84:ex4:words:6:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:84:ex4:words:7:zh":"(polite statement)","grammar:84:ex4:words:7:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:84:ex4:points:0":"「動詞辭書形＋のが楽しみです」 expresses looking forward to doing something.","grammar:84:ex4:points:1":"「その所」 is understandable, but in everyday speech people more often say 「そこ」 or 「その場所」.","grammar:84:ex5:trans":"A place that stays in my memory.","grammar:84:ex5:structure":"〜の記憶に残っている所","grammar:84:ex5:explain":"「私の記憶に」 means in my memory, and 「残る」 is an intransitive verb meaning to remain or stay. 「残っている」 describes the state of that place still remaining in memory. The sentence ends with 「所」 and has no main predicate, so it is the noun phrase \"a place that stays in my memory\".","grammar:84:ex5:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:84:ex5:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:84:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:84:ex5:words:1:zh":"(possession)","grammar:84:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex5:words:2:zh":"memory","grammar:84:ex5:words:2:note":"きおく","grammar:84:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex5:words:3:zh":"(the place where it remains)","grammar:84:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex5:words:4:zh":"to remain, to stay","grammar:84:ex5:words:4:note":"のこっ","grammar:84:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:84:ex5:words:5:zh":"(connects to the resulting state that follows)","grammar:84:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:84:ex5:words:6:zh":"(the state left behind continues to exist)","grammar:84:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:84:ex5:words:7:zh":"place","grammar:84:ex5:words:7:note":"ところ","grammar:84:ex5:words:7:pos":"noun","grammar:84:ex5:points:0":"「残っている」 expresses a resulting state that still exists after something has been left behind.","grammar:84:ex5:points:1":"The whole 「私の記憶に残っている」 modifies 「所」, and the entire sentence is a noun phrase."},"88":{"example:88:exzh":"He's taller than me.","example:88:exzh2":"This book is more interesting than that one.","example:88:exzh3":"I'm older than him.","example:88:exzh4":"Cats are cuter than dogs.","example:88:exzh5":"I think Japanese is harder than English.","grammar:88:ex:trans":"He is taller than me.","grammar:88:ex:structure":"〜は〜より〜が高いです","grammar:88:ex:explain":"This is the comparison pattern 「AはBより〜」. 「より」 is the particle marking the standard of comparison and means \"than\": 「彼は私より」 = \"than me\". The second half, 「背が高い」, is the fixed way to describe height: 「背」 means height and takes 「が」 as its subject marker, while 「高い」 is an i-adjective. The whole sentence 「彼は私より背が高いです」 = \"He is taller than me\". Remember that the thing you compare against is marked with 「より」, while the quality being compared is introduced with 「が」.","grammar:88:ex:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:88:ex:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:88:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:88:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:88:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:88:ex:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:88:ex:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:88:ex:words:3:zh":"than","grammar:88:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex:words:4:zh":"height","grammar:88:ex:words:4:note":"せ","grammar:88:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex:words:5:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:88:ex:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex:words:6:zh":"tall","grammar:88:ex:words:6:note":"たかい","grammar:88:ex:words:6:pos":"adjective","grammar:88:ex:words:7:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:88:ex:words:7:pos":"copula","grammar:88:ex:points:0":"❗より: standard of comparison, \"than\" (AはBより = A is more … than B).","grammar:88:ex:points:1":"背が高い: tall (背 = height; the subject takes が).","grammar:88:ex2:trans":"This book is more interesting than that one.","grammar:88:ex2:structure":"AはBより〜","grammar:88:ex2:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:88:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:88:ex2:words:1:zh":"book","grammar:88:ex2:words:1:note":"ほん","grammar:88:ex2:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex2:words:2:zh":"(topic)","grammar:88:ex2:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex2:words:3:zh":"that","grammar:88:ex2:words:3:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:88:ex2:words:4:zh":"book","grammar:88:ex2:words:4:note":"ほん","grammar:88:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex2:words:5:zh":"than","grammar:88:ex2:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex2:words:6:zh":"interesting","grammar:88:ex2:words:6:note":"おもしろい","grammar:88:ex2:words:6:pos":"adjective","grammar:88:ex2:points:0":"AはBより〜: A is more … than B.","grammar:88:ex2:points:1":"面白い: interesting (plain-form ending).","grammar:88:ex3:trans":"I'm older than him.","grammar:88:ex3:structure":"〜は〜より年上です","grammar:88:ex3:words:0:zh":"I","grammar:88:ex3:words:0:note":"わたし","grammar:88:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:88:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:88:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex3:words:2:zh":"he","grammar:88:ex3:words:2:note":"かれ","grammar:88:ex3:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:88:ex3:words:3:zh":"than","grammar:88:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex3:words:4:zh":"older","grammar:88:ex3:words:4:note":"としうえ","grammar:88:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex3:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:88:ex3:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:88:ex3:points:0":"年上（としうえ）: older in age.","grammar:88:ex3:points:1":"より: standard of comparison.","grammar:88:ex4:trans":"Cats are cuter than dogs.","grammar:88:ex4:structure":"AはBより〜です","grammar:88:ex4:words:0:zh":"cat","grammar:88:ex4:words:0:note":"ねこ","grammar:88:ex4:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:88:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex4:words:2:zh":"dog","grammar:88:ex4:words:2:note":"いぬ","grammar:88:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex4:words:3:zh":"than","grammar:88:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex4:words:4:zh":"cute","grammar:88:ex4:words:4:note":"かわいい","grammar:88:ex4:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:88:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:88:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:88:ex4:points:0":"より: than …","grammar:88:ex4:points:1":"可愛い: cute (i-adjective).","grammar:88:ex5:trans":"I think Japanese is harder than English.","grammar:88:ex5:structure":"〜より〜と思います","grammar:88:ex5:words:0:zh":"Japanese","grammar:88:ex5:words:0:note":"にほんご","grammar:88:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex5:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:88:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex5:words:2:zh":"English","grammar:88:ex5:words:2:note":"えいご","grammar:88:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:88:ex5:words:3:zh":"than","grammar:88:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex5:words:4:zh":"difficult","grammar:88:ex5:words:4:note":"むずかしい","grammar:88:ex5:words:4:pos":"adjective","grammar:88:ex5:words:5:zh":"(quotation)","grammar:88:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:88:ex5:words:6:zh":"think","grammar:88:ex5:words:6:note":"おもいます","grammar:88:ex5:words:6:pos":"verb","grammar:88:ex5:points:0":"AはBより難しい: A is harder than B.","grammar:88:ex5:points:1":"〜と思います: I think … (quotation)."},"89":{"example:89:exzh":"She seems to be beautiful.","example:89:exzh2":"That kind of appearance is wonderful.","example:89:exzh3":"What kind of appearance is it?","example:89:exzh4":"He looks full of confidence.","example:89:exzh5":"I like shapes that look like a dog.","grammar:89:ex:trans":"She seems to be beautiful.","grammar:89:ex:structure":"〜は〜様です","grammar:89:ex:explain":"This sentence uses the noun 「様」 to describe an appearance. 「様（よう）」 is a noun meaning \"look, appearance\". The i-adjective 「美しい」 modifies it directly, giving 「美しい様」 = \"a beautiful appearance\". 「彼女は」 makes \"she\" the topic, and 「です」 at the end makes the sentence polite. The sentence says that her appearance is beautiful. Note that when 「様」 is read 「よう」 it usually refers to an appearance, while when it is read 「さま」 it is an honorific (as in お客様); the reading makes a big difference in meaning.","grammar:89:ex:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:89:ex:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:89:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:89:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:89:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex:words:2:zh":"beautiful","grammar:89:ex:words:2:note":"うつくしい","grammar:89:ex:words:2:pos":"adjective","grammar:89:ex:words:3:zh":"appearance","grammar:89:ex:words:3:note":"よう","grammar:89:ex:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex:words:4:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:89:ex:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:89:ex:points:0":"様（よう）: appearance, look.","grammar:89:ex:points:1":"美しい様: a beautiful appearance.","grammar:89:ex2:trans":"That kind of figure is wonderful.","grammar:89:ex2:structure":"そのような＋noun＋は〜です","grammar:89:ex2:explain":"「そのような」 works as a set expression pointing to a look or way that was mentioned earlier or is already known to both speakers, meaning \"that kind of\". 「そのような姿」 as a whole is the topic, and 「素晴らしい」 evaluates it. 「素晴らしい」 is an i-adjective, so adding 「です」 makes the sentence polite.","grammar:89:ex2:words:0:zh":"that, that kind of","grammar:89:ex2:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:89:ex2:words:1:zh":"look, way","grammar:89:ex2:words:1:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex2:words:2:zh":"(the form of 「ようだ」 used before a noun)","grammar:89:ex2:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex2:words:3:zh":"figure, appearance","grammar:89:ex2:words:3:note":"すがた","grammar:89:ex2:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex2:words:4:zh":"(topic)","grammar:89:ex2:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex2:words:5:zh":"wonderful, excellent","grammar:89:ex2:words:5:note":"すばらしい","grammar:89:ex2:words:5:pos":"i-adjective","grammar:89:ex2:words:6:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:89:ex2:words:6:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex2:points:0":"「そのような＋noun」 means \"that kind of …\" as mentioned earlier.","grammar:89:ex2:points:1":"When 「ようだ」 modifies a noun it becomes 「ような」, so here it attaches to 「姿」.","grammar:89:ex3:trans":"What kind of figure is it?","grammar:89:ex3:structure":"どのような＋noun＋ですか","grammar:89:ex3:explain":"「どのような」 as a whole asks about an appearance, nature, or way, and here it modifies 「姿」. 「ですか」 forms a polite question asking what kind of figure it actually is. In casual speech you can also say 「どんな姿ですか」.","grammar:89:ex3:words:0:zh":"which, what kind of","grammar:89:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:89:ex3:words:1:zh":"look, way","grammar:89:ex3:words:1:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex3:words:2:zh":"(the form of 「ようだ」 used before a noun)","grammar:89:ex3:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex3:words:3:zh":"figure, appearance","grammar:89:ex3:words:3:note":"すがた","grammar:89:ex3:words:3:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex3:words:4:zh":"(polite statement)","grammar:89:ex3:words:4:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex3:words:5:zh":"(question)","grammar:89:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex3:points:0":"「どのような＋noun」 asks about the characteristics of something, equivalent to \"what kind of …\".","grammar:89:ex3:points:1":"「どのような」 is a little more formal than 「どんな」.","grammar:89:ex4:trans":"He looks very confident.","grammar:89:ex4:structure":"〜の様です","grammar:89:ex4:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:89:ex4:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:89:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:89:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:89:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex4:words:2:zh":"full of confidence","grammar:89:ex4:words:2:note":"じしんまんまん","grammar:89:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex4:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:89:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex4:words:4:zh":"appearance","grammar:89:ex4:words:4:note":"よう","grammar:89:ex4:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex4:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:89:ex4:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:89:ex4:points:0":"〜の様（よう）です: looks like … / seems …","grammar:89:ex4:points:1":"自信満々: full of confidence (a four-character compound).","grammar:89:ex5:trans":"I like figures that look like dogs.","grammar:89:ex5:structure":"noun＋のような＋noun＋が好きです","grammar:89:ex5:explain":"「犬のような」 means \"dog-like\" and modifies 「姿」; a 「の」 is needed between the noun 「犬」 and 「よう」. 「姿が好きです」 says that the speaker likes this kind of figure. Here 「よう」 expresses comparison or resemblance, not the \"seems\" of conjecture.","grammar:89:ex5:words:0:zh":"dog","grammar:89:ex5:words:0:note":"いぬ","grammar:89:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex5:words:1:zh":"(links the thing being compared with 「よう」)","grammar:89:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex5:words:2:zh":"like …","grammar:89:ex5:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex5:words:3:zh":"(the form of 「ようだ」 used before a noun)","grammar:89:ex5:words:3:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex5:words:4:zh":"figure, appearance","grammar:89:ex5:words:4:note":"すがた","grammar:89:ex5:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:89:ex5:words:5:zh":"(the object of liking)","grammar:89:ex5:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:89:ex5:words:6:zh":"to like","grammar:89:ex5:words:6:note":"すき","grammar:89:ex5:words:6:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:89:ex5:words:7:zh":"(polite statement)","grammar:89:ex5:words:7:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:89:ex5:points:0":"「noun＋のような＋noun」 expresses something or an appearance that is like the first noun.","grammar:89:ex5:points:1":"「犬のような姿」 is the whole object of liking, so it is followed by 「が」."},"90":{"example:90:exzh":"This is my book.","example:90:exzh2":"What kind of book is this?","example:90:exzh3":"What is this?","example:90:exzh4":"This is very convenient.","example:90:exzh5":"This is what I need.","grammar:90:ex:trans":"This is my book.","grammar:90:ex:structure":"これは〜の〜です","grammar:90:ex:explain":"This is a possessive identifying sentence. 「これ」 belongs to the こ-series of the こそあど words and refers to something close to the speaker. 「私の本」 is joined with 「の」 to show possession: \"my book\". 「は」 makes 「これ」 the topic, and the predicate 「私の本です」 uses 「です」 for a polite assertion. The whole sentence 「これは私の本です」 = \"This is my book\". 「の」 is the most basic possessive and linking particle in Japanese, clearly connecting the \"whose\" or \"what\" relationship.","grammar:90:ex:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:90:ex:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:90:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex:words:2:zh":"I","grammar:90:ex:words:2:note":"わたし","grammar:90:ex:words:2:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:90:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex:words:4:zh":"book","grammar:90:ex:words:4:note":"ほん","grammar:90:ex:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:90:ex:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:90:ex:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:90:ex:points:0":"これ: this (the こ of the こそあど series).","grammar:90:ex:points:1":"私の本: my book.","grammar:90:ex2:trans":"What kind of book is this?","grammar:90:ex2:structure":"これは＋何の＋noun＋ですか","grammar:90:ex2:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:90:ex2:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex2:words:1:zh":"marks the topic","grammar:90:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex2:words:2:zh":"what","grammar:90:ex2:words:2:note":"なん; interrogative word","grammar:90:ex2:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:90:ex2:words:3:zh":"'s","grammar:90:ex2:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex2:words:4:zh":"book","grammar:90:ex2:words:4:note":"ほん; book","grammar:90:ex2:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:90:ex2:words:5:zh":"is","grammar:90:ex2:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:90:ex2:words:6:zh":"question","grammar:90:ex2:words:6:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex2:points:0":"「これ」 refers to something near the speaker or just mentioned; here it means the book in front of you.","grammar:90:ex2:points:1":"「何の本」 links the interrogative word and the noun with 「の」，asking about the kind or content.","grammar:90:ex2:points:2":"The final 「ですか」 makes it a polite question.","grammar:90:ex3:trans":"What is this?","grammar:90:ex3:structure":"これは何ですか","grammar:90:ex3:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:90:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:90:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex3:words:2:zh":"what","grammar:90:ex3:words:2:note":"なに","grammar:90:ex3:words:2:pos":"question word","grammar:90:ex3:words:3:zh":"is","grammar:90:ex3:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:90:ex3:words:4:zh":"(question)","grammar:90:ex3:words:4:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex3:points:0":"これは何ですか: \"What is this?\" (the basic way to ask).","grammar:90:ex3:points:1":"何ですか: asks what something is.","grammar:90:ex4:trans":"This is very convenient.","grammar:90:ex4:structure":"これは＋adverb＋na-adjective＋です","grammar:90:ex4:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:90:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex4:words:1:zh":"marks the topic","grammar:90:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex4:words:2:zh":"extremely","grammar:90:ex4:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:90:ex4:words:3:zh":"convenient","grammar:90:ex4:words:3:note":"べんり; na-adjective stem","grammar:90:ex4:words:3:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:90:ex4:words:4:zh":"is","grammar:90:ex4:words:4:pos":"copula","grammar:90:ex4:points:0":"「これ」 refers to the item in front of you and is used directly as the topic of the sentence.","grammar:90:ex4:points:1":"「とても」 comes before the adjective and strengthens the degree of 「便利」.","grammar:90:ex4:points:2":"When a na-adjective is the predicate, adding 「です」 makes the sentence polite.","grammar:90:ex5:trans":"I need this.","grammar:90:ex5:structure":"これが必要です","grammar:90:ex5:words:0:zh":"this","grammar:90:ex5:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:90:ex5:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:90:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:90:ex5:words:2:zh":"necessary","grammar:90:ex5:words:2:note":"ひつよう","grammar:90:ex5:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:90:ex5:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:90:ex5:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:90:ex5:points:0":"❓Why が? It emphasizes that this is exactly the thing that is needed (が marks specification).","grammar:90:ex5:points:1":"必要です: na-adjective in polite form.","exam:90:zh":"While showing the item I was holding in my hand, I said, \"This is a new camera.\"","exam:90:why":"To point at something in your own hand, use 「これ」. 「それ」 refers to something near the listener, which doesn't match the position here."},"91":{"example:91:exzh":"Let's meet again.","example:91:exzh2":"Please come again.","example:91:exzh3":"He was late again.","example:91:exzh4":"Let's talk again tomorrow.","example:91:exzh5":"I'll go again after work is over.","grammar:91:ex:trans":"See you again.","grammar:91:ex:structure":"また〜ましょう","grammar:91:ex:explain":"This sentence uses 「また〜ましょう」 for a parting \"let's meet again\". 「また」 means \"again\", suggesting that the same thing will happen once more. The verb 「会う」 becomes the volitional form 「会いましょう」 (う→い plus ましょう), meaning \"let's …\". The whole sentence 「また会いましょう」 = \"let's meet again sometime\", a very natural greeting when parting that carries more warmth and expectation of meeting again than simply saying 「さようなら」.","grammar:91:ex:words:0:zh":"again","grammar:91:ex:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:91:ex:words:1:zh":"let's meet","grammar:91:ex:words:1:note":"あいましょう","grammar:91:ex:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex:points:0":"また: again.","grammar:91:ex:points:1":"また会いましょう: see you again (a parting phrase).","grammar:91:ex2:trans":"Please come again.","grammar:91:ex2:structure":"また〜てください","grammar:91:ex2:words:0:zh":"again","grammar:91:ex2:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:91:ex2:words:1:zh":"come","grammar:91:ex2:words:1:note":"きて","grammar:91:ex2:words:1:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex2:words:2:zh":"please","grammar:91:ex2:words:2:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:91:ex2:points:0":"また来てください: please come again (a welcome phrase).","grammar:91:ex2:points:1":"来る→来て＋ください.","grammar:91:ex3:trans":"He was late again.","grammar:91:ex3:structure":"また〜た","grammar:91:ex3:words:0:zh":"he","grammar:91:ex3:words:0:note":"かれ","grammar:91:ex3:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:91:ex3:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:91:ex3:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:91:ex3:words:2:zh":"again","grammar:91:ex3:words:2:pos":"adverb","grammar:91:ex3:words:3:zh":"was late","grammar:91:ex3:words:3:note":"おくれた","grammar:91:ex3:words:3:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex3:points:0":"また: again (something repeating, with a negative nuance).","grammar:91:ex3:points:1":"遅れる→遅れた (past plain form).","grammar:91:ex4:trans":"Let's talk again tomorrow.","grammar:91:ex4:structure":"また明日〜ましょう","grammar:91:ex4:words:0:zh":"again","grammar:91:ex4:words:0:pos":"adverb","grammar:91:ex4:words:1:zh":"tomorrow","grammar:91:ex4:words:1:note":"あした","grammar:91:ex4:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:91:ex4:words:2:zh":"let's talk","grammar:91:ex4:words:2:note":"はなしましょう","grammar:91:ex4:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex4:points:0":"また明日: again tomorrow (a parting phrase).","grammar:91:ex4:points:1":"話す→話しましょう.","grammar:91:ex5:trans":"I'll go again after work is over.","grammar:91:ex5:structure":"〜たらまた〜ます","grammar:91:ex5:words:0:zh":"work","grammar:91:ex5:words:0:note":"しごと","grammar:91:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:91:ex5:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:91:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:91:ex5:words:2:zh":"when it's over","grammar:91:ex5:words:2:note":"おわったら","grammar:91:ex5:words:2:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex5:words:3:zh":"again","grammar:91:ex5:words:3:pos":"adverb","grammar:91:ex5:words:4:zh":"go","grammar:91:ex5:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:91:ex5:points:0":"〜たら: after (finishing) … (conditional).","grammar:91:ex5:points:1":"終わる→終わったら (intransitive verb; the subject takes が).","exam:91:zh":"The food at this restaurant was delicious, so I want to come and eat here again next week.","exam:91:why":"「また」 means again, and here you have already eaten once. 「初めて」 means for the first time, which contradicts the fact that you have already eaten here."},"98":{"example:98:exzh":"There's no money in the wallet.","example:98:exzh2":"I need money.","example:98:exzh3":"With that job, you can get a lot of money.","example:98:exzh4":"She's saving money.","example:98:exzh5":"Managing money is important.","grammar:98:ex:trans":"There's no money in the wallet.","grammar:98:ex:structure":"Place＋に＋noun＋が＋ありません","grammar:98:ex:explain":"「お金」 is the everyday word for money; the 「お」 in front makes it sound a little more polite, and in everyday speech people almost always say 「お金」 rather than just 「金」. 「お金がある／ない」 is the most common pairing, meaning to have money / to have no money. This sentence uses the pattern 「場所に＋物がありません」 to say that there is no money in the wallet; things are described with 「ある」, while 「いる」 is used for people and animals.","grammar:98:ex:words:0:zh":"wallet","grammar:98:ex:words:0:note":"さいふ","grammar:98:ex:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex:words:1:zh":"exist","grammar:98:ex:words:1:note":"marks the place where something exists","grammar:98:ex:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex:words:2:zh":"money","grammar:98:ex:words:2:note":"おかね; お + 金, a polite way of saying it","grammar:98:ex:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex:words:3:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:98:ex:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex:words:4:zh":"don't have","grammar:98:ex:words:4:note":"the masu-form negative of ある","grammar:98:ex:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:98:ex:points:0":"「お金がありません」 = there's no money: お金 takes が as its subject and pairs with ある／ありません to show whether something is there or not.","grammar:98:ex:points:1":"場所に＋物が＋あります: に marks where something exists (財布に).","grammar:98:ex:points:2":"ありません is the negative of あります.","grammar:98:ex2:trans":"I need money.","grammar:98:ex2:structure":"〜が必要です","grammar:98:ex2:words:0:zh":"money","grammar:98:ex2:words:0:note":"おかね","grammar:98:ex2:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex2:words:1:zh":"(nominative)","grammar:98:ex2:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex2:words:2:zh":"necessary","grammar:98:ex2:words:2:note":"ひつよう","grammar:98:ex2:words:2:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:98:ex2:words:3:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:98:ex2:words:3:pos":"copula","grammar:98:ex2:points:0":"❗お金: money (the beautifying prefix お + 金).","grammar:98:ex2:points:1":"お金が必要: to need money.","grammar:98:ex3:trans":"Doing that job, you can get a lot of money.","grammar:98:ex3:structure":"その仕事では、たくさんのお金をもらえます","grammar:98:ex3:explain":"「その仕事では」 first sets up that job as the situation, and 「は」 can also carry a contrastive tone against other jobs. 「たくさんのお金」 means a lot of money, and the 「お」 in 「お金」 is a common beautifying prefix. 「もらう」 means to receive or get; its potential form is 「もらえる」, and the polite form is 「もらえます」. With the potential form the object can take 「が」, but the 「を」 used in this sentence is also fine.","grammar:98:ex3:words:0:zh":"that","grammar:98:ex3:words:0:pos":"pre-noun adjectival","grammar:98:ex3:words:1:zh":"work","grammar:98:ex3:words:1:note":"しごと","grammar:98:ex3:words:1:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex3:words:2:zh":"(the setting or situation of the activity)","grammar:98:ex3:words:2:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex3:words:3:zh":"(topic, contrast)","grammar:98:ex3:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex3:words:4:zh":"a lot","grammar:98:ex3:words:4:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex3:words:5:zh":"(modifies the noun that follows)","grammar:98:ex3:words:5:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex3:words:6:zh":"(polite, beautifying prefix)","grammar:98:ex3:words:6:pos":"prefix","grammar:98:ex3:words:7:zh":"money","grammar:98:ex3:words:7:note":"かね","grammar:98:ex3:words:7:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex3:words:8:zh":"(the thing received)","grammar:98:ex3:words:8:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex3:words:9:zh":"can get","grammar:98:ex3:words:9:pos":"verb","grammar:98:ex3:words:10:zh":"(polite tone)","grammar:98:ex3:words:10:pos":"auxiliary verb","grammar:98:ex3:points:0":"「では」 is made up of 「で＋は」 and presents the situation within that job.","grammar:98:ex3:points:1":"「もらえます」 is the potential form of 「もらう」, meaning 'can get'.","grammar:98:ex3:points:2":"「たくさんの＋名詞」 expresses a large quantity; here 「たくさん」 is used as a noun.","grammar:98:ex4:trans":"She's saving money.","grammar:98:ex4:structure":"〜を貯めています","grammar:98:ex4:words:0:zh":"she","grammar:98:ex4:words:0:note":"かのじょ","grammar:98:ex4:words:0:pos":"pronoun","grammar:98:ex4:words:1:zh":"(topic)","grammar:98:ex4:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex4:words:2:zh":"money","grammar:98:ex4:words:2:note":"おかね","grammar:98:ex4:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex4:words:3:zh":"(object marker)","grammar:98:ex4:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex4:words:4:zh":"saving up","grammar:98:ex4:words:4:note":"ためています","grammar:98:ex4:words:4:pos":"verb","grammar:98:ex4:points:0":"❗貯める: to save (money), to put aside.","grammar:98:ex4:points:1":"お金を貯める: to save money.","grammar:98:ex5:trans":"Money management is important.","grammar:98:ex5:structure":"〜は重要です","grammar:98:ex5:words:0:zh":"money","grammar:98:ex5:words:0:note":"おかね","grammar:98:ex5:words:0:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex5:words:1:zh":"'s","grammar:98:ex5:words:1:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex5:words:2:zh":"management","grammar:98:ex5:words:2:note":"かんり","grammar:98:ex5:words:2:pos":"noun","grammar:98:ex5:words:3:zh":"(topic)","grammar:98:ex5:words:3:pos":"particle","grammar:98:ex5:words:4:zh":"important","grammar:98:ex5:words:4:note":"じゅうよう","grammar:98:ex5:words:4:pos":"na-adjective","grammar:98:ex5:words:5:zh":"(polite form)","grammar:98:ex5:words:5:pos":"copula","grammar:98:ex5:points:0":"お金の管理: money management.","grammar:98:ex5:points:1":"重要: important.","exam:98:zh":"This shop doesn't take cards, so I took money out of the wallet and paid.","exam:98:why":"When you can't use a card, taking out 「お金」 to pay fits the situation best. 「切符」 is a train ticket or an admission ticket, and it isn't a way to pay at an ordinary shop."}};